{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong","id":1392809,"title":"V5 did the Lasombra right...and wrong","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-30T08:06:52-07:00","id":1392809,"title":"V5 did the Lasombra right...and wrong","content":"<b>short version</b><br /> <br /> when it was revealed that for V5, Lasombra would get their clan weakness extended to a handicap related to technology use,<br /> I was one of those (maybe few) who welcomed the news<br /> <br /> for me, it improved the Lasombra as player characters, as it gave the lasombra a more obvious struggle that would be easier to engage with and translate into play than the absence of reflection<br /> <br /> unfortunately, it was short lived, as it turned out obtenebration was severely nerfed and crippled in v5,<br /> making the Lasombra relatively too weak in V5, and ruining them as both player characters and npcs<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>long version</b><br /> <br /> if you're familiar with the sabbat in previous editions, you'd be familiar with the fact that the main antagonist of any Sabbat isn't the Camarilla or even the antideluvians but enemies closer to home,<br /> the Lasombra, Tzimisce, Black Hand, Inquisition etc<br /> <br /> and the Lasombra (sabbat or antitribu) were arguably the worst of them...<br /> <br /> <b>...and their design helped in that respect...</b><br /> <br /> they were overpowered in every way,<br /> they had a great/versatile discipline spread<br /> <br /> their clan weakness (no reflection) allowed them to recognize each other,<br /> made them immune to certain technological devices (cameras being the most common),<br /> combined with obtenebration, they were pretty good at maintaining their masquerade,<br /> and the sour feeling they got from the absence of their reflection helped in raising the young lasombra into more ruthless individuals, in a similar fashion to the Nosferatu ugly appearance<br /> <br /> they had a clan body to regulate their conflicts and diableries, keeping a fairly stable and strong clan<br /> <br /> the ritae always acted in their favour,<br /> the vinculum made sure that any hostile sentiment towards the clan (by the antitribu or otherwise) was shut down,<br /> the monomacy was rigged in favor of obtenebration users, which worked well in combination with potence, and they had dominate and exclusive access to abyss mysticism for the few cases where the first two failed<br /> <br /> the obtenebration nerf in v5 ruined it<br /> they're not as intimidating anymore<br /> <br /> <b>...but they sucked as player characters</b><br /> <br /> for the reasons above, the lasombra PCs were privileged in every way, in addition to having the easiest access to some of the best mentors<br /> <br /> their clan weakness wasn't enough to offset the balance, at least not to the same extent that other clan weakness like the Nosferatu weakness did,<br /> <br /> even if the absence of reflection would be a real struggle in real life, it didn't translate well in a PnP game,<br /> plus, there are ways to get around it (having someone draw your portrait)<br /> <br /> that's why, the technology handicap in V5 was good imo,<br /> but without obtenebration...it's just overkill","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 05-30-2020, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T08:54:38-07:00","id":1392816,"title":"","content":"No, I don't agree. The technology bane is so hamfisted its not even funny. +2 difficulty to even drive now, use smartphones, operate computers, etc. They aren't viable as PCs at all by any margin, now they would be annoying to play. Though I do agree that the destruction of Obtenebration for &quot;Oblivion&quot; is really nonsensical since it seems Low Umbra/Necromantic in flavor while Obtenebration had something to do with pure cosmic alien darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 05-31-2020, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T09:15:14-07:00","id":1392819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392816#post1392816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't agree. The technology bane is so hamfisted is not even funny. +2 difficulty to even drive now, use smartphones, operate computers, etc. They aren't viable as PCs at all by any margin, now they would be annoying to play. Though I do agree that the destruction of Obtenebration for &quot;Oblivion&quot; is really nonsensical since it seems Low Umbra/Necromantic in flavor while Obtenebration had something to do with pure cosmic alien darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the Underworld and Umbra have cosmic alien darkness.<br /> <br /> It's like saying, &quot;It's alien and incomprehensible like Cthulhu!&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;Cthulhu exists in the game. He's in the Labyrinth.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T09:15:54-07:00","id":1392820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392816#post1392816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't agree. The technology bane is so hamfisted is not even funny. +2 difficulty to even drive now, use smartphones, operate computers, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>you can have a ghoul use them for you, or dominate someone into using them for you,<br /> <br /> and obtenebration makes up for it (well, used to),<br /> you can't use a car, but you can teleport through shadows or turn into a shadow and move through cracks<br /> <br /> if obtenebration wasn't as weak as it is now, the new weakness wouldn't be as damning","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T09:52:15-07:00","id":1392829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392819#post1392819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both the Underworld and Umbra have cosmic alien darkness.<br /> <br /> It's like saying, &quot;It's alien and incomprehensible like Cthulhu!&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;Cthulhu exists in the game. He's in the Labyrinth.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Low Umbra has nothing to do with Cthulhu. Not everything that is &quot;spooky, mysterious, or incomprehensible&quot; has to do with Cthulhu. Bringing up that point to justify this.. &quot;Oblivion&quot; technique doesn't do anything for me, its literally how some people in the Whitewolf reddit always say any combat in VTM is &quot;literally DnD&quot;. Even then Oblivion doesn't make sense for the Lasombra because apparently its also a Necromantic based power in lieu with the so called &quot;Hecata&quot; also having it. I assume this was only ever done because for some reason they wanted to scrap all the unique Necromantic disciplines, while taking out Obtenebration.. for whatever reason. &quot;Two birds, one stone,&quot; something I remember typing out avidly in another thread speaking about this topic.<br /> <br /> Also to respond back to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a>, the new bane for Lasombra as it is, is WAY, WAY, too much. Its a really strange retcon to the already servicable curse the Lasombra used to have. Because since when did being cursed due to the closeness of shadows all of a sudden now has to deal with technology? This also breaks how the Lasombra are because their practically a clan focused on pulling your own weight and not relying on others as much- now they have to use a bunch of Ghouls just to be viable, wut?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 05-31-2020, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T10:01:45-07:00","id":1392833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392829#post1392829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Low Umbra has nothing to with Cthulhu. Not everything that is &quot;spooky, mysterious, or incomprehensible&quot; has to do with Cthulhu. Bringing up that point to justify this.. &quot;Oblivion&quot; technique doesn't do anything for me, its literally how some people in the Whitewolf reddit always say any combat in VTM is &quot;literally DnD&quot;. Even then Oblivion doesn't make sense for the Lasombra because apparently its also a Necromantic based power in lieu with the so called &quot;Hecata&quot; also having it. I assume this was only ever done because for some reason they wanted to scrap all the unique Necromantic disciplines, while taking out Obtenebration.. for whatever reason. &quot;Two birds, one stone,&quot; something I remember typing out avidly in another thread speaking about this topic.<br /> <br /> Also to respond back to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a>, the new bane for Lasombra as it is, is WAY, WAY, too much. Its a really strange retcon to the already servicable curse the Lasombra used to have. Because since when did being cursed due to the closeness of shadows all of a sudden now has to deal with technology? This also breaks how the Lasombra are because their practically a clan focused on pulling your own weight and not relying on others as much- now they have to use a bunch of Ghouls just to be viable, wut?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to assume you're joking with me because it's not about Cthulhu, it's about spooky and incomprehensible things period. Which is to say that the spooky and incomprehensible things of the setting are not undefined, they're defined in-universe all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T10:14:29-07:00","id":1392835,"title":"","content":"I actually find the challenge in playing the Lasombra quite rewarding and the \u201cnerf\u201d to Obtenebration is slightly annoying and at times confusing lore-wise, I still find it incredibly fun to give the Clan a new unique set of challenges and rewards the player much more for heavier role playing. I like that they have to think through more than just \u201cShadow Magic bash\u201d everything into the dirt. It allows them to truly strive for that feeling of superiority when a plan works out with what they have. There is a lot about V5 that I have to admit I house rule, mostly because my players are dogmatic about role playing through challenges and the rules are really loose and general, but I think they did great making the Lasombra both fun and challenging to play, not to mention making them fit a bit more with their Camarilla cousins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26172-twilightspire","name":"Twilightspire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:05:54-07:00","id":1392848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392833#post1392833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to assume you're joking with me because it's not about Cthulhu, it's about spooky and incomprehensible things period. Which is to say that the spooky and incomprehensible things of the setting are not undefined, they're defined in-universe all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Huh? You mentioned Cthulhu in the first place to begin with as some sort of example. Either way it still doesn't really remotely justify for why Obtenebration and the various Necromantic paths should've been merged. Obteneration is one thing entirely, it tenuously has anything to do with Necromancy to begin with besides both being &quot;dark&quot;- Obtenebration is mostly Deep Umbric aligned, while Necromancy is solely based on the Low Umbra alone, i.e the Underworld. Where has it been noted that the Lasombra heavily deal with Necromancy? You can't because they never practiced it in a clan wide manner at all, maybe a miniscule amount of Lasombra learned Necromancy (pre-V5 of course) from trading favors with the Giovanni, Nagaraja, Samedi, etc. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">At the meat of it though the merge doesn't make sense at all.<br /> <br /> Also make the Lasombra fun to play? Yeah I don't know about that. The way V5 has it, your now more tailored to being a neonate now more than ever before. Though if you play as a Lasombra who has been embraced recently, now you can't use Tech anymore at ALL. Can't use ATMs, can't use your phone anymore, your computer is useless now, can't drive your car, and a whole bunch of other things. People just say use Ghouls, but how can neonate expect to maintain a whole bunch of Ghouls when they're so weak starting out? The Lasombra are tedious now. Not to mention that realistically the Lasombra would be taken WAY advantage of. They'd probably owe a huge bunch of favors to the Noseferatu just to get even the most miniscule of things done. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 05-31-2020, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:16:25-07:00","id":1392851,"title":"","content":"The Abyss is one of the name of the section of the Labyrinth where the Nephandi Lords, the Neverborn, and creators of all things eldritch and horrifying via their dreams exist. Those beings were also revealed to be the Archemons from Demon: The Fallen.<br /> <br /> Obternation tapping into the Underworld abyss would actually tie together:<br /> <br /> * The Abyss<br /> * The Underworld<br /> * Cthulhuoid Horrors<br /> * The Lasombra's weird Catholicism<br /> <br /> Sorry for the confusion but I was just using Cthulhu as an example of, &quot;People say the Lasombra were tied to something alien and incomprehensible but if they were tied to something existing, they'd have an alien and incomprehensible example there.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-30-2020, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:20:48-07:00","id":1392853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392829#post1392829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also to respond back to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a>, the new bane for Lasombra as it is, is WAY, WAY, too much. Its a really strange retcon to the already servicable curse the Lasombra used to have. Because since when did being cursed due to the closeness of shadows all of a sudden now has to deal with technology? This also breaks how the Lasombra are because their practically a clan focused on pulling your own weight and not relying on others as much- now they have to use a bunch of Ghouls just to be viable, wut?</div> </div> </div> </div>well, even if you can use technology,<br /> you still need people to build your castle,<br /> you need them to build your car, your TV, your cellphone and write the code for you computer,<br /> you need them to dig the oil for fuel, make batteries and plug some electricity into your haven<br /> <br /> relying on technology doesn't make you independent, quite the opposite, it makes you very dependent on others<br /> <br /> what makes vampires independent is their vampiric powers,<br /> and all you need for vampiric powers to work is blood<br /> <br /> and, if you're already using humans for blood, might as well use them to run your PC,<br /> which vampires probably don't use cause they have better senses, the fans are too loud and the frame rate (which is probably slow by their standards) is jarring to their eyes<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:22:45-07:00","id":1392854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392848#post1392848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where has it been noted that the Lasombra heavily deal with Necromancy?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</i> page 474.<br /> <br /> I'm not a huge fan of the necromancy/obtenebration merger, but there is lore backing for it, even if I don't particularly like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:26:00-07:00","id":1392856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392854#post1392854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</i> page 474.<br /> <br /> I'm not a huge fan of the necromancy/obtenebration merger, but there is lore backing for it, even if I don't particularly like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>the whole obtenebration-underworld thing dates back to 2nd ed, I believe<br /> <br /> it was forgotten in revised, and brought back later,<br /> Revised was more &quot;obtenebration is Dark Matter, black-holes are cool, Lasombra do Astrophysics&quot; or something like that<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:27:50-07:00","id":1392857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392848#post1392848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though if you play as a Lasombra who has been embraced recently, now you can't use Tech anymore at ALL. Can't use ATMs, can't use your phone anymore, your computer is useless now, can't drive your car, and a whole bunch of other things. People just say use Ghouls, but how can neonate expect to maintain a whole bunch of Ghouls when their so weak starting out? The Lasombra are tedious now. Not to mention that realistically the Lasombra would be taken WAY advantage of. They'd probably owe a huge bunch of favors to the Noseferatu just to get even the most miniscule of things done.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the book they can't drive cars, use ATMs, etc, but according to one of the devs that's an error. The intent was that anything capturing their image or likeness, or transmitting a representation of them, glitches out (as an extension of the previous &quot;no shadow&quot; thing). The extent of the issues depends on their age; older and more powerful Lasombra have more issues than neonates do.<br /> <br /> So (according to dev intent) touchscreens, voice and video calls, and on-screen keyboards pose an issue, but cars, physical keyboards, and even touchscreens with an appropriately-modified stylus are fine. The core of the bane is the same as it's always been\u2014people who know what they're looking for can identify Lasombra easily. (Which means other Lasombra, but also means the Society of Leopold etc.)<br /> <br /> (And this is absolutely a flaw in the books, and one that I hope gets corrected. Because I agree that Lasombra not being able to drive cars is annoying.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:41:30-07:00","id":1392861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392819#post1392819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both the Underworld and Umbra have cosmic alien darkness.<br /> <br /> It's like saying, &quot;It's alien and incomprehensible like Cthulhu!&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;Cthulhu exists in the game. He's in the Labyrinth.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, yes ok you can have monsters in the Labyrinth...but they are to human, they are to bound to earth and human souls, to really hit the Outer God, Elder God etc terror of the Mythos, that sure knowledge that their are brings beyond comprehension who could obliterate the world (or universe, depending on which deity...but they don't care) the Incarna in the Labyrinth explicitly do care, they need human souls, so they don't fulfill the same Cosmic Horror role, they aren't incomphrensible, they aren't alien, they are fallen angels, that's it . Terrifying in the way a nuclear weapon is, directed power and malice, not the way a Gamma Ray Burst is, no malice, no interest, no intent, just obliteration of everything for no real reason you could ever begin to grasp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-30-2020, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:44:05-07:00","id":1392862,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra Bane was a <i>good bane</i>. Try getting into the back of a taxi. Try walk around in the glass metropolises we've built, or approach wet roads as they reflect the light. Your enemies can practice area denial by installing mirrors in the public places you want to visit. Sure, it had advantages, but most clan banes have a minor positive aspect to it (Bloodlines with no positive: Settites, Baali... Blood brothers don't have anything nice for themselves but the no-sire rule is good for creators) . The lasombra bane did not need to change. <br /> <br /> Now, for Obtenebration. <br /> I'll agree that it was too strong in prior editions. <br /> I'll agree that Oblivion's a bad joke. <br /> <br /> But I'm telling ya. <br /> Lasombra PCs were great. Lasombra Antitribu PCs are also great. They're fun and work with the party. <br /> <br /> I don't think the old lasombra are thematically compatible with V5. They're too goal oriented for personal horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:44:34-07:00","id":1392863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392851#post1392851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyss is one of the name of the section of the Labyrinth where the Nephandi Lords, the Neverborn, and creators of all things eldritch and horrifying via their dreams exist. Those beings were also revealed to be the Archemons from Demon: The Fallen.<br /> <br /> Obternation tapping into the Underworld abyss would actually tie together:<br /> <br /> * The Abyss<br /> * The Underworld<br /> * Cthulhuoid Horrors<br /> * The Lasombra's weird Catholicism<br /> <br /> Sorry for the confusion but I was just using Cthulhu as an example of, &quot;People say the Lasombra were tied to something alien and incomprehensible but if they were tied to something existing, they'd have an alien and incomprehensible example there.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Neverborn have nothing to do with Demons, their literally the first entities that spawned when Life separated from Death, spontaneously coming to existence near the well of Oblivion itself. Hence their name, &quot;Neverborn&quot;. The Neverborn are only slumbering in PARTS of the Labyrinth as you said OR at the near well of Oblivion itself. No where is a Neverborn outside the Underworld or has anything to do with the Abyss. <br /> <br /> Not only that Nephandi you twist the Labyrinth of the Low Umbra with the personal &quot;Labyrinths&quot; every Nephandi goes through to become a Nephandi in the first place. Those Labyrinths are explicitly in the Deep Umbra, completely different things. <br /> <br /> The Abyss? That alone can mean many things at once because as far as I remember is that their is an &quot;Abyss&quot; in WTA, the &quot;Abyss&quot; where DTF somehow explains the fallen were underneath OBLIVION itself (yeah, that totally makes sense), and the Abyss as I mentioned tacked before that the Lasombra tap into come from none of the previously said things. They're all completely different. That's what makes Obtenebration unique because it comes from an Abyss that we can only speculate about, but truly we have no clue of. Tying it with the Low Umbra out of nowhere for no reason makes no sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:49:48-07:00","id":1392865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392863#post1392863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Neverborn have nothing to do with Demons, their literally the first entities that spawned when Life separated from Death, spontaneously coming to existence near the well of Oblivion itself. Hence their name, &quot;Neverborn&quot;. The Neverborn are only slumbering in PARTS of the Labyrinth as you said OR at the near well of Oblivion itself. No where is a Neverborn outside the Underworld or has anything to do with the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Not only that Nephandi you twist the Labyrinth of the Low Umbra with the personal &quot;Labyrinths&quot; every Nephandi goes through to become a Nephandi in the first place. Those Labyrinths are explicitly in the Deep Umbra, completely different things.<br /> <br /> The Abyss? That alone can mean many things at once because as far as I remember is that their is an &quot;Abyss&quot; in WTA, the &quot;Abyss&quot; where DTF somehow explains the fallen were underneath OBLIVION itself (yeah, that totally makes sense), and the Abyss as I mentioned tacked before that the Lasombra tap into come from none of the previously said things. They're all completely different. That's what makes Obtenebration unique because it comes from an Abyss that we can only speculate about, but truly we have no clue of. Tying it with the Low Umbra out of nowhere for no reason makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this was retconned in Demon: The Fallen.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I've always favored having a more coherent tied together mythology between the splats so you can understand why I support this move.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, Belial the Fallen is described as a giant squid faced dragon in his idol.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:56:39-07:00","id":1392869,"title":"","content":"If that's true that even brings more reason for me to hate DTF. It doesn't even make the mythology more coherent, it just literally broke a bunch of lines at once for whatever reason when they even thought that up. The entirety of DTF lore was a hamfist to legitimize Abrahamic style demons into oWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-04-2020, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T12:00:52-07:00","id":1392872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong#post1392809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>short version</b><br /> <br /> <b>...but they sucked as player characters</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the issue, the Lasombra were overpowered and made for great antagonists but once players began to want to play as them that caused balance issues, especially as the limits of obtenebration were not clearly defined. You had neonates with 3 dots of obtenebration using their shadow tentacles to flip buses over their enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","user":"BR_Malk","date":". 05-30-2020, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T12:16:33-07:00","id":1392877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BR_Malk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392872#post1392872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats the issue, the Lasombra were overpowered and made for great antagonists but once players began to want to play as them that caused balance issues, especially as the limits of obtenebration were not clearly defined. You had neonates with 3 dots of obtenebration using their shadow tentacles to flip buses over their enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, and I would want either obtenebration to be nerfed (which would make them suck as antagonists) or their clan weakness to be tougher<br /> <br /> unfortunately, V5 did both","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 05-30-2020, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T12:22:08-07:00","id":1392878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392865#post1392865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, this was retconned in Demon: The Fallen.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I've always favored having a more coherent tied together mythology between the splats so you can understand why I support this move.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, Belial the Fallen is described as a giant squid faced dragon in his idol.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where as I like mystery, contradictory information and doubt, especially in horror, Shadows of Innsmouth is terrifying, Hellraiser is just gory ( a great film, a great story, but not that visceral, existential horror). Oh also Oblivion as the accretion disk of the prison of the Fallen kinda works, but, again, they aren't the same breed of horror as the things of the deep umbra and far horizon, things older than Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T13:41:41-07:00","id":1392894,"title":"","content":"Eh, all you have to do to make that tenable is figure the demons in the Abyss are suspended from the murky underside of existence by their metaphorical toes, and that other less comprehensible things from below/beyond occasionally swim up and reach past them, attracted by glimmers of light and emotion that filter down. &quot;Wait, did you feel that? I thought we were supposed to be alone down here at the edge of Creation\u2014<i>what's in here with us</i>?!?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T14:24:28-07:00","id":1392899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392856#post1392856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the whole obtenebration-underworld thing dates back to 2nd ed, I believe<br /> <br /> it was forgotten in revised, and brought back later,<br /> Revised was more &quot;obtenebration is Dark Matter, black-holes are cool, Lasombra do Astrophysics&quot; or something like that</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect it\u2019s because the Abyss=Oblivion thing was essentially a Wraith crossover, and when Revised began they\u2019d just killed off the Wraith line and were probably keen to prune back that kind of thing. Then later they decided to subtly bring it back in Orpheus, but note how disconnected from the rest of the WoD that game was.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T14:54:23-07:00","id":1392905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392899#post1392899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I expect it\u2019s because the Abyss=Oblivion thing was essentially a Wraith crossover, and when Revised began they\u2019d just killed off the Wraith line and were probably keen to prune back that kind of thing. Then later they decided to subtly bring it back in Orpheus, but note how disconnected from the rest of the WoD that game was.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, either that or they wanted to distance the lasombra from the Giovanni...or one of the devs was a Neil DeGrass fan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:58:42-07:00","id":1392987,"title":"","content":"In terms of this discussion, I\u2019m defaulting to Mage, as it has the most extensive breakdown of the cosmology (WtA is second, but it mostly deals with the Middle Umbra and only has limited contact with the High or Low or Deep Umbra)... <br /> <br /> - Cthuhlu and it\u2019s associated Elder Gods are absolutely a Deep Umbra entities. Alien geometries and similar madness that the rational mind can\u2019t even fathom can only exist beyond the Far Horizon because reality simply can\u2019t support them (sufficiently high madness Marauders drop out of reality and end up here). It\u2019s an endless black void outside creation wherein things that cannot be dwell (it is also sometimes called the Outer Darkness).<br /> <br /> -There is an Abyss in the Middle Umbra; the result of some cataclysm and is know to the wolves as a place where things dropped into its bottomless pit are lost forever. A group of Wraiths who were blown out of the Low Umbra by the 6th Maelstrom and wound up here; unable to return to the underworld they made a home along one of the paths that winds along the walls of this Abyss. No one knows what lies at the bottom because it appears to be truly bottomless.<br /> <br /> - The DTF Abyss exists in a layer beneath the Underworld/Low Umbra. Given the revelations in Orpheus about the nature of Oblivion, it\u2019s unlikely that this Abyss is actually IN Oblivion, but rather that Oblivion was used by God as an impassable barrier to keep this Abyss separate from the rest of creation. It is also noted that no human soul is capable of entering this Abyss; it was created solely to imprison the demons for eternity.<br /> <br /> - The Neverborn of the Low Umbra have never entered the Abyss, they reside in Labyrinth surrounding Oblivion; similarly, the Labyrinths of the Nephandi are not in the Low Umbra, but are reflections of the true Labyrinth in the Middle Umbra (many of the entities worshipped by the Nephandi were actually just the dream projections of sleeping Neverborn). Neither the Malfeans (neverborn or triatic) nor the Nephandi have any affliation with the Demons of DtF.<br /> <br /> So, other than the aforementioned ghost legion that wound up in the Middle Umbra due to the 6th Maelstrom, none of the Abysses in WoD cosmology are associated with undead spirits; making the merger of the Abyss with what is merely the Low Umbra a bit tenuous at best.<br /> <br /> My hunch is that the decision was made to merge these for V5 (even though its going to make things weird if they ever get around to a Mage5) for the same reason they merged Quietus into Blood Sorcery and split aspects of Serpentis up into Protean and Presence... the V5 developers have expressed a desire to eliminate Clan exclusive disciplines in this edition and by combining Obtenebration and Necromancy using the tenuous excuse that the Demon Abyss and Low Umbra of Wraiths are spiritually adjacent (even if they don\u2019t actually interact any more than humans watching a zoo aquarium interact with the fish) they\u2019ve essentially made the gestalt discipline non-exclusive because two clans have it as a discipline.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the spin some are trying to put on it, it IS a retcon, just like Thin-bloods got retconned to not having real disciplines, just Thin-Blood Alchemy and being able to take merits that allow them to actually walk in daylight without taking damage (whereas previously 14th gen took damage normally and 15-16th took lethal with no option to take none) and being able to transition back to mortal with some effort.<br /> <br /> But those retcons are pretty typical whenever a setting desides to change its mechanics. Some fantasy settings will try to include cataclysmic events that result in the setting now following the new rules (see every major upheaval in the Forgotten Realms setting corresponding to an Edition change). <br /> <br /> Others just pretend it\u2019s always been this way and the easiest way to square it in this case is to employ the \u201cWorlds of Darkness\u201d model outlined in some of the Revised Mage books that basically said \u201ceach game takes place in its own universe where some things are the same and others are different; echoes are felt in nearby worlds and sometimes these worlds even touch and allow crossovers to happen.<br /> <br /> In other words, VtM1-3e took place in one set of universes (that ended with Gehenna), V20 is a collection of universes parallel to that where the metaplot never happened, and V5 is in another set of universes with a few more differences, but still close enough you\u2019d call them part of the overall cluster (with CoD being on the distant edge of the WoD cluster with a few similarities still, but even more differences).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T21:46:09-07:00","id":1392999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392862#post1392862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra Bane was a <i>good bane</i>. Try getting into the back of a taxi. Try walk around in the glass metropolises we've built, or approach wet roads as they reflect the light. Your enemies can practice area denial by installing mirrors in the public places you want to visit. Sure, it had advantages...</div> </div> </div> </div>And with the introduction of the 2nd Inquisition as a major antagonist, it's potential good far outweighed the bad. Cause really what self-respecting Lasombra lowers themselves to ride in a cab?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T23:01:58-07:00","id":1393012,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m glad that they have added some Lasombra to the Camarilla, I\u2019d like to see them become more of a full fledged Camarilla Clan. So that is a change that I do like. I would rather just stick with the old Clan flaw though. As for Oblivion, I feel a bit torn. Some of the powers seem cool but it does seem strange to tie Obtenebration to Necromancy, because they have traditionally been so different, though I can see the thematic connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T23:36:50-07:00","id":1393015,"title":"","content":"Why are they removing unique clan disciplines, for what reason exactly? I've already stated this before in another thread way back, but who know's what their going to do to the Tzimisce since they've adopted this policy. You definitely know they don't like Vicissitude with all the whack-a-moles they've done with other said unique disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T23:43:58-07:00","id":1393016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393012#post1393012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m glad that they have added some Lasombra to the Camarilla, I\u2019d like to see them become more of a full fledged Camarilla Clan. So that is a change that I do like. I would rather just stick with the old Clan flaw though. As for Oblivion, I feel a bit torn. Some of the powers seem cool but it does seem strange to tie Obtenebration to Necromancy, because they have traditionally been so different, though I can see the thematic connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um...there were already Lasombra Anti-tribu in the Cam for a few editions now.....it just wasn't the majority of the Clan....which makes zero sense.... but thats par for the course for most of V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T23:55:17-07:00","id":1393018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zahana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1392999#post1392999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And with the introduction of the 2nd Inquisition as a major antagonist, it's potential good far outweighed the bad. Cause really what self-respecting Lasombra lowers themselves to ride in a cab?</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't. The Lasombra weakness is pretty much the greatest &quot;Hey look, Hunters, I'm a Vampire&quot; weakness. &quot;Oh look, that guy looks a bit cool on our thermal imaging&quot; raises suspicions. &quot;Oh look, That guy didn't show up&quot; removes all doubts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T23:56:41-07:00","id":1393019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393016#post1393016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um...there were already Lasombra Anti-tribu in the Cam for a few editions now.....it just wasn't the majority of the Clan....which makes zero sense.... but thats par for the course for most of V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know, the rare Lasombra Antitribu has been around for a long time, but they were oddities. I want a major Lasombra presence in the Camarilla, which seems to be what V5 is going for and it\u2019s a change that I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T00:36:22-07:00","id":1393027,"title":"","content":"I liked the special snowflake, Me and My sire are the only Lasombra in this city. It was tense, we'd pretend to be other clans, because if the news was spread we'd get a hit squad on us. You've got one more layer of masquerade for your masquerade. Having the Lasombra be &quot;The new guys&quot; would've been tense for half a decade or so, except they'd joined at a time where the Camarilla had lost it's gangrel, lost it's non-fascist brujah, and had those also-shifty assamites joining. They're not the awkward new guys, they're welcome reinforcements (That they're killing eachother off for possitions is just standard lasombra fare) <br /> <br /> Bringing Lasombra En-mass into the camarilla just seems like another way of putting the Camarilla as evil Fascists that the good, sometimes complex but ultimately more wholesome anarchs must destroy. <br /> <br /> Oh and the whole Sabbat thing is BS so, whilst I'd welcome More lasombra into the cam (So I can get more Storytellers to give me the go-ahead!) the method sacrifices just far too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T02:25:59-07:00","id":1393041,"title":"","content":"the lasombra transfer, and most changes to the sects is just the devs taking the cool stuff from the sabbat and putting them on the Cam<br /> (I can't blame them, the sabbat was rad, I'd be jealous too)<br /> <br /> sadly, alot was lost in translation, the new lasombra aren't as great as the former lasombra, and aren't as cool as the former lasombra-antitribu either<br /> <br /> I blame WW's obsession with continuity,<br /> rather than retcon previous canon, they felt obligated to find some half-assed plot development to justify the lasombra switching sides,<br /> it's not just a V5 thing, they did the same with the Gangrel and Tremere antitribu in revised<br /> <br /> if they want the lasombra in the Cam so bad, they should just reboot the Lasombra canon, and say that they've always been there, or make up some new backstory","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T03:24:04-07:00","id":1393046,"title":"","content":"I'd just have the lasombra antitribu grow naturaly: more embraces, more defections, more elders exiting torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T03:34:53-07:00","id":1393048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393046#post1393046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just have the lasombra antitribu grow naturaly: more embraces, more defections, more elders exiting torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, I'd be fine with that<br /> <br /> there's just the issue of the blood courts,<br /> if the camsombra grow large enough, the blood courts can't ignore them or deny them a seat in the courts<br /> <br /> and if the camsombra don't join the courts, they'd be making enemies with every lasombra brood who adheres to the courts...I think<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T03:39:49-07:00","id":1393049,"title":"","content":"They'd make their own blood courts, with blackjack, and... <br /> <br /> Courts, like ventrue boards, are localised anyway. I think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T04:10:24-07:00","id":1393053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393019#post1393019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I know, the rare Lasombra Antitribu has been around for a long time, but they were oddities. I want a major Lasombra presence in the Camarilla, which seems to be what V5 is going for and it\u2019s a change that I like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the elitist clan who like control finally get to be in the elitist sect who like control, which they would have happily joined in the first place if it hadn\u2019t been for a disagreement about acknowledging the existence of the Antediluvians, which is now moot. And that\u2019s after multiple editions has been telling us how the Lasombra had lost control of the Sabbat over the course of several civil wars that the Lasombra always seemed to be on the losing side of, and which had already canonically resulted in a number of defections. <br /> <br /> But I guess in some people\u2019s minds the very Lasombra elders who had manufactured the Sabbat\u2019s religion in the first place are now supposed to martyr themselves to it instead of joining what they perceive to be the winning team (and one they can eventually exert real control over).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T05:35:47-07:00","id":1393063,"title":"","content":"I'm ok with what they did with the Lasombra although I have aproblem with Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Let's see:<br /> The old Lasombra weakness wasn't a weakness at all. Claiming it was a drawback because hunters could easily spot a Lasombra is willfully ignore how the game works. In game hunters come after you because they've found out you are a vamp, and no, they don't need to carry mirrors around to confirm you are one. This is true if you play Lasombra, Ventrue, Gangrel or whatever wlse suits your fancy, unless the storyteller wants to add a bit of comedy to their story hunters have other methods to confirm a vampire identity (like learning certain individuals are only active at night...). In truth the old Lasombra's clan flaw was and advantage: it even gave them the ability to shrug-off eletronic surveliance systems.<br /> Considering the wording in CbN (5th ed) the current clan flaw seems to work as intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chicago by Night 5th Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone seeing the reflection or recording (live and otherwise) of a Lasombra vampire can instantly recognize them for what they are, provided they know what they\u2019re looking for. People with no prior knowledge will know something is wrong, but likely attribute the distortion to irregularities in the reflecting surface or recording errors. Note that this will not hide the identity of the vampire with any certainty, and the Lasombra are no less likely to be caught on surveillance than any other vampire. In addition, use of modern technology, including making a simple phone call, requires a Technology test at Difficulty 2 + Bane Severity as microphones have similar problems with the voice of a Lasombra as cameras with their image. Avoiding electronic vampire detection systems is also done at a penalty equal to Bane Severity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to me the problem arises from the way people define &quot;modern technology&quot;: in my opinion it's pretty clear cars, automatic weapons and the like are not meant to be hindered by this flaw, that's technology that has existed for over a century after all! The Lasombra's bane is clearly meant to make uses of phones and other communication systems relying on advanced tech difficult, it's not meant making them unable to shoot a rifle or drive a car.<br /> <br /> As for Oblivion: powerwise the discipline is now in line with the rest of them. It's weaker than it used to be, but that's because Obtenebration was overpowered in the past (and I suspect a few of those who complain about the current system just wanted to keep it OP). In V5 Oblivion is still strong but you need to study your surroundings and plan your actions a bit more than you did before, and that's a good thing, imo.<br /> That said I've a problem with the way Oblivion works because I don't like the idea that you use a discipline and you automatically risk gaining a stain. I don't think that's a good idea: morality degeneration should come from what players choose to do or not do while the current Oblivion system makes stains happen if the players are unlucky with their dice. I mean, sure, you summon the arms of Arhiman and choke the life out of some poor sap? Degeneration roll is a given (well depends but it usually is). You use Obtenebration to hide into the shadow and escape pursuit? I don't think that deserves losing humanity even if you are summoning the essence of the Abyss. Ultimately this system makes moral choices less relevant for Lasombra vampires as their degeneration is basically a given if they use Oblivion on a sustained period of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 05-31-2020, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T05:44:16-07:00","id":1393064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393053#post1393053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, the elitist clan who like control finally get to be in the elitist sect who like control, which they would have happily joined in the first place if it hadn\u2019t been for a disagreement about acknowledging the existence of the Antediluvians, which is now moot. And that\u2019s after multiple editions has been telling us how the Lasombra had lost control of the Sabbat over the course of several civil wars that the Lasombra always seemed to be on the losing side of, and which had already canonically resulted in a number of defections.<br /> <br /> But I guess in some people\u2019s minds the very Lasombra elders who had manufactured the Sabbat\u2019s religion in the first place are now supposed to martyr themselves to it instead of joining what they perceive to be the winning team (and one they can eventually exert real control over).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been stated that the Lasombra did not want to join the Camarilla because it was a creation of the Ventrue, and the Lasombra always considered themselves the Ventrue's betters. If you go back to the Dark Ages line, you'll find the Lasombra actually had a lot of kindred on the Via Coeli and were no strangers to the road of humanity either. Their shift to the Sabbat was driven by political motivations at least as much as it was from ideological ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T06:44:33-07:00","id":1393073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393063#post1393063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and I suspect a few of those who complain about the current system just wanted to keep it OP)</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, I actually wanted it to stay OP,<br /> because, as I described in my original post, obtenebration being op in addition to their ability to shrug off surveilance tech helped in making them intimidating,<br /> which was an important aspect of the clan, especially as antagonists<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T06:52:34-07:00","id":1393075,"title":"","content":"When the Lasombra Clan loyalists defected to the Camarilla is there any mention of whether there was any mass assassinations of the remaining Sabbat on the wayout?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24792-vashna","name":"Vashna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:04:43-07:00","id":1393081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393063#post1393063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">That said I've a problem with the way Oblivion works because I don't like the idea that you use a discipline and you automatically risk gaining a stain. I don't think that's a good idea: morality degeneration should come from what players choose to do or not do while the current Oblivion system makes stains happen if the players are unlucky with their dice. I mean, sure, you summon the arms of Arhiman and choke the life out of some poor sap? Degeneration roll is a given (well depends but it usually is). You use Obtenebration to hide into the shadow and escape pursuit? I don't think that deserves losing humanity even if you are summoning the essence of the Abyss. Ultimately this system makes moral choices less relevant for Lasombra vampires as their degeneration is basically a given if they use Oblivion on a sustained period of time.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Just a side note:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This is established for pretty much all kindred, as getting a messy critical can result in stains on p. 207 of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">V5 core </span></span><span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">with the example of a vampire using Auspex and gaining a stain because of a messy critical. I think it could reasonably be argued, the same could happen when using Obfuscate to hide. This feels like less of a thing about the Lasombra specifically but more of a way V5 handles chance interference in the characters moral stature.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Gaining a higher blood potency for Lasombra seems to be the intended key objective here, since that would allow re-rolling the rouse check and thus avoiding a possible stain. In practice it doesn't make it Lasombra PCs degenerate that much faster than other characters (unless intended), but since the V5 design includes one gaining stains by chance (messy crit, loss of touchstone, \u2026) this does not strike me to be out of the ordinary. Now if the whole concept of potential humanity loss due to chance is not one's cup of tea, well\u2026 the Lasombra's slight increase in potential to gain stains would not be the hill to die on in that battle in my opinion.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","user":"Pangur B\u00e1n","date":".  so many spelling errors, I gave up halfway... 05-31-2020, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:21:36-07:00","id":1393085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vashna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393075#post1393075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Lasombra Clan loyalists defected to the Camarilla is there any mention of whether there was any mass assassinations of the remaining Sabbat on the wayout?</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, and lasombra defectors are required to sacrifice sabbat lasombra to be accepted in the Camarilla,<br /> <br /> the defectors also destroyed the sabbat Cardinals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:36:37-07:00","id":1393087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393073#post1393073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah, I actually wanted it to stay OP,<br /> because, as I described in my original post, obtenebration being op in addition to their ability to shrug off surveilance tech helped in making them intimidating,<br /> which was an important aspect of the clan, especially as antagonists</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Storyteller I can attest you don't need OP rules to make a character intimidating, you need to build an intimidating charcter, which is a different thing that requires skill and no amount of rules will help you do that. On the other hand as options for player characters giving a clan more power than the others is not a good idea.<br /> As for the old clan flaw the fact it translated to an advantage was simply wrong and I'm glad they rectified that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:42:41-07:00","id":1393089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393087#post1393087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a Storyteller I can attest you don't need OP rules to make a character intimidating,</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but what I said was that the OPness was what made the Lasombra intimidating in prior editions,<br /> other clans were intimidating for other reasons, but for the lasombra, their power played a huge part<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand as options for player characters giving a clan more power than the others is not a good idea.<br /> As for the old clan flaw the fact it translated to an advantage was simply wrong and I'm glad they rectified that. </div> </div> </div>that why I'm saying the new clan bane is a good thing (maybe my post wasn't clear enough),<br /> it balances out the OPness of obtenebration<br /> <br /> but in V5; they not only gave them a crippling bane, they also nerfed Obetenebration","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 05-31-2020, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:44:34-07:00","id":1393090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pangur B\u00e1n</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393081#post1393081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Just a side note:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This is established for pretty much all kindred, as getting a messy critical can result in stains on p. 207 of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">V5 core </span></span><span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">with the example of a vampire using Auspex and gaining a stain because of a messy critical. I think it could reasonably be argued, the same could happen when using Obfuscate to hide. This feels like less of a thing about the Lasombra specifically but more of a way V5 handles chance interference in the characters moral stature.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Gaining a higher blood potency for Lasombra seems to be the intended key objective here, since that would allow re-rolling the rouse check and thus avoiding a possible stain. In practice it doesn't make it Lasombra PCs degenerate that much faster than other characters (unless intended), but since the V5 design includes one gaining stains by chance (messy crit, loss of touchstone, \u2026) this does not strike me to be out of the ordinary. Now if the whole concept of potential humanity loss due to chance is not one's cup of tea, well\u2026 the Lasombra's slight increase in potential to gain stains would not be the hill to die on in that battle in my opinion.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and I don't like the fact a messy critical can result into degeneration either, but at least that's something every vampire risks. In Oblivion's case risking degeneration is an intrinsical aspect of the discipline (so only the Hecata face the same problem with the same frequency). I think the developers wrote it that way because the discipline is now supposed to make you manipulate the essence of the Abyss, which is considered to be Evil (with capital E), but even so, making you risk degeneration every time you want to use one of your powers is not the right way to represent such things imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 05-31-2020, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:54:03-07:00","id":1393093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393064#post1393064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go back to the Dark Ages line, you'll find the Lasombra actually had a lot of kindred on the Via Coeli and were no strangers to the road of humanity either. Their shift to the Sabbat was driven by political motivations at least as much as it was from ideological ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's largely my point. The Lasombra who founded the sect did so as a form of social engineering to create a vampiric society to protect their interests in the Jyhad. They cobbled it together from Catholicism, the Cainite Heresy, late medieval ideas about witchcraft, etc. Even if their concerns about the Antediluvians were genuine, the religion itself is a construct, and the Amici Noctis would know that because many of them were there. That isn't to say that some Lasombra aren't true believers, but it's not the true believers that are defecting, and a lot of them were never true believers to begin with.<br /> <br /> As for their pride and the matter of the Ventrue, the defectors are playing a long game, relying on the Ventrue obsession with the outward trappings of superiority and relatively crude understanding of victory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:55:05-07:00","id":1393094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393089#post1393089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, but what I said is that the OPness is what made the Lasombra intimidating in prior editions, other clans were intimidating for other reasons, but for the lasombra, their power played a huge part</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be part of your personal experience or taste but citing a meta reason for a clan being intimidating does not make much sense to me. The Lasombra were suposed to be boogeymen because they were amoral, elitist monsters commanding the darkness and having no qualms committing the most heinous of acts in order to gain what they wanted. In that respect they are still the same as they were if you wish them to be as Oblivion gives you the tools to represent them that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> that why I'm saying the new clan bane is a good thing (maybe my post wasn't clear enough),it balances out the OPness of obtenebration but in V5; they not only gave them a crippling bane, they also nerfed Obetenebration </div> </div> </div>Obtenebration power was reduced for sure but the discipline is simply in line with other disciplines now, so I don't see the problem. I believe any game system should strive to give players different options of comparable power level/usefulness and in that respect bringing Oblivion down a notch while keeping it useful was the right move imo (the same way that making Fortitude better was a good thing).<br /> <br /> And claiming their new clan flaw (bane now) is &quot;crippling&quot; is a bit of an exageration. I've posted the wording of the rules above. It basically means Lasombras have problems using cell phones and computers and need to be extra careful with eletronical surveliance (instead of magically ignoring it because of the supposed &quot;clan flaw&quot;). Hardly an insurmuntable problem for a clan with dominate...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 05-31-2020, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T08:08:45-07:00","id":1393097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vashna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393075#post1393075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Lasombra Clan loyalists defected to the Camarilla is there any mention of whether there was any mass assassinations of the remaining Sabbat on the wayout?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's stated that roughly half the clan left the Sabbat while the other half remained loyal. The Amici Noctis (which is a Lasombra institution that predates the Anarch revolt...) decided that the Gehenna crusade was a doomed and mad effort, and opened channels of communication with the Camarilla for acceptance. The fact that the Camarilla was trying to ally itself with the Ashirra probably played a role in their eventual acceptance. The Lasombra always were one of the most powerful clans in the Ashirra sect. Only the Assamites could match their influence there. Curiously the Ashirra Assamite left the body of the main clan and joined the Camarilla as well.<br /> <br /> To answer your question: some Cardinals were killed by the schismatics, or at least many of those cardinals who didn't join the Gehenna crusade.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell individual Camarilla courts in any given city can decide if they want to accept the Lasombra in their ranks. If they do they can set the conditions for acceptance. Some courts my ask for the destruction of an elder while others might limit themselves to terms of service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 05-31-2020, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T08:54:02-07:00","id":1393106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393089#post1393089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, but what I said was that the OPness was what made the Lasombra intimidating in prior editions,<br /> other clans were intimidating for other reasons, but for the lasombra, their power played a huge part</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't work for a game, though. One clan can't be obviously more powerful than another if they're presented to players as equally valid options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> that why I'm saying the new clan bane is a good thing (maybe my post wasn't clear enough),<br /> it balances out the OPness of obtenebration<br /> <br /> but in V5; they not only gave them a crippling bane, they also nerfed Obetenebration </div> </div> </div>I disagree on all points. 1) No bane would balance an unbalanced discipline, since that's just not how it works. 2) Unbalanced disciplines are a problem in themselves, since no clan has a monopoly on them, and all disciplines are presented as equally valid choices. 3) The Lasombra bane is far from crippling. It's no worse than those of other clans in terms of bane severity.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra used to be a joke, with a &quot;bane&quot; that was actually beneficial to them most of the time, and a unique discipline that was stupidly powerful. Both have been fixed. Bringing the Lasombra in line with the other clans is not a bad thing, as they don't get to have being OP as their thing in a game in which they're just one of many options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T09:43:42-07:00","id":1393123,"title":"","content":"The bane of &quot;modern technology doesn't work&quot; is pants-on-head when you realise vampires are meant to be ancient, unchanging creatures and clan Lasombra has been around for a very long time. Like, was that weakness waiting around going &quot;Some day I'll be useful&quot; or was their problem with tech relative to the times? Did they have trouble working with belt buckles when they were introduced? <br /> <br /> If you don't think the original clan flaw works, you haven't been playing lasombra long enough. <br /> <br /> The only issue with the old Lasombra (other than the name) is that Obtenebration could've used some soft nerfs. I liked the concepts of the powers; Shadow play, Shroud of night, Arms of the Abyss, Black metamorphisis, Tenebrous form.... But 2 and 3 would work better if they were weaker. Some good ways to do so: The usual vampire banes are doubly effective against combatting obtenebration effects, Shroud needs blood to use, gunshots through shroud leave trails that reveal positions... Auspex+eyes of the beast beat shroud if they're higher rated (and you can combine them) Arms of the Abyss can only secure one limb or the torso, the other limbs can still act (with penalty)... <br /> <br /> Maybe It'd make obtenebration a bit too complex, but it'd work nicely. Oblivion is just... No thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T10:08:29-07:00","id":1393130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393123#post1393123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bane of &quot;modern technology doesn't work&quot; is pants-on-head when you realise vampires are meant to be ancient, unchanging creatures and clan Lasombra has been around for a very long time. Like, was that weakness waiting around going &quot;Some day I'll be useful&quot; or was their problem with tech relative to the times? Did they have trouble working with belt buckles when they were introduced?<br /> <br /> If you don't think the original clan flaw works, you haven't been playing lasombra long enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played and run stories with Lasombra for quite a few years, thank you and in my opinion their clan weakness was not a weakness at all. More often than not it was beneficial and no clan flaw should be beneficial as it's drawback.<br /> <br /> As for the V5 clan weakness it's pretty clear by reading the actual words that it applies to recording devices and technological stuff that deals with one's image, so mainly phones, microphones possibly computers. So in the middle ages the Lasombra only had problems with mirrors but in current times things have become worse for them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T12:05:48-07:00","id":1393168,"title":"","content":"The technology weakness seems odd for Lasombra. Imo, weaknesses and discipline spreads should push a clan towards their stereotypical behaviors, being why those stereotypical behaviors evolved in the first place. The Nosferatu are hideous, and their discipline spread is most useful in places with lots of rats and such. So even a Nos who wants to be a social butterfly is going to be pushed into skulking about sewers. A Ventrue's weakness makes them extremely vulnerable to herd attacks, including the sort of accidental herd attacks caused by simple chaos. Their disciplines are most useful in social situations. So even a Ventrue inclined towards a chaotic lifestyle will be pushed towards fighting for order and stability to avoid starvation.<br /> <br /> How does technology weakness push Lasombra towards behaving in their stereotypical way? Tech not working sounds like a weakness they could have given the Gangrel or Tzimisce and it would have fit better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T12:15:43-07:00","id":1393170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393018#post1393018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it doesn't. The Lasombra weakness is pretty much the greatest &amp;quot;Hey look, Hunters, I'm a Vampire&amp;quot; weakness. &amp;quot;Oh look, that guy looks a bit cool on our thermal imaging&amp;quot; raises suspicions. &amp;quot;Oh look, That guy didn't show up&amp;quot; removes all doubts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what you\u2019re getting at here. Do you mean to say that it will make them easier to be hunted so...what? The player that picks them will actually have to pay attention and the ST will have more story hooks; is that a bad thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26172-twilightspire","name":"Twilightspire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T12:22:38-07:00","id":1393172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393168#post1393168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does technology weakness push Lasombra towards behaving in their stereotypical way? Tech not working sounds like a weakness they could have given the Gangrel or Tzimisce and it would have fit better.</div> </div> </div> </div>it pushes you to rely more on your powers, which fits the lasombra (and sabbat) mentality from previous editions,<br /> and it only really affects the youngsters, as the elders rely less on modern tech (whatever modern tech is supposed to mean)<br /> <br /> personally, I don't think it fits the lasombra either, I'd say it fits more Tremere or koldun since their magic follows medieval (or pre-medieval) paradigms<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:01:19-07:00","id":1393175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393123#post1393123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bane of &quot;modern technology doesn't work&quot; is pants-on-head when you realise vampires are meant to be ancient, unchanging creatures and clan Lasombra has been around for a very long time. Like, was that weakness waiting around going &quot;Some day I'll be useful&quot; or was their problem with tech relative to the times? Did they have trouble working with belt buckles when they were introduced?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like you haven't actually read their writeup in Chicago by Night, in which case you've developed some very strong opinions based on pure speculation and no real information.<br /> <br /> It's explicitly stated that their problem isn't with technology in general but specifically technology that relies on imaging, microphonics, and haptic feedback - in other words, things that work kind of like mirrors in a sense, relying on creating an impression of them, don't pick them up clearly. Even so, it only makes using those things harder, not impossible. It basically means Lasombra have to roll to do things that would be automatic for other characters (who aren't ghosts).<br /> <br /> There's also zero effect when they operate a radio or drive a car or use a tv remote. It's pretty much just cameras and microphones and touchscreens. Even ordinary Kindred have to use the Blush of Life to operate a smartphone because they require electric feedback from the conductivity of the skin. Lasombra just have an additional issue that these things tend to glitch on them. Their voices also tend to come out distorted on phone calls, and their images are distorted in video as they are in reflections (but not absent as before).<br /> <br /> I think people are seeing &quot;modern technology&quot; and missing the fact that that term is defined for this context in the section <i>right before</i> the bane, where it also explains the reason why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:15:41-07:00","id":1393179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393172#post1393172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">personally, I don't think it fits the lasombra either, I'd say it fits more Tremere or koldun since their magic follows medieval (or pre-medieval) paradigms</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not fit Tremere philosophy. It doesn't fit the Assamites either. Alchemy is part magic, part science, and hermetic philosophy marries science to magic too. I don't think the Settites have anything that says it wouldn't be a fitting weakness, but that might be a gap in my knowledge, and there's nothing to say it would be a fitting weakness. Besides, the aversion to light weakness is extremely debilitating.<br /> <br /> Kolduns... eh.. the magic isn't in the blood; Koldunism is always out of clan. Maybe you could manifest the weakness as a sideeffect, but that goes against vampire permanence and... I don't really like it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure what you\u2019re getting at here. Do you mean to say that it will make them easier to be hunted so...what? The player that picks them will actually have to pay attention and the ST will have more story hooks; is that a bad thing? </div> </div> </div>That's what weaknesses are for. You might as well come out and say the Lasombra weakness was perfect.<br /> <br /> Look, your player might be like &quot;I sneak up on him and HE WONT SEE ME IN HIS CAR VIEW MIRROR&quot; and that's all well and good. But then you've also got &quot;I approach him and... He's running away? Oh he knows I'm a vampire because he noticed I don't show up on the wet pavement/glass reflection.<br /> <br /> The lasombra weakness is far more damaging than the Toreador weakness (And the Toreador weakness is very exploitable if you know who you're hunting). They must avoid highly reflective places in public. Lasombra wear a lot of black not just because of the darkness but also probably to mitigate the reflection issue on nighttime streets, which makes em more noticable. You can go round with a mirror to make them very easily spottable. Anybody with auspex is gonna notice. Even if you 1000 face your lasombra you've got a critical weakness. And when the hunters come knocking, everyone gets to point at the reflection myth and direct those hunters towards you.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra weakness is only not a weakness if your storyteller isn't paying attention. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-31-2020, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:28:51-07:00","id":1393183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393015#post1393015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are they removing unique clan disciplines, for what reason exactly? I've already stated this before in another thread way back, but who know's what their going to do to the Tzimisce since they've adopted this policy. You definitely know they don't like Vicissitude with all the whack-a-moles they've done with other said unique disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just part of the new edition's design philosophy, as far as I can tell. Previously the rule was &quot;every clan/bloodline has a unique discipline except four&quot;, the new rule is &quot;no clan/bloodline has a unique discipline, they're all doubled up&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which in most cases I like\u2014do we really need &quot;The Discipline Of Turning Into A Snake&quot; completely unrelated to &quot;The Discipline Of Turning Into Anything That's Not A Snake&quot;? Oblivion is the only place I don't really like it, and I think a lot of that comes down to how it was implemented in <i>Cults</i>; I'm hoping we see some changes to that before publication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:30:22-07:00","id":1393185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393175#post1393175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's explicitly stated that their problem isn't with technology in general but specifically technology that relies on imaging, microphonics, and haptic feedback - in other words, things that work kind of like mirrors in a sense, relying on creating an impression of them, don't pick them up clearly. Even so, it only makes using those things harder, not impossible. It basically means Lasombra have to roll to do things that would be automatic for other characters (who aren't ghosts).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not take this a step further? What if they can't write, can't paint, can't sew, can't work with clay... Can they Fax?<br /> <br /> The surface of a pool of water is not technology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even ordinary Kindred have to use the Blush of Life to operate a smartphone because they require electric feedback from the conductivity of the skin. </div> </div> </div>This is bullshit. Phones don't work like that. If they're going to make errors like this in today's information age they're obviously not thinking things through.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lasombra just have an additional issue that these things tend to glitch on them. Their voices also tend to come out distorted on phone calls, and their images are distorted in video as they are in reflections (but not absent as before).<br /> . </div> </div> </div>There was a really cool merit in LotC. <i>Bigger boys came. </i>where you can use your backgrounds to screw with other people using their backgrounds. How is that going to work in a world where they can't just call someone up. How is it that the cunning, Machiavellian lasombra known for their schemes, operate without modern communication technology? I know they're elites, but are they 5d chess players with vast foresight that can make up for this absurd denial of specifically modern communication technology? How did the masterminds behind the sabbat who dominated it's politics on nearly every level achieve so much? Did a clan of proud, goal oriented individualists have to hide behind ghouls when they wanted to negotiate on the phone?<br /> <br /> You might as well have them allergic to blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:31:42-07:00","id":1393186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393175#post1393175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also zero effect when they operate a radio or drive a car or use a tv remote. It's pretty much just cameras and microphones and touchscreens. Even ordinary Kindred have to use the Blush of Life to operate a smartphone because they require electric feedback from the conductivity of the skin. Lasombra just have an additional issue that these things tend to glitch on them. Their voices also tend to come out distorted on phone calls, and their images are distorted in video as they are in reflections (but not absent as before).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the book specifically calls out &quot;driving around a city&quot; as something they need help with. (Which the devs have said isn't the intent, and it makes more sense for it to be only image-related things. But the people who thinks cars are affected do have RAW backing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:38:02-07:00","id":1393188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393123#post1393123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bane of &quot;modern technology doesn't work&quot; is pants-on-head when you realise vampires are meant to be ancient, unchanging creatures and clan Lasombra has been around for a very long time. Like, was that weakness waiting around going &quot;Some day I'll be useful&quot; or was their problem with tech relative to the times? Did they have trouble working with belt buckles when they were introduced?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, modern technology <b>relying on touch or other forms of direct interaction</b> \u2014 such as voice activation or use of a stylus \u2014 tends to glitch or simply act unresponsive to Magisters </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. In other words, it's an extension of the broken-reflection thing, with your image on a camera being symbolically equivalent to a &quot;reflection&quot;. Their bane in earlier times was presumably the same as it is today:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Anyone seeing the reflection</b> or recording (live and otherwise) <b>of a Lasombra vampire can instantly recognize them for what they are</b>, provided they know what they\u2019re looking for. </div> </div> </div>That's the very first sentence of their bane in the official writeup. The &quot;roll to use tech&quot; thing is a side note at the end, to incorporate the Bane Severity mechanic (like how the most debilitating part of the Tremere bane is the inability to bond other vampires, and there's a small side detriment involving Bane Severity added on).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:40:45-07:00","id":1393189,"title":"","content":"I admit, when I do Lasombra I had, &quot;Lasombra don't show up in mirrors but do show up on cameras and videos because it's about vampire hunters being able to detect them, not about being invisible.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also added a weakness to silver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:41:19-07:00","id":1393190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393185#post1393185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is bullshit. Phones don't work like that. If they're going to make errors like this in today's information age they're obviously not thinking things through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately it's difficult to be sure how touchscreens interact with magically reanimated corpses in the real world, because it's really hard to find vampires and zombies willing to act as product testers. If you find a real-world study on the undead and touchscreens, though, do let me know, I'd be interested to read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:44:33-07:00","id":1393191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393190#post1393190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately it's difficult to be sure how touchscreens interact with magically reanimated corpses in the real world, because it's really hard to find vampires and zombies willing to act as product testers. If you find a real-world study on the undead and touchscreens, though, do let me know, I'd be interested to read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's right about the touch screen thing, otherwise stylus and the posh gloves would not work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:59:36-07:00","id":1393197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393189#post1393189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, when I do Lasombra I had, &quot;Lasombra don't show up in mirrors but do show up on cameras and videos because it's about vampire hunters being able to detect them, not about being invisible.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of storytellers do that. They did justify it with 'modern cameras don't all use mirrors&quot; (I think most still do) but it works nicely anyway.<br /> I wouldn't add a silver weakness. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393191#post1393191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's right about the touch screen thing, otherwise stylus and the posh gloves would not work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall someone using a sausage to demonstrate the effect. I think you do need a degree of conductivity, but you don't have to be alive for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-31-2020, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:09:10-07:00","id":1393200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393185#post1393185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not take this a step further? What if they can't write, can't paint, can't sew, can't work with clay... Can they Fax?</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re not even attempting to discuss in good faith here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is bullshit. Phones don't work like that. If they're going to make errors like this in today's information age they're obviously not thinking things through. </div> </div> </div>Try operating your smartphone with a stick or a pencil, or even wearing gloves without special conductive thread worked into them, and then get back to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 05-31-2020, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:13:43-07:00","id":1393201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393186#post1393186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the book specifically calls out &quot;driving around a city&quot; as something they need help with. (Which the devs have said isn't the intent, and it makes more sense for it to be only image-related things. But the people who thinks cars are affected do have RAW backing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not actually what it says, though. It says they have ghouls to do basic things for them, up to and including chauffeuring them about, so little things like making calls are no biggie. It doesn\u2019t actually say they have trouble driving themselves. That\u2019s something people are inferring from the proximity of the statements that\u2019s not intended. (Sure, an editor might have caught it as a possible misread, but here we are.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:17:06-07:00","id":1393204,"title":"","content":"Random headcanon but I assume Lasombra would only have trouble driving modern electronic cars.<br /> <br /> Oddly, the more you focus on this weakness, the more it becomes like Harry Dresden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:20:56-07:00","id":1393205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393191#post1393191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's right about the touch screen thing, otherwise stylus and the posh gloves would not work.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember right, capacitive touchscreens by design only detect big conductive things\u2014it's how they avoid being set off by drops of water. Styluses are generally too small to activate screens on their own, so they're designed to connect to your body and use that. Same with gloves with capacitive threads in the fingertips.<br /> <br /> Now, my previous snarky post aside, I actually don't know if cadavers are very conductive. Most of the papers I've found about that are about e.g. ways to estimate time of death by checking the conductivity of muscle tissue, not about the skin. But as you've mentioned, I know reasonably-sized sausages do work; I'd allow a Lasombra to make a Crafts roll or whatever to connect a stylus to a piece of metal in their sleeve or something like that, at which point the stylus works fine, since it's not relying on anything symbolically associated with their shadow or reflection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:21:57-07:00","id":1393207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393204#post1393204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random headcanon but I assume Lasombra would only have trouble driving modern electronic cars.<br /> <br /> Oddly, the more you focus on this weakness, the more it becomes like Harry Dresden.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect they\u2019d have trouble with a fancy car lock that required a fingerprint or the entering of a code on a touchscreen. But most keyless entry is based on the proximity of the key fob or the press of an actual button, so they\u2019re good. They can work mechanical things just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:24:10-07:00","id":1393208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393204#post1393204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly, the more you focus on this weakness, the more it becomes like Harry Dresden.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one take on it; I prefer the take that it comes down to their lack of reflection (and photographs are symbolically reflections, and phone calls are symbolically echoes, etc).<br /> <br /> But I did invent an Oblivion power for the Dresden take, since I know some players like that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">Jinx</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">All Lasombra are intimately familiar with how Oblivion interacts with technology. Most of the time, it's nothing but a headache, turning a simple text message into a minutes-long struggle to make the keyboard respond properly. But some Lasombra have found ways to twist this trait into something more useful against the SI.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">Cost: One Rouse Check.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">System: The Lasombra pulls on the Oblivion-energy in their blood, drawing it into their mouth and lungs, then exhales it as a faint black-and-red mist that disperses into the air. If they succeed at a Resolve + Oblivion roll (difficulty 3), all complex technology within five meters per point of margin jams, malfunctions, or shuts down. On a critical win, the devices burn out and cannot be reactivated without extensive repairs. \u201cComplex technology\u201d generally includes all electronics and any mechanical device with at least five moving parts.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","user":"Draconis","date":". 05-31-2020, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:24:29-07:00","id":1393209,"title":"","content":"I find it funny that someone could claim the old clan flaw made hunting difficult for Lasombras. They could hide into the shadows and refelctive surfaces would not give them away when attacking prey from behind. The only way for the old clan flaw to hinder Lasombras hunting could conceivably be when talking with the meal to be at a bar or something like that. But even then the victim would have to be able to manage noticing the no reflection thing when talking with someone with dominate (and possibly some Presence). Not likely at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:25:20-07:00","id":1393210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393204#post1393204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random headcanon but I assume Lasombra would only have trouble driving modern electronic cars.</div> </div> </div> </div>considering modern cars can be shut down at a distance, by satellite or whatever,<br /> I'd assume most careful vampires would stick to older cars","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:25:32-07:00","id":1393211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393201#post1393201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s not actually what it says, though. It says they have ghouls to do basic things for them, up to and including chauffeuring them about, so little things like making calls are no biggie. It doesn\u2019t actually say they have trouble driving themselves. That\u2019s something people are inferring from the proximity of the statements that\u2019s not intended. (Sure, an editor might have caught it as a possible misread, but here we are.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm just trying to say that I don't really blame players who read it that way\u2014I think more of the blame falls on the editors. Because I read it the same way until I saw the dev clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:34:35-07:00","id":1393215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393209#post1393209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it funny that someone could claim the old clan flaw made hunting difficult for Lasombras. They could hide into the shadows and refelctive surfaces would not give them away when attacking prey from behind. The only way for the old clan flaw to hinder Lasombras hunting could conceivably be when talking with the meal to be at a bar or something like that. But even then the victim would have to be able to manage noticing the no reflection thing when talking with someone with dominate (and possibly some Presence). Not likely at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mirrors are basically everywhere so it would be an enormous inconveinance to go to a bar and be the only person lacking a reflection. Which will, if you are a person familiar with pop culture, immediately point out the person as a vampire. One of the best ways to violate the Masquerade since its a harmless way to prove someone is supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/dshJG5PEOqY\" data-code=\"dshJG5PEOqY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/dshJG5PEOqY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It's also very easy for a vampire hunter to test a Lasombra about their vampire status.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:47:49-07:00","id":1393219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393215#post1393215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mirrors are basically everywhere so it would be an enormous inconveinance to go to a bar and be the only person lacking a reflection. Which will, if you are a person familiar with pop culture, immediately point out the person as a vampire. One of the best ways to violate the Masquerade since its a harmless way to prove someone is supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, add to that the no drinking/no eating (still a thing in v5, right?), the no going out during the day, and the whole issue with biting people when you don't have dominate to make them forget<br /> <br /> I think having no reflection is a very small inconvenience when you have the ability to make people forget, to not being identified on camera, to teleport through shadows etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:49:10-07:00","id":1393221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393219#post1393219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah, add to that the no drinking/no eating (still a thing in v5, right?), the no going out during the day, and the whole issue with biting people when you don't have dominate to make them forget<br /> <br /> I think having no reflection is a very small inconvenience compared to the ability to make people forget, not being identified on camera, teleporting through shadows etc</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree the &quot;not being identified on camera&quot; thing is a huge benefit and I would never do it in my game. Lasombra should have much-much more trouble with the Masquerade not be easier to cover up their presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:53:28-07:00","id":1393223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393221#post1393221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lasombra should have much-much more trouble with the Masquerade not be easier to cover up their presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>exactly, Haquim was saying that the old weakness made things easier, not harder<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:54:49-07:00","id":1393224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393223#post1393223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> exactly, Haquim was saying that the old weakness made things easier, not harder</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I posted how I modified it. Honestly, I think the new version is overcompensating, though. I don't think it is very &quot;classic&quot; vampire to have mirrors have distortion and not being able to use cellphones versus a missing reflection in mirrors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:56:15-07:00","id":1393225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393215#post1393215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mirrors are basically everywhere so it would be an enormous inconveinance to go to a bar and be the only person lacking a reflection. Which will, if you are a person familiar with pop culture, immediately point out the person as a vampire. One of the best ways to violate the Masquerade since its a harmless way to prove someone is supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/dshJG5PEOqY\" data-code=\"dshJG5PEOqY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/dshJG5PEOqY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It's also very easy for a vampire hunter to test a Lasombra about their vampire status.</div> </div> </div> </div>Realistically people won't notice unless under the right circumstances (a few people at the bar, the action has not started yet) and besides Lasombras are well aware of their weakness so they can easily avoid hunting grounds where they can be easily spotted. Even more to the point, people tend to rationalize stuff like not seeing a reflection in a mirror (that's how the Masquerade works...) they don't immediately jump to the conclusion they are dealing with something that they believe does not exist, UNLESS they know what they are dealing with before hand (which is pointed out in the new Lasombra clan flaw).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:59:32-07:00","id":1393227,"title":"","content":"are there any Requiem players here?<br /> <br /> iirc, Requiem had all vampires not cast reflections and don't appear on pictures and videos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T15:21:33-07:00","id":1393231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393225#post1393225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Realistically people won't notice unless under the right circumstances (a few people at the bar, the action has not started yet) and besides Lasombras are well aware of their weakness so they can easily avoid hunting grounds where they can be easily spotted. Even more to the point, people tend to rationalize stuff like not seeing a reflection in a mirror (that's how the Masquerade works...) they don't immediately jump to the conclusion they are dealing with something that they believe does not exist, UNLESS they know what they are dealing with before hand (which is pointed out in the new Lasombra clan flaw).</div> </div> </div> </div>The best hunting grounds are most often mirror mad though: clubs, bars. most elevators have mirrors in them. Walking by a busy road is a masquerade hazard. standing near calm bodies of water is a hazard. There are mirrors where you dont expect them. You also have no way of knowing that your packmate drew a penis on your forhead before you woke, they could just be bluffing. you'd also be at a big disadvantage in a hall if mirrors setpiece.... <br /> <br /> <br /> the phone ban simply does not fit with lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T15:28:37-07:00","id":1393234,"title":"","content":"Pro tip for Sabbat players:<br /> <br /> If you find yourself in monomacy with a Lasombra, just stand back, cock your head to the side, and ask, &quot;What's up with your hair? I never noticed... the way it... did you do that on purpose?&quot;<br /> <br /> Demand an initiative bonus from your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T15:30:46-07:00","id":1393237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393234#post1393234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pro tip for Sabbat players:<br /> <br /> If you find yourself in monomacy with a Lasombra, just stand back, cock your head to the side, and ask, &quot;What's up with your hair? I never noticed... the way it... did you do that on purpose?&quot;<br /> <br /> Demand an initiative bonus from your ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit part of why I love the idea they show up in cameras is a Spaceballs joke.<br /> <br /> *Lasombra embraced in the Dark Ages looks at photos in 1920s*<br /> <br /> &quot;WHY DIDN'T SOMEONE TELL ME MY ASS WAS SO BIG!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T15:32:19-07:00","id":1393238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393237#post1393237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;WHY DIDN'T SOMEONE TELL ME MY ASS WAS SO BIG!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>all you have to do is dominate someone into telling you if your ass is too big","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T15:33:21-07:00","id":1393239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393238#post1393238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> all you have to do is dominate someone into telling you if your ass is too big</div> </div> </div> </div>They won't have a Lasombra's eye and any other Lasombra would be lying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T15:34:27-07:00","id":1393240,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> <br /> \u200bEXACTLY. The new bane for the Lasombra is one of the most bizarre things possible. Why should their bane be related to Technology, what sense does this make? Since when did the original [Lasombra] was duking it out with some sort of time traveled iPhone all the back in the BCE era? What does mere technology have to do with being one with the shadows? They just made this new bane for the modern age specifically when ICly the REAL clan curse pre-V5 should be the one that makes the most sense. It's just ludicrous that they'd just whack out Lasombra's other fitting curse.<br /> <br /> To touch on another topic that has been brought up in this thread: The Lasombra joining the Camarilla is a disaster. The VENTURE are supposed to be the aristocratic styled clan that is supposed to be the main for the Camarilla- the Lasombra SHOULD be with the Sabbat where they fit the best, a sect specifically devoted to shredding the illusion maintaining humanity. You can really tell the writers just don't like the Sabbat.. for whatever reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T15:53:04-07:00","id":1393242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393205#post1393205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I remember right, capacitive touchscreens by design only detect big conductive things\u2014it's how they avoid being set off by drops of water. Styluses are generally too small to activate screens on their own, so they're designed to connect to your body and use that. Same with gloves with capacitive threads in the fingertips.<br /> <br /> Now, my previous snarky post aside, I actually don't know if cadavers are very conductive. Most of the papers I've found about that are about e.g. ways to estimate time of death by checking the conductivity of muscle tissue, not about the skin. But as you've mentioned, I know reasonably-sized sausages do work; I'd allow a Lasombra to make a Crafts roll or whatever to connect a stylus to a piece of metal in their sleeve or something like that, at which point the stylus works fine, since it's not relying on anything symbolically associated with their shadow or reflection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just know that my cheap ass bit of rubber on a tube stylus works <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and my faux leather riding gloves work fine as well, so it can't be living tissue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T15:54:02-07:00","id":1393243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393227#post1393227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are there any Requiem players here?<br /> <br /> iirc, Requiem had all vampires not cast reflections and don't appear on pictures and videos</div> </div> </div> </div>No, 1st edition Requiem had them work a bit like current Lasombra, in that they produced distorted reflections and images, except when they concentrated really hard. Requiem 2e dropped that in favor of saying the Beast just instinctively knows where to stand so as to not be identifiable on camera, even if the vampire isn\u2019t conscious of it (and reflections are normal). But the Beast in Requiem 2e is more of a sentient being in its own right than just an irrational hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T16:18:50-07:00","id":1393249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393243#post1393243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, 1st edition Requiem had them work a bit like current Lasombra, in that they produced distorted reflections and images, except when they concentrated really hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>how did they explain maintaining the masquerade with that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T16:23:56-07:00","id":1393250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393249#post1393249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how did they explain maintaining the masquerade with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>People's default assumption is a camera glitch rather than vampires (like with V5 Lasombra). But actual vampire hunters generally know better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T16:29:42-07:00","id":1393252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393249#post1393249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> how did they explain maintaining the masquerade with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Draconis said, but it\u2019s also worth noting this was one of the first things on the chopping block in 2e because it seems most people ignored it anyway. As a generalized thing for all vampires it didn\u2019t serve much of a purpose, and players weren\u2019t all that interested in spending Willpower to look at themselves in the mirror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T16:32:20-07:00","id":1393254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393227#post1393227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are there any Requiem players here?<br /> <br /> iirc, Requiem had all vampires not cast reflections and don't appear on pictures and videos</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Flag has explained how it works for vampires in general, but V5 Lasombra are a bit like Hollow Mekhet, such as Francis Black, the protagonist of the Mekhet clanbook. The reflections of Hollow Mekhet have separate lives and don't appear in the mirror or video footage at all unless they choose to do so. She can't record her voice or make phone calls either. She can use email and text messaging however.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that the bane isn't supposed to have anything to do with technology so much as anything to that reflects or records their image in some way besides sensory organs; they should be able to use <i>mobile </i>phones (texts), computers and cars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 05-31-2020, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T16:43:05-07:00","id":1393256,"title":"","content":"I see...well, a few years back, whenever the &quot;masquerade is untenable&quot; topic would spring up,<br /> there were always Requiem fans mentioning that requiem handled it better","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T18:01:34-07:00","id":1393273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393256#post1393256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see...well, a few years back, whenever the &quot;masquerade is untenable&quot; topic would spring up,<br /> there were always Requiem fans mentioning that requiem handled it better</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that would not have occurred to me. I think Requiem\u2019s main contribution is in framing the Masquerade as safeguarding specific knowledge of vampiric institutions, powers, weaknesses, and individual identities, but being generally unconcerned about whether individual humans believe in vampires. The assumption is that most Requiem vampires have herds of mortals who consent to be fed on and know what\u2019s happening. I don\u2019t think their reflections had anything to do with it (and certainly don\u2019t now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 05-31-2020, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T19:31:44-07:00","id":1393298,"title":"","content":"In some ways, I feel a little bad for the developers/writers/editors etc.<br /> <br /> I've been picking through the details of VtM since the old days of the White Wolf forum. I was there when it vanished. What I'm saying is I am old... and getting older by the minute. But, I digress, as old folks are prone to do.<br /> <br /> Anyway, since the Lasombra's first appearance, fans have been gnawing on the bone of the Lasombra bane.<ul><li>&quot;Wait, what about those automatic doors in grocery stores?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, what about car phones?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, what about ambient lighting. People reflect light onto surrounding surfaces, don't they?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, what if they leave a fingerprint on a mirror? Does it reflect?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, does it affect objects they hold or wear?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, what if they hold a mirror and reflect someone else's image in it into a third mirror. Could you see that image?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, what if they ate another creature whole... like a goldfish... would you see it hanging in mid-air in a mirror?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;wait, what if they throw an object in front of a mirror? Does it magically appear in mid-air?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, if it affects objects they hold, a Lasombra could never work as a checkout cashier, because of the upc scanners?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, if they are cut and bleed all over someone, would the bloody person look clean in the mirror?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, if a Lasombra picked me up in front of a mirror, would it look like I was flying or would I be invisible, too?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, could you bounce a laser off a mirror, and shoot it <i>through</i> the Lasombra?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, so if I hide behind a Lasombra, and you see them in a mirror, you can see me?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, the only way we see anything is by reflecting light within the lens of our eyes to focus it on the retina. How does anyone see the Lasombra, ever?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, so if they sat on a photocopier and sent their image of themselves as a fax, what would happen?&quot; (This <i>was</i> 1996!)</li> <li>&quot;Wait, what if an AI system drew a picture of them, and put it up on a screen?&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Wait, so do diamonds look different on them, since the Lasombra's reflected light isn't bouncing around inside?&quot;</li> </ul><br /> And so on, and so on, and etcetera, ad infinitum, ad nauseum... seriously it grew tiresome. Understand, it has been going on for a long time. Nations have appeared and vanished. Whole industrial sectors have risen and fallen. It's been so long the poles have moved.<br /> <br /> For V5, the writers tried to create the best written weakness they could, and they did an okay job of it. Not a homerun, but they a least got on base.<br /> <br /> How would all y'all have written it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T19:38:31-07:00","id":1393302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393298#post1393298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would all y'all have written it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that I combined a vulnerability to silver with the invisibility in mirrors (even though most mirrors don't have silver backings anymore).<br /> <br /> Its magic after all and shouldn't be something that you have to overthink.<br /> <br /> But if I was hired to remake it for V5 and not use my own stuff?<br /> <br /> Lasombra are invisible in mirrors, reflective surfaces, and puddles but not cameras or photographs. Lasombra are acutely aware of this quality and their lack of humanity in such that if they are caught by a reflective surface, they suffer a -1 to all dice rolls. The discomfort from their inhumanity being captured existing on an instinctual level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T19:54:08-07:00","id":1393308,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393046#post1393046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d just have the lasombra antitribu grow naturaly: more embraces, more defections, more elders exiting torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>For that matter, hasn\u2019t Montano been a member of the Camarilla since it was founded, if not actually one of the Founders themselves? That justifies a full range of generations for Lasombra antitribu going back 500+ years even without other refugees of the Anarch Revolt. Who would have told <i><b>him</b></i> that he couldn\u2019t embrace childer?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393197#post1393197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall someone using a sausage to demonstrate the effect. I think you do need a degree of conductivity, but you don\u2019t have to be alive for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the sake of Science I just tested my smartphone with a roughly finger-shaped piece of turkey fresh out of the fridge and below-room-temperature dead meat works just fine aside from leaving the screen greasy. Whatever\u2019s at work with the Lasombra weakness re: smartphones, it\u2019s more than just lacking a living body\u2019s electrical conductivity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393215#post1393215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mirrors are basically everywhere so it would be an enormous inconveinance to go to a bar and be the only person lacking a reflection. Which will, if you are a person familiar with pop culture, immediately point out the person as a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d imagine Dracula is one of the Lasombra\u2019s least favorite people in the whole World of Darkness since his authorized biography made their Clan Bane popular knowledge throughout the western world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:01:35-07:00","id":1393310,"title":"","content":"I think the Lasombra defecting nicely underscores that they have a Clan culture that believes in survival of the fittest. They don't believe in Loyalty and think of that as a weakness.<br /> <br /> Them betraying the Sabbat just shows what they do to anyone who shows the slightest sign of weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:37:27-07:00","id":1393322,"title":"","content":"A &quot;weakness&quot; in the Sabbat that was arbitrarily done to fit in with the current tone and &quot;themes&quot; of V5. The writers didn't like the Sabbat, but liked the Lasombra, so this is why these mass defections to the Camarilla have taken despite centuries of Jyhadic warfare against the Cam. The Lasombra are a proud Clan and I couldn't think of them abandoning what they've built up in the Sabbat to go to the sect on the opposite field that for the most part has been cultivated by the Ventrue, the Clan they rival and despise the most. A sect if I may add again- that is primarily headed by Ventrue. I wonder.. the mass defections to the Camarilla alone don't make sense, but at the time of thinking this up, how come they never did to reactions on what the Ventrue would even allow this mass influx to go about in the first place?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't the Ventrue not want the Lasombra in the Clan at all because further down the line they'd be more struggle for who has the most influence in the Camarilla? They already have alot on their plate in the form of Tremere and Toreador, so what gives?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-01-2020, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:56:16-07:00","id":1393330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393322#post1393322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A &quot;weakness&quot; in the Sabbat that was arbitrarily done to fit in with the current tone and &quot;themes&quot; of V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this how Storytelling works? You want to tell a story and explain how things got there? Natural events don't happen in a fictional world. So you create a theme and talk about how they came about.<br /> <br /> Metaplot by nature requires things to happen that are shocking and world-changing. It's my favorite part of vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The writers didn't like the Sabbat, but liked the Lasombra, so this is why these mass defections to the Camarilla have taken despite centuries of Jyhadic warfare against the Cam. </div> </div> </div>That's making assumptions about the writers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lasombra are a proud Clan and I couldn't think of them abandoning what they've built up in the Sabbat to go to the sect on the opposite field that for the most part has been cultivated by the Ventrue, </div> </div> </div>Also, this would be a valid argument if not for the fact that we already have several high profile Lasombra abandoning the sect like Giangaleazzo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A sect if I may add again- that is primarily headed by Ventrue. I wonder the mass defections to the Camarilla alone don't make sense, but at the time of thinking this up, how come they never did to reactions on what the Ventrue would even allow this mass influx to go about in the first place? </div> </div> </div>Because they intend to take the Camarilla for themselves. Because the Ventrue can strike at their enemies (The Sabbat) and enrich the sect at its weakest moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wouldn't the Ventrue not want the Lasombra in the Clan at all because further down the line they'd be more struggle for who has the most influence in the Camarilla? They already have alot on their plate in the form of Tremere and Toreador, so what gives? </div> </div> </div>No, I can't imagine any scenario the Ventrue wouldn't want the Lasombra against their enemies. They don't shirk from challenges anymore than the Lasombra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T21:05:29-07:00","id":1393333,"title":"","content":"But the Lasombra and the Tzimisce ARE (were as of V5) the face of the Sabbat (the enemies that the Camarilla focus on). How can the long lived Elders of the Ventrue and via extent of having the most control, the Camarilla, can trust all of these Lasombra despite centuries of sect war off the bat so readily to justify these mass unvetted defections?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T21:23:04-07:00","id":1393335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393333#post1393333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Lasombra and the Tzimisce ARE (were as of V5) the face of the Sabbat (the enemies that the Camarilla focus on). How can the long lived Elders of the Ventrue and via extent of having the most control, the Camarilla, can trust all of these Lasombra despite centuries of sect war off the bat so readily to justify these mass unvetted defections?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They do not trust them. They are bidding their time, as they have been doing for centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T21:34:54-07:00","id":1393340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393333#post1393333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Lasombra and the Tzimisce ARE (were as of V5) the face of the Sabbat (the enemies that the Camarilla focus on). How can the long lived Elders of the Ventrue and via extent of having the most control, the Camarilla, can trust all of these Lasombra despite centuries of sect war off the bat so readily to justify these mass unvetted defections?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because at the end of the day the Sabbat and Camarilla were two sides of the same coin. It was all a scam on their Neonates anyway. The real fight was always for power and domain.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Honestly, in Doylist terms rather than Watsonian, the choice to have the Lasombra join the Camarilla was done fairly late in the game with the decision made for Chicago by Night. Apparently, there were questions of whether it would be the Hecata or the Banu Haqim who would join the sect and ended up being the Banu Haqim and Lasombra. The writers had to submit reasons why they thought it would be a good idea as well as presentations.<br /> <br /> I think having the Lasombra join the Camarilla was a good idea out of universe because they're an extremely popular clan and well-known for intrigue as well as subtlety. Those are things that the Camarilla have always been famous for and Lasombra Antitribu are very common in LARPs. Previous game books always emphasized the Lasombra Antitribu were hunted relentlessly and discouraged Camarilla characters of that Clan. So it makes sense to make it easier for Lasombra to be part of the Camarilla as a favor to the fandom that loves them as well as taking advantage of them as a well-loved clan. Certainly, by also adding them to Chicago by Night, it meant Sabbat players could also have the rules for playing them in their games.<br /> <br /> In-universe, I think the Lasombra defection makes sense as a nice way to handle the aftermath of the events of Beckett's Jyhad Diary. The end of the book has the Friends of the Night encounter the quite-alive and kicking Lasombra Antediluvian at his castle along with Beckett. You shouldn't have the realization the basis for the Sabbat's entire Lasombra defection [we beat our eldest] being revealed to be a lie have no consequences. Throw in the various Civil Wars, Crusades, and the Second Inquisition and you have a pretty good argument that the Sabbat will have Lasombra who want to try and do something better for themselves.<br /> <br /> I assume the half of the Lasombra who stayed are the ones who have thrived in the sect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T22:37:33-07:00","id":1393350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393330#post1393330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's making assumptions about the writers.</div> </div> </div> </div>One that seems totally warranted by everything written about the Sabbat this edition. Seriously, nothing so far shows anything but contempt for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T22:37:37-07:00","id":1393351,"title":"","content":"Well, with any large scale change in setting politics, we can always ask the question of how realistic it would be for such a change to happen in such a short amount of time when there has been relatively little change in the past 500 years.<br /> <br /> How is it the Gangrel, such a chaotic Clan of individualists, joined the Camarilla in the first place and then how did they organize so completely as to leave it as a whole? How did the Brujah leave the Camarilla so quickly as a whole? Why were the Banu Haqim accepted when for centuries the were a Clan dedicated to murdering and diablerizing other vampires. The Lasombra joining the Camarilla is no less realistic than any change that has been introduced in V5 or even Revised for that matter. At least the Lasombra being in the Camarilla is something that makes a lot of sense and is something that some people (like me) have wanted for a long time. <br /> <br /> With all of those seemingly sudden changes, we could imagine that these changes happen slowly over time and the books only bring these changes to our attention when they reach a critical mass. We have to keep in mind that role playing books that follow a real world timeline can\u2019t spend a century slowly having Lasombra enter the Camarilla, become more of an influence, and so on. New changes get made with new editions and if they are changes that we like (this is one I like) we admit that it had to seem a bit jarring, but we can better contextualize these changes by imagining the events before the current year building towards this. <br /> <br /> I think that the Lasombra make an interesting dichotomy with the Ventrue, as the Lasombra are more ruthless social Darwinist sorts of rulers, where as the Ventrue are more aristocratic with a sort of Noblesse Oblige.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T22:41:58-07:00","id":1393353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393350#post1393350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One that seems totally warranted by everything written about the Sabbat this edition. Seriously, nothing so far shows anything but contempt for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it may be the case what they like about them is not necessarily what you like about them.<br /> <br /> But I don't actually disagree with you--I think a Sabbat book should have been the fourth thing released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T22:51:40-07:00","id":1393354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393351#post1393351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, with any large scale change in setting politics, we can always ask the question of how realistic it would be for such a change to happen in such a short amount of time when there has been relatively little change in the past 500 years.<br /> <br /> How is it the Gangrel, such a chaotic Clan of individualists, joined the Camarilla in the first place and then how did they organize so completely as to leave it as a whole? How did the Brujah leave the Camarilla so quickly as a whole? Why were the Banu Haqim accepted when for centuries the were a Clan dedicated to murdering and diablerizing other vampires. The Lasombra joining the Camarilla is no less realistic than any change that has been introduced in V5 or even Revised for that matter. At least the Lasombra being in the Camarilla is something that makes a lot of sense and is something that some people (like me) have wanted for a long time.<br /> <br /> With all of those seemingly sudden changes, we could imagine that these changes happen slowly over time and the books only bring these changes to our attention when they reach a critical mass. We have to keep in mind that role playing books that follow a real world timeline can\u2019t spend a century slowly having Lasombra enter the Camarilla, become more of an influence, and so on. New changes get made with new editions and if they are changes that we like (this is one I like) we admit that it had to seem a bit jarring, but we can better contextualize these changes by imagining the events before the current year building towards this.<br /> <br /> I think that the Lasombra make an interesting dichotomy with the Ventrue, as the Lasombra are more ruthless social Darwinist sorts of rulers, where as the Ventrue are more aristocratic with a sort of Noblesse Oblige.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think the answer to your question is, &quot;Very easily.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Because there's not that many vampires in the world. Assuming the usual, 100K vampires in the world number is mostly accurate then divide that by 14 (13+Caitiff) and you have roughly 7000 vampires per Clan. We're not counting the Bloodlines in this but assume they're just added to the above 100K for the sake of simplicity.<br /> <br /> Vampires are not nations, they're small towns at best.<br /> <br /> But let's throw out some other numbers.<br /> <br /> Let's say that the Antitribu of a given clan consist of roughly 10% of their numbers.<br /> <br /> That means that's 700 or so from the existing numbers.<br /> <br /> 6,300 vampires in the Clans of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Now how many memberd are part of the Anarchs?<br /> <br /> An equal amount as the Antitribu?<br /> <br /> Less? More?<br /> <br /> Let's actually not remove any and assume they're Camarilla by default like the Inner Council says (at least until later). Let's also pretend the Second Inquisition hasn't killed thousands of vampires and a substantial chunk of the Kindred race (maybe as much as 10%--leading to the whole feuding). Let's also not include any losses to the Beckoning or Gehenna War.<br /> <br /> It could also be much higher percentage than 1:10 vampires but let's go with this. Xavier would have to just convince more than 3150 Gangrel that it's better being independent than going with the Camarilla to have more than half be independent. Even then, it's already a Clan that is mostly nomadic and wandering the wilderness. For the Brujah, all you'd have to do was have the Camarilla say &quot;we're keeping the Elders and Loyalists.&quot;<br /> <br /> If that's say, 4000--less than a 3/rd of the population of my shitty town, that's the majority of Brujah by far. Hell, if they just banished all of the Anarch Brujah that's a huge chunk of the clan itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-01-2020, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T22:54:43-07:00","id":1393355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393353#post1393353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it may be the case what they like about them is not necessarily what you like about them.<br /> <br /> But I don't actually disagree with you--I think a Sabbat book should have been the fourth thing released.</div> </div> </div> </div>They like mindless, idiotic orcs for anarchs to beat up, and acceptable target terrorists, 2 dimensional cannon fodder basically. Anything with greater nuances than that is being stripped out, killed or retgoned.<br /> <br /> So naked loathing of the sect basically (which shouldn't really be a shock, and has been a trend since the Sabbat on humanity disaster of revised.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-01-2020, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T22:58:13-07:00","id":1393356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393355#post1393355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They like mindless, idiotic orcs for anarchs to beat up, and acceptable target terrorists, 2 dimensional cannon fodder basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I don't think you can say that because:<br /> <br /> 1. The Gehenna Crusaders aren't there to fight<br /> 2. The Lasombra aren't mindless orcs because the defectors are portrayed as intelligent ruthless geniuses.<br /> 3. The Seven Fires are one specific terrorist group in a book and a breakway sect. I felt the writing was really good there.<br /> <br /> Have you read the Seven Fires section of THE CHICAGO FOLIOS?<br /> <br /> Anyway, we'll see what happens come Players Guide but....well, that'll be awhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-01-2020, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T23:03:55-07:00","id":1393359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393356#post1393356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I don't think you can say that because:<br /> <br /> 1. The Gehenna Crusaders aren't there to fight<br /> 2. The Lasombra aren't mindless orcs because the defectors are portrayed as intelligent ruthless geniuses.<br /> 3. The Seven Fires are one specific terrorist group in a book and a breakway sect. I felt the writing was really good there.<br /> <br /> Have you read the Seven Fires section of THE CHICAGO FOLIOS?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) the Gehenna crusade are their to die, or get replaced by possessing ancients.<br /> <br /> 2) and CbN makes it clear the Lasombra left behind where the mindless ones <br /> <br /> 3) not read them, don't own Folios, and furlough is not the time to buy pdfs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't expect a Sabbat book that is anything more than a monster manual this edition, Anarchs are supposed to fill that need now, and the new humanity system is supposed to make paths obsolete, maybe for some that works, but not for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-01-2020, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T23:05:13-07:00","id":1393361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393333#post1393333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Lasombra and the Tzimisce ARE (were as of V5) the face of the Sabbat (the enemies that the Camarilla focus on). How can the long lived Elders of the Ventrue and via extent of having the most control, the Camarilla, can trust all of these Lasombra despite centuries of sect war off the bat so readily to justify these mass unvetted defections?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your view of things is awfully simplistic and contradicted in numerous places in the lore going back to 2nd edition, which has been pointed out repeatedly, not to mention that you clearly haven\u2019t even read the treatment of the subject in Chicago by Night, which addresses all of these issues and explicitly contradicts your assertions here. The real question is why anyone should be baited into arguing with you when you won\u2019t even inform yourself about the subject, in fact have no interest in it, made up your mind before even beginning to investigate it, and are not really interested in anything anyone says in response to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T23:09:08-07:00","id":1393363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393361#post1393361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your view of things is awfully simplistic and contradicted in numerous places in the lore going back to 2nd edition, which has been pointed out repeatedly, not to mention that you clearly haven\u2019t even read the treatment of the subject in Chicago by Night, which addresses all of these issues and explicitly contradicts your assertions here. The real question is why anyone should be baited into arguing with you when you won\u2019t even inform yourself about the subject, in fact have no interest in it, made up your mind before even beginning to investigate it, and are not really interested in anything anyone says in response to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, everyone has a right to say what they love or don't love on the forums as long as they're respectful of other posters as well as the developers.<br /> <br /> Taggie also tried the Conviction system. It just didn't work for him.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T23:24:36-07:00","id":1393367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393354#post1393354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think the answer to your question is, &quot;Very easily.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Because there's not that many vampires in the world. Assuming the usual, 100K vampires in the world number is mostly accurate then divide that by 14 (13+Caitiff) and you have roughly 7000 vampires per Clan. We're not counting the Bloodlines in this but assume they're just added to the above 100K for the sake of simplicity.<br /> <br /> Vampires are not nations, they're small towns at best.<br /> <br /> But let's throw out some other numbers.<br /> <br /> Let's say that the Antitribu of a given clan consist of roughly 10% of their numbers.<br /> <br /> That means that's 700 or so from the existing numbers.<br /> <br /> 6,300 vampires in the Clans of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Now how many memberd are part of the Anarchs?<br /> <br /> An equal amount as the Antitribu?<br /> <br /> Less? More?<br /> <br /> Let's actually not remove any and assume they're Camarilla by default like the Inner Council says (at least until later). Let's also pretend the Second Inquisition hasn't killed thousands of vampires and a substantial chunk of the Kindred race (maybe as much as 10%--leading to the whole feuding). Let's also not include any losses to the Beckoning or Gehenna War.<br /> <br /> It could also be much higher percentage than 1:10 vampires but let's go with this. Xavier would have to just convince more than 3150 Gangrel that it's better being independent than going with the Camarilla to have more than half be independent. Even then, it's already a Clan that is mostly nomadic and wandering the wilderness. For the Brujah, all you'd have to do was have the Camarilla say &quot;we're keeping the Elders and Loyalists.&quot;<br /> <br /> If that's say, 4000--less than a 3/rd of the population of my shitty town, that's the majority of Brujah by far. Hell, if they just banished all of the Anarch Brujah that's a huge chunk of the clan itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that brings up an issue - what determines whether a Clan is in a Sect? Of course you can have members of any Clan in any Sect, but when is Brujah officially a Camarilla Clan and when is it not. I very much doubt it has anything to do with what percentage of the Clan population is in the Camarilla versus outside of it. A Clan with 6000 total vampires could still be recognized as a Camarilla Clan and have a Justicar and representation on the Inner Circle even if only 2000 of those vampires were in the Camarilla. That, it seems, is what determines Camarilla membership. Does the Clan have a Justicar, yes or no. Yes, it is a Camarilla Clan. No, it is not one. So we have had Lasombra in the Camarilla for years, Lasombra antitribu, but when the right elders make the right deals, then Lasombra has a seat on the Inner Circle, Lasombra has a Justicar, the Lasombra is a Camarilla Clan. That seems straightforward to me.<br /> <br /> It actually seems a lot harder for a Clan to leave the Camarilla by that criteria. If a high ranking member of Clan Gangrel or Brujah are one the Inner Circle, why do they leave it and abandon that authority when they have been working to get it for centuries perhaps? If they do abdicate, why wouldn\u2019t another elder of that Clan step forward and say that they were the next in line? It seems like enough members of the Clan would have to leave such that the other Clan leaders stopped recognizing elders of the exiting Clan as representative of the Clan as a whole. When enough Brujah leave the Camarilla that when an elder Brujah steps up and says they are the Brujah Justicar, the Camarilla Inner Circle says no, you aren\u2019t, there is no Brujah Justicar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 06-01-2020, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T23:24:42-07:00","id":1393368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393363#post1393363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Taggie also tried the Conviction system. It just didn't work for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>If all you want is to be able to be monsters, the new system makes it easier (agree tenets that let you, ditch all touchstones, possibly via a wood chipper, go for it). If you want the Paths as alternate ways of looking at the world, and for them to be hard to follow, not so much, tenets as a system doesn't play well with world views that divergent amongst the characters, neither do convictions, you simply can't get down in the weeds enough, at least IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T23:32:17-07:00","id":1393370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393361#post1393361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your view of things is awfully simplistic and contradicted in numerous places in the lore going back to 2nd edition, which has been pointed out repeatedly, not to mention that you clearly haven\u2019t even read the treatment of the subject in Chicago by Night, which addresses all of these issues and explicitly contradicts your assertions here. The real question is why anyone should be baited into arguing with you when you won\u2019t even inform yourself about the subject, in fact have no interest in it, made up your mind before even beginning to investigate it, and are not really interested in anything anyone says in response to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chicago by Night alone is V5 material, how could I trust that when obviously the people who are doing V5 will try to justify the Lasombra defection in the first place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">at the end of the day the Sabbat and Camarilla were two sides of the same coin. It was all a scam on their Neonates anyway. The real fight was always for power and domain.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This couldn't be further from the truth. The Sabbat and the Camarilla are radically different from one another. The Sabbat alone is a faction that deliberately established Paths of thinking (Vampiric philosophy) to fully acknowledge and accept their inhumanity, clinging off the folly vistage of human thought they held before embrace. The Camarilla on the other end attempt to hold some semblance of human morality despite becoming in the condition they found themselves into. Even way from their prominent different beliefs, the Sabbat operate in a completely different way than how the Camarilla go on about. Sabbat has heavy catholic influences, while the Camarilla is secular. Sabbat often stick in elaborate packs, while Camarilla sometimes operate in cotieres- but unlike Sabbat groups, they don't do Vinculum. This isn't even to mention the various Rites the Sabbat has. The Camarilla and Sabbat aren't the same at all- their polar opposites, which made them interesting enemies of eachother in the Jyhad. The Anarchs are the ones who have more closeness to the Camarilla in comparison. Not to even mention if both factions find either in their own territory (when Sabbat still had territory that is) they literally KOS the offending party- apart from unique circumstances of parley (of which are very rare)<br /> <br /> This is why the Lasombra in bulk coming to the Camarilla doesn't make sense. <i>At all</i>. The most of them are just way to aligned with the Sabbat than with the Camarilla.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-04-2020, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T00:51:35-07:00","id":1393373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393330#post1393330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't this how Storytelling works? You want to tell a story and explain how things got there? Natural events don't happen in a fictional world. So you create a theme and talk about how they came about.</div> </div> </div> </div>You write books and you think all events need to happen in accorance to themes, and they can't just naturally happen according to logic and reason...? Well, that seems to be how V5 is doing things, and it's really a weakness. While I can (and have) rationalize some things like Camarilla exclusivity or house carna (I suspect these rationalizations were not what the writers had in mind) I really, really can't make sense of the Sabbat. Maybe there's some notion of magical realism but it still doesn't make sense. <hr /><br /> <br /> A big thing I don't like about the weakness of the lasombra is the dependence on ghouls. If it was the ventrue, who's whole thing was conntrolling people with two social disciplines, who organize themselves on boards and cultivate herds like no other clan, it'd make a little bit of sense. It'd be the perfect weakness of a bloodline with Dominate, Obfuscate, Presence. A Lasombra is, however, a Professional. A domineering loner who surrounds herself with tools*, which is why they have dominate, no presence, and potence instead of fortitude. Their Obtenebration drives people away. They're not supposed to be a clan that needs to talk to larry the ghoul to make a phonecall, they are the ones to make a phonecall. How could such a demeaning thing effect such a proud clan?<br /> <br /> <br /> *Clan stereotype, not a universal truth. Smart Lasombra are nice Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-01-2020, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T06:20:58-07:00","id":1393405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393361#post1393361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your view of things is awfully simplistic and contradicted in numerous places in the lore going back to 2nd edition, which has been pointed out repeatedly, not to mention that you clearly haven\u2019t even read the treatment of the subject in Chicago by Night, which addresses all of these issues and explicitly contradicts your assertions here. The real question is why anyone should be baited into arguing with you when you won\u2019t even inform yourself about the subject, in fact have no interest in it, made up your mind before even beginning to investigate it, and are not really interested in anything anyone says in response to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe their views are simplistic. I agree that I think Chicago by Night did a great job in explaining the issues, though, and that every single player should pick up a copy. It's not just one of Onyx Path's best books but it's one of the best books for V:TM period. I also think it becomes somewhat hard to argue the subject with posters as a lot of people attempt to discuss the issues of V5 without actually having read the material -- which means a lot of things have to be repeated and made.<br /> <br /> If you want to discuss Lasombra in V5, you should own CBN, IMHO.<br /> <br /> *is slipped $20 to advertise book by White Wolf*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393367#post1393367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that brings up an issue - what determines whether a Clan is in a Sect? Of course you can have members of any Clan in any Sect, but when is Brujah officially a Camarilla Clan and when is it not. I very much doubt it has anything to do with what percentage of the Clan population is in the Camarilla versus outside of it. A Clan with 6000 total vampires could still be recognized as a Camarilla Clan and have a Justicar and representation on the Inner Circle even if only 2000 of those vampires were in the Camarilla. That, it seems, is what determines Camarilla membership. Does the Clan have a Justicar, yes or no. Yes, it is a Camarilla Clan. No, it is not one. So we have had Lasombra in the Camarilla for years, Lasombra antitribu, but when the right elders make the right deals, then Lasombra has a seat on the Inner Circle, Lasombra has a Justicar, the Lasombra is a Camarilla Clan. That seems straightforward to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla is basically a Vampire United Nations and the Inner Council is its Security Council. A Justicar isn't really that important in the grand scheme of things because a Justicar just exists to enforce the will of the Inner Council. You could have a Daughter of Cacophony Justicar for the Camarilla and it wouldn't necessarily mean the DoC are any more powerful as a whole. The Inner Council is where the big deals happen.<br /> <br /> But I do think that the Camarilla's membership goes beyond even just having an Inner Council member because while the Ivory Tower has always maintained the polite fiction that it represents all vampires, the fact is that Independent vampires and Antitribu don't have the freedom of movement or protection of the Traditions that the main Seven clans do. Lodin kept the Followers of Set from ever settling in Chicago after all and plenty of Princes made it a point that any Ravnos who visited their cities were either chased out or actually destroyed. The Giovanni were outright forbidden to involve themselves in vampire politics in any way so you could never have a Giovanni Prince, Primogen, or other titled Elder.<br /> <br /> Being a Clan in the Camarilla as we see with the Assamites/Banu Haqim in Revised/V5 is a tacit acknowledgement that they are one of the pillars of the organization with position, voting rights, and the powert o back it up. If you've played MASS EFFECT then humankind is a member of the Citadel Races but it considers itself a bunch of second-class citizens unless it can get itself a seat at the table that other races have been waiting for for ages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It actually seems a lot harder for a Clan to leave the Camarilla by that criteria. If a high ranking member of Clan Gangrel or Brujah are one the Inner Circle, why do they leave it and abandon that authority when they have been working to get it for centuries perhaps? If they do abdicate, why wouldn\u2019t another elder of that Clan step forward and say that they were the next in line? It seems like enough members of the Clan would have to leave such that the other Clan leaders stopped recognizing elders of the exiting Clan as representative of the Clan as a whole. When enough Brujah leave the Camarilla that when an elder Brujah steps up and says they are the Brujah Justicar, the Camarilla Inner Circle says no, you aren\u2019t, there is no Brujah Justicar. </div> </div> </div>The Brujah Inner Council member was assassinated according to The Camarilla and the Ivory Tower neglected to select a new one.<br /> <br /> Page 120, The Camarilla, Karl Schrekt:<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The attack on the Camarilla Inner Circle some years ago was a blip, I believe, and though rumors hold of the Brujah losing their representative (I am shedding no tears since their betrayal) and one of the Nosferatu disappearing somewhere beyond the veil, I feel the city is entirely safe. Ten years without an incident is not bad for our kind, and anyway, if you hang around long enough you may be able to report back to me what the Clan of Death is doing in the city\u2019s bowels. </span></i><br /> <br /> It's in the Vienna entry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-01-2020, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:18:03-07:00","id":1393413,"title":"","content":"this discussion is kinda pointless,<br /> there's no flawless logic that can be applied to the VtM lore,<br /> the Lasombra joining the sabbat, their victories and losses, their betrayal and defection are all arbitrary,<br /> all of it can be both justified and argued against within the plot<br /> <br /> when the lasombra was made a sabbat clan, and when, later it was swapped for a camarilla one, it wasn't because of logic but a design choice<br /> <br /> the design choices pre-v5 favored the Sabbat,<br /> the way the lasombra, Tzimisce and other factions were fleshed out gave alot of depth to the sect,<br /> their history, their conflicts, their struggles etc<br /> <br /> the design choice in v5 destroys all of that depth for the sabbat, and gives it (well, part of it) to the camarilla<br /> <br /> they don't really dislike the sabbat, they just want the camarilla to have what made the sabbat good,<br /> <br /> and we can't fight it, because VtM doesn't sell well, and a sabbaty-Camarilla sells better than a sabbaty-sabbat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:47:46-07:00","id":1393424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393370#post1393370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chicago by Night alone is V5 material, how could I trust that when obviously the people who are doing V5 will try to justify the Lasombra defection in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well when discussing things like Lasombra in V5, it's probably a good idea to discuss the primary source of information about Lasombra in V5. If you don't want to include any element of V5 in your games, that's fine but you probably shouldn't show up in threads about Lasombra in V5. It's just a matter of making sure you are best prepared for discussing the subject, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Also, it's widely believed that CBN V5 is the best V5 book so far and fixes a lot of the problems of the setting while expanding on the original Chicago lore.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This couldn't be further from the truth. The Sabbat and the Camarilla are radically different from one another. The Sabbat alone is a faction that deliberately established Paths of thinking (Vampiric philosophy) to fully acknowledge and accept their inhumanity, clinging off the folly vistage of human thought they held before embrace. The Camarilla on the other end attempt to hold some semblance of human morality despite becoming in the condition they found themselves into. Even way from their prominent different beliefs, the Sabbat operate in a completely different way than how the Camarilla go on about. Sabbat has heavy catholic influences, while the Camarilla is secular. Sabbat often stick in elaborate packs, while Camarilla sometimes operate in cotieres- but unlike Camarilla groups, they don't do Vinculum. This isn't even to mention the various Rites the Sabbat has. The Camarilla and Sabbat aren't the same at all- their polar opposites, which made them interesting enemies of eachother in the Jyhad. The Anarchs are the ones who have more closeness to the Camarilla in comparison. Not to even mention if both factions find either in their own territory (when Sabbat still had territory that is) they literally KOS the offending party- apart from unique circumstances of parley (of which are very rare) </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I disagree 100%. The Sabbat and Camarilla are nothing more than the same scam by Elders on Neonates. The Camarilla is equally evil to the Sabbat, making the cities they inhabit some of the worst and nastiest places on Earth so nobody will care when people go missing as well as the police being hopelessly corrupt.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Camarilla claims to be about Humanity and the Sabbat about throwing away the shackles of it but both are lying. It's all about power and Domain for both of them. Neonates exist in both sects to be thrown into the jaws of Hunters, other vampires, or in needless conflicts so that the people above them can benefit.<br /> <br /> To quote Doctor No, &quot;East, West - just points of the compass, each as stupid as the other.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's no difference between a Archbishop and Prince at the end of the day. Same with a Baron.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is why the Lasombra in bulk coming to the Camarilla doesn't make sense. At all. The most of them are just way to aligned with the Sabbat than with the Camarilla. </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> I think the character of Sierra Van Burace was a pretty good &quot;show don't tell&quot; argument. She's a Lasombra who had potentially billions of dollars available to her and huge amounts of influence but couldn't touch it because the Sabbat kept trying to rope her into ritae and rituals versus increasing mortal influence. Lots of Lasombra are going to want to seize an opportunity when it presents itself.<br /> <br /> In this case, those who have power in the sect will stay with the sect while those who don't have power in the sect will seek greener pastures. Especially if the Sabbat is suffering due to the Second Inquisition, Gehenna Crusade, loss of Paths to the Beast, and their Antediluvian being alive like CBN5E says.<br /> But that's my read of the Lasombra, yours could be different at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-01-2020, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:56:35-07:00","id":1393427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393373#post1393373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You write books and you think all events need to happen in accorance to themes, and they can't just naturally happen according to logic and reason...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I think you basically are just writing yourself into a corner here.<br /> <br /> 1. I am God of my universe so every event that happens in my books happens according to my whims and decisions.<br /> <br /> 2. The two most important things that will happen as established by previous games will be: <b>The Rise of the Surveillance State </b>and <b>The Rise of the Antediluvians.</b><br /> <br /> So, therefore, according to your logic, updating the V:TM setting to 2020 will result in the Second Inquistion and the Gehenna Wars. You've just established that following the natural course of events in previous games and RL will result in the two things you hate most.<br /> <br /> How do you reconcile that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, that seems to be how V5 is doing things, and it's really a weakness. While I can (and have) rationalize some things like Camarilla exclusivity or house carna (I suspect these rationalizations were not what the writers had in mind) I really, really can't make sense of the Sabbat. Maybe there's some notion of magical realism but it still doesn't make sense. <hr /> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat was always going to have to change as the depiction in canon is not one that can continue with an age of cellphones and globalized intelligence services.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A big thing I don't like about the weakness of the lasombra is the dependence on ghouls. If it was the ventrue, who's whole thing was conntrolling people with two social disciplines, who organize themselves on boards and cultivate herds like no other clan, it'd make a little bit of sense. It'd be the perfect weakness of a bloodline with Dominate, Obfuscate, Presence. A Lasombra is, however, a Professional. A domineering loner who surrounds herself with tools*, which is why they have dominate, no presence, and potence instead of fortitude. Their Obtenebration drives people away. They're not supposed to be a clan that needs to talk to larry the ghoul to make a phonecall, they are the ones to make a phonecall. How could such a demeaning thing effect such a proud clan?<br /> <br /> *Clan stereotype, not a universal truth. Smart Lasombra are nice Lasombra. </div> </div> </div>I agree, I think the tech-bane element of the Lasombra doesn't make sense with them and ghouls don't work for the majority of Packs. For those Lasombra who live in a communal haven, where would the ghouls even exist? There's some Paths that would have their brethren murdering them just because.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393413#post1393413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this discussion is kinda pointless,<br /> there's no flawless logic that can be applied to the VtM lore,<br /> the Lasombra joining the sabbat, their victories and losses, their betrayal and defection are all arbitrary,<br /> all of it can be both justified and argued against within the plot</div> </div> </div> </div>I think everyone's version of the Lasombra, Sabbat, and Camarilla depend greatly on their Storytellers and own interpretation of lore. Discussing that is what makes these forums, fun. While the books provide canon answers, there's also <b>Death of the Author</b> and the fact that you might think your version is better.<br /> <br /> Which is fine and fun. This is, at the end of the day, just a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> when the lasombra was made a sabbat clan, and when, later it was swapped for a camarilla one, it wasn't because of logic but a design choice </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think it depends where you define logic. Some versions of the Lasombra are so anti-Camarilla they make no sense ever defecting while others are people you have to wonder about ever not being Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the design choices pre-v5 favored the Sabbat,<br /> the way the lasombra, Tzimisce and other factions were fleshed out gave alot of depth to the sect,<br /> their history, their conflicts, their struggles etc<br /> <br /> the design choice in v5 destroys all of that depth for the sabbat, and gives it (well, part of it) to the camarilla<br /> <br /> they don't really dislike the sabbat, they just want the camarilla to have what made the sabbat good,<br /> <br /> and we can't fight it, because VtM doesn't sell well, and a sabbaty-Camarilla sells better than a sabbaty-sabbat </div> </div> </div>I think there's some merit to the idea that the Sabbat has been spread around a lot. The Blood Cults for instance have brought a lot of Cainite mysticism and inhumanity to all parts of the setting versus just locked up in one sect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-01-2020, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:41:38-07:00","id":1393438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393427#post1393427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's some merit to the idea that the Sabbat has been spread around a lot. The Blood Cults for instance have brought a lot of Cainite mysticism and inhumanity to all parts of the setting versus just locked up in one sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly doubt it,<br /> the previous morality system (and road system for dark ages) allowed for more diversity in blood cults,<br /> <br /> the cults weren't locked up in one sect (sabbat, setites in their different forms, assamite, nahualli etc)<br /> <br /> the Camarilla traditionally had blood cults, but I'm sure v5 is gonna pretend they invented that<br /> sabbat was just a large ramassis of gehenna cults and other death cults<br /> <br /> even if the sabbat had monopoly on cults, they had enough territory to offer much variety of them,<br /> <br /> if v5 wants diversity, they'll have to modify the morality system","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-01-2020, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:47:46-07:00","id":1393441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393438#post1393438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I highly doubt it,<br /> the previous morality system (and road system for dark ages) allowed for more diversity in blood cults,<br /> <br /> the cults weren't locked up in one sect (sabbat, setites in their different forms, assamite, nahualli etc)<br /> <br /> the Camarilla traditionally had blood cults, but I'm sure v5 is gonna pretend they invented that<br /> sabbat was just a large ramassis of gehenna cult (and other death cults)<br /> <br /> even if the sabbat had monopoly on cults, they had enough territory to offer much variety of them,<br /> <br /> if v5 wants diversity, they'll have to modify the morality system</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of quoting The Last Jedi:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/736x/04/f4/cd/04f4cda650c7fe693905a0ff83aef566.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> 1. I disagree because an infinite number of Conviction and Tenet possibilities are listed in Blood Cults. The Cult of Mithras, Church of Set, and so on list dozens of examples of such.<br /> <br /> 2. The Cults are not locked up in sects in V5. You can be an Anarch Church of Mithras follower, a Camarilla one, an independent one, or just a member of said sect.<br /> <br /> 3. The Camarilla previously punished followers of Gehenna Cults with death. Ayesha Jocastian was put on the RED LIST for publishing copies of the Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> 4. The Sabbat only allowed certain kinds of cults to thrive as they exterminated the Path of Harmony because they didn't agree with their doctrine of Faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T09:01:47-07:00","id":1393444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393441#post1393441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I disagree because an infinite number of Conviction and Tenet possibilities are listed in Blood Cults. The Cult of Mithras, Church of Set, and so on list dozens of examples of such.</div> </div> </div> </div>as always, backer privilege saving your ass, huh?<br /> <br /> considering disclosing info to non backers is against the rules, I'll just ignore that until the book is published<br /> or you could <i>cough</i>break<i>cough</i>the rules<i>cough</i> for me<br /> <br /> the current morality rules don't allow for much diversity in setting,<br /> and if it does, it still doesn't allow much diversity in play<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. The Cults are not locked up in sects in V5. You can be an Anarch Church of Mithras follower, a Camarilla one, an independent one, or just a member of said sect. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say they were locked in v5, you're the one who said they were locked pre-v5,<br /> also, ever read sins of the blood?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. The Sabbat only allowed certain kinds of cults to thrive as they exterminated the Path of Harmony because they didn't agree with their doctrine of Faith. </div> </div> </div>last I heard, they lived on as autarkis *shrug*, and sabbat replaced them with their own version<br /> <br /> if anything, it got more diverse, not less","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-01-2020, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T09:09:01-07:00","id":1393449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393444#post1393444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> as always, backer privilege saving your ass, huh?<br /> <br /> considering disclosing info to non backers is against the rules, I'll just ignore that until the book is published<br /> or you could <i>cough</i>break<i>cough</i>the rules<i>cough</i> for me</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of points.<br /> <br /> 1. Onyx Path is actually pretty awesome about allowing the material of the Kickstarters to be discussed. That's why they let me do a WIR of Chicago by Night 5th Edition before its release. Solid bunch of people.<br /> <br /> 2. You can actually Pre-Order CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS and get all the free previews that actual Backers did. It's called Backer Kit and I strongly recommend it for people who missed out on the initial Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://cults-of-the-blood-gods.backerkit.com/hosted_preorders\" target=\"_blank\">https://cults-of-the-blood-gods.back...sted_preorders</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T09:56:28-07:00","id":1393460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393441#post1393441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the risk of quoting The Last Jedi:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/736x/04/f4/cd/04f4cda650c7fe693905a0ff83aef566.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> 1. I disagree because an infinite number of Conviction and Tenet possibilities are listed in Blood Cults. The Cult of Mithras, Church of Set, and so on list dozens of examples of such.<br /> <br /> 2. The Cults are not locked up in sects in V5. You can be an Anarch Church of Mithras follower, a Camarilla one, an independent one, or just a member of said sect.<br /> <br /> 3. The Camarilla previously punished followers of Gehenna Cults with death. Ayesha Jocastian was put on the RED LIST for publishing copies of the Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> 4. The Sabbat only allowed certain kinds of cults to thrive as they exterminated the Path of Harmony because they didn't agree with their doctrine of Faith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1.) From your descriptions so far, they sound far more shallow and less interesting than even the worst paths, but that is always going to be a YMMV, and they are also locked behind the horrible lore sheet points tax.<br /> <br /> 2) Erm they never where locked, so why would they be now? Less popular sure, but their were Cam vampires on paths and the Cult of Mithras was pretty much Cam exclusive, as well as Setites having associates damn near every where, <br /> <br /> 3) True.<br /> <br /> 4) Also true.<br /> <br /> As an aside: the Paths falling to the Beast makes zero sense, if anything the flat and hollow lie of humanity should have, as it does nothing to actually address being a vampire, and is completely delusional. ( And also not any fun to roleplay with IMHO, haven't enjoyed a humanity based vampire...ever pretty much, I was lucky I started playing at the start of second Ed so the paths could save the setting for me, the current system is somehow even less fun, which takes some doing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-01-2020, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T10:04:36-07:00","id":1393461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393441#post1393441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/736x/04/f4/cd/04f4cda650c7fe693905a0ff83aef566.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/cor