 where -the logical thing- happens. Having things perfectly line up in a convenient plot that goes where you want it to go is what you want to do with movies, but isn't that important for long stories. Even though it does have some -chosen one- stuff in it and a lot of it's unduly pessimistic, a lot of what I love about <i>A song of ice and fire</i> is that the <i>perfectly reasonable</i> thing happens most of the time. (The show is completely different)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, therefore, according to your logic, updating the V:TM setting to 2020 will result in the Second Inquistion and the Gehenna Wars. You've just established that following the natural course of events in previous games and RL will result in the two things you hate most.<br /> <br /> How do you reconcile that?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Sabbat was always going to have to change as the depiction in canon is not one that can continue with an age of cellphones and globalized intelligence services.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>You know my stance; I don't believe that the masquerade will be endangered by an age of cell cameras. Not with movie magic what it is now. I've wrote threads on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there's some merit to the idea that the Sabbat has been spread around a lot. The Blood Cults for instance have brought a lot of Cainite mysticism and inhumanity to all parts of the setting versus just locked up in one sect. </div> </div> </div>I really liked the camarilla's secret cults. Having worship out in the open is lame and should feel lame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T10:08:20-07:00","id":1393462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393015#post1393015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are they removing unique clan disciplines, for what reason exactly? I've already stated this before in another thread way back, but who know's what their going to do to the Tzimisce since they've adopted this policy. You definitely know they don't like Vicissitude with all the whack-a-moles they've done with other said unique disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't see anyone answer you, but it's removal of redundancy. Serpentis was literally two powers that fit Protean, two powers that fit Presence, and a power 'because egyptians'. Oblivion is the outlier, but as has been discussed, there were some tie mentions about the Abyss being tied to Oblivion in Revised era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T10:10:39-07:00","id":1393463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393449#post1393449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. You can actually Pre-Order CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS and get all the free previews that actual Backers did. It's called Backer Kit and I strongly recommend it for people who missed out on the initial Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://cults-of-the-blood-gods.backerkit.com/hosted_preorders\" target=\"_blank\">https://cults-of-the-blood-gods.back...sted_preorders</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The preorder doesn't give access to the backer manuscript, after the first part was closed. If you back it via backerkit, you'll get the PDF when it actually drops, but not the backer manuscript.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T10:45:34-07:00","id":1393467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393463#post1393463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The preorder doesn't give access to the backer manuscript, after the first part was closed. If you back it via backerkit, you'll get the PDF when it actually drops, but not the backer manuscript.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does give you access to the Updates section that allow you to download the manuscript sections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T11:05:41-07:00","id":1393470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393460#post1393460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) From your descriptions so far, they sound far more shallow and less interesting than even the worst paths, but that is always going to be a YMMV, and they are also locked behind the horrible lore sheet points tax.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of points.<br /> <br /> 1. I really think you'd enjoy the Blood Cults book and they are very much what you like about the Sabbat with their focus on rejecting humanity and having elaborate moral as well as theological frameworks.<br /> <br /> 2. Loresheets actually play no role whatsoever in them. That was a popular fanon way to handle Paths that was not adopted by the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Erm they never where locked, so why would they be now? Less popular sure, but their were Cam vampires on paths and the Cult of Mithras was pretty much Cam exclusive, as well as Setites having associates damn near every where. </div> </div> </div>Officially, Roads were persecuted and destroyed by the Cam, which I always felt was ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an aside: the Paths falling to the Beast makes zero sense, if anything the flat and hollow lie of humanity should have, as it does nothing to actually address being a vampire, and is completely delusional. ( And also not any fun to roleplay with IMHO, haven't enjoyed a humanity based vampire...ever pretty much, I was lucky I started playing at the start of second Ed so the paths could save the setting for me, the current system is somehow even less fun, which takes some doing) </div> </div> </div>1. The Sabbat has long maintained that Humanity was an impossible way to hold against the Beast indefinitely and that it was a doomed effort that would eventually result in one succumbing. This has always been Sabbat propaganda because most Elders plateau around Humanity 4 or Humanity 3 at least to the point that ancients like Helena are fine on it.<br /> <br /> 2. <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>CHAINING THE BEAST</b></span> despite being a very pro-Path book contained the following notes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 15</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus a path follower has to try a lot harder to stay on her course than a Humanity practicioner does to maintain night to night existence. For us humans, it takes a tremendous an effort to completely collapse our Humanity as it does to exalt it. For vampires, collapsing any spiritual construct into the abyss of the Beast is frighteningly easy.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 15</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cainites belonging to a path must adopt every tenet, every teaching with every fiber of their undead being. To doubt, to stumble, to err is to potentially dislodge a gear that brings the whole path-machine crashing down.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 15, 16</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not to say all Sabbat practice Paths of Enlightenment. The majority still follow Humanity, albeit at low levels. It is the Sabbat, though, that exalts Paths of Enlightenment and their practitioners. Ironically, this is the act that causes many neonate members to lose themselves to the Beast, attempting to adhere to a path before they're ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paths have never been easy and have always been something only the strongest willed Cainites could adhere to because they're fundamentally artificial rather than natural to the vampire state or human.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-01-2020, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T11:16:55-07:00","id":1393474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Honestly, I disagree 100%. The Sabbat and Camarilla are nothing more than the same scam by Elders on Neonates. The Camarilla is equally evil to the Sabbat, making the cities they inhabit some of the worst and nastiest places on Earth so nobody will care when people go missing as well as the police being hopelessly corrupt.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Yes, the Camarilla claims to be about Humanity and the Sabbat about throwing away the shackles of it but both are lying. It's all about power and Domain for both of them. Neonates exist in both sects to be thrown into the jaws of Hunters, other vampires, or in needless conflicts so that the people above them can benefit.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">To quote Doctor No, &quot;East, West - just points of the compass, each as stupid as the other.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">There's no difference between a Archbishop and Prince at the end of the day. Same with a Baron.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Wut? The Sabbat and the Camarilla have CLEAR differences in ideology, supernatural in make specifically, that set them in the constant Jyhads they have against one another. Domain and Territory are parcels, but they fight for much more than that. Why would they be the same at all? Have you even read the specific Paths Sabbat members dedicate themselves too? How much it takes to even get there? Their serious, along with the Camarilla who wants to enforce the masquerade at all costs- something they believe the Sabbat are near to break at any moment. Not everything is about the whole &quot;Neonates vs Elder&quot; thing you like to prop up, because if that was the case it'll just get old fast from a meta perspective. Neonates eventually become the new Elders, what doesn't change is the new beliefs they are shaped by when they are embraced and inducted into their Sect. </span><br /> <br /> Most Elders are centuries old crafting up plans of Jyhad warfare to finally strike down the opposite sect- why would they make up lies for the underlying convictions it for some nascent Neonates in the first place? That's just dumb. The Camarilla and the Sabbat were perfect enemies for one another because of their opposite takes of Vampirism. One wants an immortal status quo, while the others want to shrug off status quo and commit to their Vampirism fully. &quot;Power and Domain&quot; are both things that come in and go, the ideology of both Sects stay within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T11:19:19-07:00","id":1393475,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Anecdotal Story: Is it fun playing a Sabbat who &quot;gets it&quot; versus the Sabbat who &quot;don't&quot;?</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Alternate Title: &quot;Stop being stereotypical, Shovelhead!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> This is going to be anecodtal but one of my all-time favorite characters to roleplay was Tet-Anubis, a Serpent of Light who was a follower of the Path of Caine. Well before V5 came out, we had the character running through the Transylvania Chronicles and dealing with the fact that he was Embraced as a Follower of Set but defected when he discovered the existence of the Antediluvians as well as &quot;proof&quot; of Caine.<br /> <br /> One of the things that we roleplayed out was the idea that Tet-Anubis joined the First Anarch Revolt because he was disgusted with the control of the Elders and their casual corruption. He wanted to help create a higher morality for Kindred and transcend the bonds of Cainite existence to become a superior godlike being, moral but wholly alien to humanity.<br /> <br /> One of the things I liked was the Storyteller said that Tet-Anubis was surrounded by Sabbat in the Modern Day who couldn't really walk-the-walk. They were Bestial, stupid, arrogant, and about as far from intelligent philosopher vampires as they were going to find. He compared it to the Brujah Clan after Carthage and how it had degenerated from the Learned Clan to being the Rabble.<br /> <br /> I really enjoyed that because it was a theme that was explored in MONTREAL BY NIGHT and other Sabbat supplements where there's the &quot;real&quot; Sabbat who are alien, arcane, eldritch, and inhuman geniuses ala Dracula or even Deacon Frost while there's the other who are just a bunch of Near Dark mooks. I feel like that's a great thing they've sort of canonized.<br /> <br /> Not just in V5 either as we have other Sabbat founders like Giangaleazzo and Vasantasena coming to the conclusion in Revised and V20 that the sabbat are a failed experiment. For me, it was a great roleplaying opportunity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are the Sabbat worth saving? How do you go about reforming it? Is it possible to reform it or should you just start a new sect/join another?&quot;<br /> <br /> For Tet-Anubis, he ended up joining the True Hand who I roleplayed as the &quot;Real&quot; Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T11:20:21-07:00","id":1393476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393474#post1393474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/FONT]<br /> <br /> [FONT=Helvetica]Wut? The Sabbat and the Camarilla have CLEAR differences in ideology, supernatural in make specifically, that set them in the constant Jyhads they have against one another. Domain and Territory are parcels, but they fight for much more than that. Why would they be the same at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>All Elders have only one ideology: themselves.<br /> <br /> :ZING:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you even read the specific Paths Sabbat members dedicate themselves too? How much it takes to even get there? </div> </div> </div>Yes, though only a handful of Elders will actually devote themselves seriously enough to their Paths to have high rankings in them. In the end, most will focus on power and prestige like most Elders.<br /> <br /> Vykos is the exception not the rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their serious, along with the Camarilla who wants to enforce the masquerade at all costs- something they believe the Sabbat are near to break at any moment. </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat keep the Masquerade just as vigorously as the Camarilla. They just claim they won't after Gehenna.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not everything is about the whole &quot;Neonates vs Elder&quot; thing you like to prop up, because if that was the case it'll just get old fast from a meta perspective. Neonates eventually become the new Elders, what doesn't change is the new beliefs they are shaped by when they are embraced and inducted into their Sect. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the Jyhad eventually widdles down the idealism of most Elders and even most Ancilla so they become the scheming power-hungry scumbags that run the sect. This was discussed a lot in ELYSIUM and THE ANARCHS UNBOUND. We also have many examples of it like with Tyler who went from the founder of the Anarchs to a Brujah sellout.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Elders are centuries old crafting up plans of Jyhad warfare to finally strike down the opposite sect- why would they make up lies for the underlying convictions it for some nascent Neonates in the first place? That's just dumb. The Camarilla and the Sabbat were perfect enemies for one another because of their opposite takes of Vampirism. One wants an immortal status quo, while the others want to shrug off status quo and commit to their Vampirism fully. &quot;Power and Domain&quot; are both things that come in and go, the ideology of both Sects stay within. </div> </div> </div>In the end, the fundamental conflict between the Sabbat is who has territory and feeding and money and power versus those who don't.<br /> <br /> But I emphasize Gothic PUNK.<br /> <br /> One is Aztechnology, one is AresCorp. They're both megacorporations at the end of the day.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Take note this is not me saying you're WRONG but this is my INTERPRETATION of what the books have presented and how I run it at my table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-01-2020, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T12:35:00-07:00","id":1393486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393470#post1393470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A couple of points.<br /> <br /> 1. I really think you'd enjoy the Blood Cults book and they are very much what you like about the Sabbat with their focus on rejecting humanity and having elaborate moral as well as theological frameworks.<br /> <br /> 2. Loresheets actually play no role whatsoever in them. That was a popular fanon way to handle Paths that was not adopted by the books.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Officially, Roads were persecuted and destroyed by the Cam, which I always felt was ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1. The Sabbat has long maintained that Humanity was an impossible way to hold against the Beast indefinitely and that it was a doomed effort that would eventually result in one succumbing. This has always been Sabbat propaganda because most Elders plateau around Humanity 4 or Humanity 3 at least to the point that ancients like Helena are fine on it.<br /> <br /> 2. <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>CHAINING THE BEAST</b></span> despite being a very pro-Path book contained the following notes:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Paths have never been easy and have always been something only the strongest willed Cainites could adhere to because they're fundamentally artificial rather than natural to the vampire state or human.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also thought I would like CbN, it is safe to say I do not, in fact I find the Lasombra section damn close to insulting. But then as I have previously stated I thought that Sabbat on Humanity was a mistake when it first happened, in Revised.<br /> <br /> <br /> If Cults get rid of Touch Stones and tenets in favour of a proper morality system, not the perverted<br /> , Sadistic disgusting ,tamagotchi Sim we have now, and don't involve Loresheets, they may help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-01-2020, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T12:41:03-07:00","id":1393489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393486#post1393486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also thought I would like CbN, it is safe to say I do not, in fact I find the Lasombra section damn close to insulting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to hear your thoughts on the Lasombra section of CBN. It's great to have passionate criticism informed on the subject matter of V5's progress with Lasombra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But then as I have previously stated I thought that Sabbat on Humanity was a mistake when it first happened, in Revised. </div> </div> </div>Getting people to change their entire worldview and abide by new practices is going to be a hard one. The Sabbat aren't going to be able to convert everyone who falls in their ranks.<br /> <br /> You're going to have your &quot;Christians in name only&quot; who do what they want and praise Caine, saying they're on a Path without actually acting like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T13:04:44-07:00","id":1393496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393489#post1393489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)I'd love to hear your thoughts on the Lasombra section of CBN. It's great to have passionate criticism informed on the subject matter of V5's progress with Lasombra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2)Getting people to change their entire worldview and abide by new practices is going to be a hard one. The Sabbat aren't going to be able to convert everyone who falls in their ranks.<br /> <br /> You're going to have your &quot;Christians in name only&quot; who do what they want and praise Caine, saying they're on a Path without actually acting like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Part one: they have taken what up to that point had been a clan that while it was cynical, devious and power hungry, had also, since Dark Ages, actually had a really strong current of Faith, and thrown that faith away, just discarded all that plot, all that story, to give us what feels like 'exotic and slightly edgy Ventrue', Path of Night: gone, not a thing, (and since that path is used in fanon to explain why the Lasombra bailed, that causes problems), the utter contempt for humans, that they have had since DA, gone, human touchstones forced on them, as diosgusting as that concept is, the reverence they paid to the trappings of faith, all gone (iirc, it was stated that the use of Catholic titles was genuine respect for that organisation, not mockery) basically the personality is gone, the flavour is all thrown away to make them fit as a new Cam Clan. it just feels off, fundamentally so. <br /> <br /> Part Two: Oblivion as a discipline, having it merged with necromancy, and being a direct threat of Stains in a way no other disciplines are, is a frankly bizarre decision, but a lesser problem, linking it to the underworld is the larger one, but again lesser than the issues I listed in part one. <br /> <br /> 2) Oh I understand why, the 'shovel of enlightenment' also caused problems, I just feel that it was cleaner to have 'True Sabbat' all be on paths, just as all Cam were on Humanity, it provided a contrast, allowed the two to have stronger identities, and made a lot more sense, as a piece of world building. I prefer the DA Road approach, everyone is on a Path/Road, it provides better stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T13:17:14-07:00","id":1393500,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a>! I appreciate you taking time to give us your review.<br /> <br /> 1:] I'm very confused by this description as I felt like the Lasombra Clan write-up in CBN5E <b>*OVER-emphasized*</b> the role of faith. The Lasombra haven't been involved in mortal churches and religions for 600 years since they were driven out by the Inquisition but the book suggests that a major reason the Camarilla would want the Lasombra was their heavy involvement in churches and how that could be used against the Second Inquisition. I'm not sure where you got the idea the Lasombra are being forced to have Touchstones either since Talley is the only character in the book who doesn't have any. Proof the Sabbat don't bother with them.<br /> <br /> 2:] I felt it was there to help emphasize the Lasombra are evil and corrupt in a way that is innately inhuman rather than clinging to Humanity. I'm not really sold on it, though, because I don't think vampire should ever have a &quot;One Ring&quot; or &quot;Dark Side of the Force&quot; effect. You should lose Humanity because you violate the tenets you believe in, not because of evil magic.<br /> <br /> 3:] Honestly, I feel like the Camarilla being champions of Humanity was always stupid and I wish in Revised they'd had Roads and Paths be a thing more Elders are on. The Camarilla is corrupt, vicious, and inhuman in ways that only Sabbat Elders could hope to match. I can't imagine them caring about Humanity and keeping vampires on it unless it's part of some larger plan to cripple the Neonates and keep them weak. Which is possible but not the way they're presnted. If I'd rebooted the Camarilla I'd make Roads and Gehenna Cults go hand in hand.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's LAUGHABLE that the Camarilla would give a shit about humanity. They're the boot on humanity's face and the reason the world sucks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393486#post1393486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Cults get rid of Touch Stones and tenets in favour of a proper morality system, not the perverted sadistic disgusting ,tamagotchi Sim we have now, and don't involve Loresheets, they may help.</div> </div> </div> </div>FYI, I also want to comment on the fact that this is just straight up wrong. Touchstones CAN be abusive but they don't have to be. They can be True Love or the one good thing in your vampire's life. You have a serious issue with abusive relationships in gaming and good for you but that's not something that I think the game is advocating for. Fans just point out that it can be a horror story that players may want to involve themselves in, perhaps if they want to take down the Jacob Schumpeter equivalent and his abused prisoners.<br /> <br /> (Yay for Matthew Dawkins taking him out)<br /> <br /> Also, they don't have any involvement with Loresheets so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-01-2020, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T13:29:30-07:00","id":1393503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393500#post1393500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a>! I appreciate you taking time to give us your review.<br /> <br /> 1:] I'm very confused by this description as I felt like the Lasombra Clan write-up in CBN5E <b>*OVER-emphasized*</b> the role of faith. The Lasombra haven't been involved in mortal churches and religions for 600 years since they were driven out by the Inquisition but the book suggests that a major reason the Camarilla would want the Lasombra was their heavy involvement in churches and how that could be used against the Second Inquisition. I'm not sure where you got the idea the Lasombra are being forced to have Touchstones either since Talley is the only character in the book who doesn't have any. Proof the Sabbat don't bother with them.<br /> <br /> 2:] I felt it was there to help emphasize the Lasombra are evil and corrupt in a way that is innately inhuman rather than clinging to Humanity. I'm not really sold on it, though, because I don't think vampire should ever have a &quot;One Ring&quot; or &quot;Dark Side of the Force&quot; effect. You should lose Humanity because you violate the tenets you believe in, not because of evil magic.<br /> <br /> 3:] Honestly, I feel like the Camarilla being champions of Humanity was always stupid and I wish in Revised they'd had Roads and Paths be a thing more Elders are on. The Camarilla is corrupt, vicious, and inhuman in ways that only Sabbat Elders could hope to match. I can't imagine them caring about Humanity and keeping vampires on it unless it's part of some larger plan to cripple the Neonates and keep them weak. Which is possible but not the way they're presnted. If I'd rebooted the Camarilla I'd make Roads and Gehenna Cults go hand in hand.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's LAUGHABLE that the Camarilla would give a shit about humanity. They're the boot on humanity's face and the reason the world sucks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> FYI, I also want to comment on the fact that this is just straight up wrong. Touchstones CAN be abusive but they don't have to be. They can be True Love or the one good thing in your vampire's life. You have a serious issue with abusive relationships in gaming and good for you but that's not something that I think the game is advocating for. Fans just point out that it can be a horror story that players may want to involve themselves in, perhaps if they want to take down the Jacob Schumpeter equivalent and his abused prisoners.<br /> <br /> (Yay for Matthew Dawkins taking him out)<br /> <br /> Also, they don't have any involvement with Loresheets so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) That's the difference between having Faith (which they do, of a weird cainite kind,) and having influence over the mortal faiths (Which I agree is odd). All the Lasombra except Talley have them...which shows that the Sabbat actually do have them, and Talley is the exception.<br /> <br /> 2) It doesn't work for that without an alternative morality system.<br /> <br /> 3) Cam as nakedly, wickedly human was what made them such effective satire, humans are corrupt and vicious, conspiratorial and greedy, embracing them just makes that more obvious. The Sabbat where the answer to what happens when they stop pretending to be humans and explore what it means to be vampires. That contrast really worked for me, neither side was good, neither side was nice, but the seperation was profound, in a way that it wasn't in later editions<br /> <br /> All Vampire to Touchstone relationships are by their nature abusive, you are explicitly placing said person at risk, both of your own beast, and of other vampires, you also cannot allow them to change, cannot allow them to grow, because doing so 'damages' them, which risks your humanity, if a vampire really cares about a human, they sever all contact and never try to find out about them again, every other outcome is either intentionally abusive, or directly placing them in extreme danger, and in both cases utterly unforgivable and reprehensible. Especially as the Core rules tell STs to attack and abuse touchstones for drama, domestic violence and abuse is a core mechanic of the game, which you cannot nope out of. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-01-2020, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T13:43:37-07:00","id":1393504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393500#post1393500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it's LAUGHABLE that the Camarilla would give a shit about humanity. They're the boot on humanity's face and the reason the world sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>the Cam didn't care about humanity (well the Torries and Brujah did, but that's not the reason why they stuck with humanity as a path)<br /> <br /> the Camarilla was the masquerade enforcer, and they banned other paths to better regulate the masquerade,<br /> humanity also prevented/reduced conflict,<br /> vampires on humanity are less likely to start brawls,<br /> compare that to sabbat leaders who go on frenzy every time their hear something they don't like, forcing youngsters to communicate with their leaders through ghouls<br /> <br /> the sabbat had the vinculum to prevent the different paths to tear each other apart,<br /> and the elders were willing to clean up the masquerade<br /> <br /> that said, paths were still followed in the camarilla, all it required was a permission from the prince, and the willingness to lose social points and be tagged as a threat to the elders<br /> (a camarilla guy on a path of caine who is obsessed with diablerie isn't something most elders would be comfortable with)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T13:55:48-07:00","id":1393507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393503#post1393503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) That's the difference between having Faith (which they do, of a weird cainite kind,) and having influence over the mortal faiths (Which I agree is odd). All the Lasombra except Talley have them...which shows that the Sabbat actually do have them, and Talley is the exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another Touchstone-less Lasombra in the Chicago Folios. Malenkov's Touchstone is also his ghoul, which I think barely counts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All Vampire to Touchstone relationships are by their nature abusive, you are explicitly placing said person at risk, both of your own beast, and of other vampires, you also cannot allow them to change, cannot allow them to grow, because doing so 'damages' them, which risks your humanity, if a vampire really cares about a human, they sever all contact and never try to find out about them again, every other outcome is either intentionally abusive, or directly placing them in extreme danger, and in both cases utterly unforgivable and reprehensible. Especially as the Core rules tell STs to attack and abuse touchstones for drama, domestic violence and abuse is a core mechanic of the game, which you cannot nope out of. </div> </div> </div>Bluntly, this makes a lot of assumptions about how Touchstones works that aren't true.<br /> <br /> <b>1. All Vampire to Touchstone relationships are by their nature abusive,</b><br /> <br /> You could just pay for their college and make sure that they are protected against supernatural predators like an undead guardian angel.<br /> <br /> <b>2. you are explicitly placing said person at risk, both of your own beast, and of other vampires, </b><br /> <br /> They might be at least risk depending on how dangerous their life is. A vampire's presence in their life might keep them safer and humans are vulnerbale to the undead anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>3. you also cannot allow them to change, cannot allow them to grow, because doing so 'damages' them, which risks your humanity, </b><br /> <br /> Depending on your Conviction, your Touchstone may be perfectly fine living out their lives.<br /> <br /> <b>4. if a vampire really cares about a human, they sever all contact and never try to find out about them again, every other outcome is either intentionally abusive, or directly placing them in extreme danger, and in both cases utterly unforgivable and reprehensible. </b><br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is very dangerous. Having someone who can protect you from other vampires, Pentex, crime, capitalism, or more may be important. Severing all contact also means that they're vulnerable in ways that a Dark Protector might be useful against.<br /> <br /> Also, while ghouldom IS horrible and degrading, it is also something many humans might choose for themselves if they were terminally ill or in otherwise need of vampire blood to survive.<br /> <br /> Plus, not everyone's vampire game is THAT DARK. Some people might actually want to do a Beauty and the Beast love story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T14:10:09-07:00","id":1393514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393507#post1393507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's another Touchstone-less Lasombra in the Chicago Folios. Malenkov's Touchstone is also his ghoul, which I think barely counts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bluntly, this makes a lot of assumptions about how Touchstones works that aren't true.<br /> <br /> 1)<b>1. All Vampire to Touchstone relationships are by their nature abusive,</b><br /> <br /> You could just pay for their college and make sure that they are protected against supernatural predators like an undead guardian angel.<br /> <br /> 2)<b>2. you are explicitly placing said person at risk, both of your own beast, and of other vampires, </b><br /> <br /> They might be at least risk depending on how dangerous their life is. A vampire's presence in their life might keep them safer and humans are vulnerbale to the undead anyway.<br /> <br /> 3)<b>3. you also cannot allow them to change, cannot allow them to grow, because doing so 'damages' them, which risks your humanity, </b><br /> <br /> Depending on your Conviction, your Touchstone may be perfectly fine living out their lives.<br /> <br /> 4)<b>4. if a vampire really cares about a human, they sever all contact and never try to find out about them again, every other outcome is either intentionally abusive, or directly placing them in extreme danger, and in both cases utterly unforgivable and reprehensible. </b><br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is very dangerous. Having someone who can protect you from other vampires, Pentex, crime, capitalism, or more may be important. Severing all contact also means that they're vulnerable in ways that a Dark Protector might be useful against.<br /> <br /> 5)Also, while ghouldom IS horrible and degrading, it is also something many humans might choose for themselves if they were terminally ill or in otherwise need of vampire blood to survive.<br /> <br /> Plus, not everyone's vampire game is THAT DARK. Some people might actually want to do a Beauty and the Beast love story.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Still runs into the core rule that Touchstones should be attacked for drama.<br /> <br /> 2) Again, STs are, in the CRB encouraged to attack touchstones, and it is Vampire tactics 101 to strike at tounchstones to provoke degradation<br /> <br /> 3) have to agree to disagree on that one<br /> <br /> 4) Severing all contact takes them off the board of the Jyhad, which is more dangerous than being a random human.<br /> <br /> 5) Ghouldom is separate from Touchstones, you aren't forced to take ghouls, you are forced to take touchstones, their is no way in core to not have them (and not having them makes you degenerate faster)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-01-2020, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T14:44:22-07:00","id":1393520,"title":"","content":"So.... uh... We never got round to explaining how so many lasombra could throw off the Viniculum did we?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T14:46:28-07:00","id":1393521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393520#post1393520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.... uh... We never got round to explaining how so many lasombra could throw off the Viniculum did we?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vinculum doesn't prevent monomancy, murdering your superiors, or brutal slaughtering of rival packs.<br /> <br /> Provided a Lasombra doesn't kill his own brothers and sisters in their pack, there's nothing preventing him from defecting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T14:55:51-07:00","id":1393524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393520#post1393520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.... uh... We never got round to explaining how so many lasombra could throw off the Viniculum did we?</div> </div> </div> </div>no<br /> <br /> but Lasombra elders traditionally murder antitribu packmates when they want to free a lasombra from their ties to a pack<br /> still, assuming v5 didn't retcon the vaulderie, the defectors are probably still tied to other sabbat, since sect gatherings usually has you taking part in the vaulderie with sabbat outside your pack<br /> <br /> that said, I'm certain the vinculum got retconned, since iirc, some defectors are required to be blood bond to camarilla members to be accepted (which should not be possible),<br /> so...unless the Cam is being duped...<br /> <br /> either way, I'd rather it be retconned than them comming up with another half assed plot device,<br /> (just look at how they explained the toreador antitribu defection in MET...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-01-2020, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T15:04:50-07:00","id":1393528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393524#post1393524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no<br /> <br /> but Lasombra elders traditionally murder antitribu packmates when they want to free a lasombra from their ties to a pack<br /> still, assuming v5 didn't retcon the vaulderie, the defectors are probably still tied to other sabbat, since sect gatherings usually has you taking part in the vaulderie with sabbat outside your pack<br /> <br /> <b>that said, I'm certain the vinculum got retconned, since iirc, some defectors are required to be blood bond to camarilla members to be accepted (which should not be possible),<br /> so...unless the Cam is being duped...</b><br /> <br /> either way, I'd rather it be retconned than them comming up with another half assed plot device,<br /> (just look at how they explained the toreador antitribu defection in MET...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Jason Carl explictly stated that, &quot;Yes, the Lasombra readily agreed to the Blood Bond because the Camarilla doesn't understand the Vinculum.&quot;<br /> <br /> They similarly laughed about the &quot;trade an Elder Sabbat for their defection&quot; because the Lasombra were going to have to murder a shit ton of their fellow Sabbat on their way out anyway.<br /> <br /> The defectors aren't stupid enough to leave enemies at their back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T15:12:02-07:00","id":1393531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393528#post1393528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The defectors aren't stupid enough to leave enemies at their back.</div> </div> </div> </div>which makes me wonder how we're still supposed to take the sabbat seriously","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value"