m Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T16:21:28-07:00","id":1393544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393543#post1393543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. That is how you CAN use Touchstones.<br /> <br /> 2. And yet there's all manner of other mortal ways to die and suffer plus other supernaturals that could end up taking their life.<br /> <br /> 3. And I am now officially informing you that such is not how it works and you should not say that it is that way. Because you are spreading misinformation. Also, &quot;the entire concept is disgusting and reprehensible&quot; is an attack on the gameline which is against the rules we've set down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. That is how the devs TELL YOU to use touchstones. <br /> <br /> 2. They can, but again, less chance than the developers telling the ST to abuse and kill touchstones for drama.<br /> <br /> 3. then how else can I express the visceral reaction I have to the concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T16:32:59-07:00","id":1393545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393544#post1393544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. That is how the devs TELL YOU to use touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>You remember it's not the ONLY way to use Touchstones, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. They can, but again, less chance than the developers telling the ST to abuse and kill touchstones for drama. </div> </div> </div>FYI, this is EVERYTHING that is said about Touchstones in V5's sourcebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Touchstones</b></span><br /> <br /> Each vampire begins with as many Touchstones as Convictions: humans who represent what you used to value in life, someone who represents or seems to incarnate one of your Convictions. If lost, the Conviction is lost as well. A Touchstone must be a living human being; connecting to Humanity through the inhuman is, at the very least, going the long way around.<br /> <br /> A Touchstone might be:<br /> <br /> \u25a0\u25a0 Your surviving human spouse, lover, or parent<br /> \u25a0\u25a0 Your human child, or (for older vampires) a descendant of your family line<br /> \u25a0\u25a0 A human who looks exactly like someone you loved in life<br /> \u25a0\u25a0 A human you admired in life or their descendant<br /> \u25a0\u25a0 A human related to someone you killed very early in your unlife: someone you swore you didn\u2019t have to kill because you aren\u2019t a monster, not really.<br /> \u25a0\u25a0 Someone you have come to recognize as a rare decent person even in your eyes: a volunteer at the animal shelter, a priest, a nurse, a social worker, a nice old lady in the neighborhood<br /> \u25a0\u25a0 Someone who represents something you once held dear in life and still cling to: a soldier, a baseball player, a musician or artist, clergy from your faith<br /> \u25a0\u25a0 Someone who guards, symbolizes, or protects a thing you value: the doorman of the building you used to live in, the cop on your old beat, a crusading reporter, the single mom living in your childhood home, the caretaker who sweeps your gravesite Touchstones provide links to and mechanical support for your<br /> <br /> Humanity; see p. 239 for detailed rules. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Damaging and destroying touchstones</b></span><br /> <br /> In addition to Tenet violations, other acts endanger the vampire\u2019s Humanity. When such acts occur, the vampire gains additional Stains based on the severity of the occurrence. <b>A Touchstone is damaged when something bad happens to them, usually something caused by the Kindred or even something stirred up indirectly by the vampire\u2019s actions.</b> (It\u2019s up to the Storyteller whether a normal disease or job loss counts as \u201cbad\u201d in this case.)<br /> <br /> A Touchstone is also damaged if they change in a way the vampire doesn\u2019t approve of: their widow remarries, the priest leaves the parish, the ballplayer moves from the White Sox to the Twins. By trying to prevent the Touchstone from changing, of course, the vampire may make things bad enough to damage the Touchstone anyway. A Touchstone is destroyed when they betray their convictions (specifically, when they betray the Conviction for which the vampire values them), when they are killed violently or Embraced, or when something truly disastrous happens to them.<br /> <br /> If a vampire directly causes the damage or the destruction of their own Touchstone, the Stains gained increase. <b>Of course, any Storyteller worth their salt creates story and drama that puts pressure on the player to decide between preserving their Touchstone and achieving some vampiric goal.</b><br /> <br /> If, by contrast, your Touchstone dies peacefully or just in the normal course of things, you may be able to transfer your fixation to another human connected to them: their child or sibling, their successor in the position, etc. This change requires a Humanity test (Difficulty 4) while meeting or observing them, and likely requires further story action.<br /> <br /> Unless you manage to transfer your attention to a new Touchstone, your Conviction connected to the destroyed Touchstone is lost. </div> </div> </div>You have repeatedly cited the section &quot;Damaging and Destroying Touchstones&quot; as if that was the only section on Touchstones or even the section on Storytelling them. It never says to do these things, it merely gives the rules for doing so. You have been misrepresenting Touchstones and the books handling of them for numerous posts.<br /> <br /> Please stop unless you have citations to provide that encourages STs to go after loved ones or encourage abuse. You have made your fanon take on them into something it is not as all the examples are loving kind relationships.<br /> <br /> The bolded part seems to be the only part that may even IMPLY that but it is in no way an encouragement to actual abuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. then how else can I express the visceral reaction I have to the concept? </div> </div> </div>Please don't. If it's a subject you can't speak of without trashing the game, then just skip the topic. I'm sorry but it's for the good of the forum unless you can provide citation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announ