blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2020, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T22:51:25-07:00","id":1393963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393959#post1393959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean? Vicissitude pre-V5 when the older versions and V20 were in the helm was the one of the most FREEFORM and RP intensive disciplines in all of VTM in how much you could even <i>do</i> with it. What do you mean by that? This the reason WHY the Tzimisce are so damn popular- because of all the unique and crazy possibilities you could do with them. This is why taking out Vicissitude would be one of the greatest disasters to happen with V5 if that is carried out. Why take it out? For what reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I like the Tzimisce for reasons other than their Discipline. But sure, I guess I can see people liking it.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce = Inhuman Modern Day Noble.<br /> <br /> But different strokes for different folks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes it IS. Vicissitude is its own entire thing, minute similarities would justify clobbering out such a classic discipline such as Vicissitude. Not only that its the SIGNATURE of the Tzimisce bare none. There have already been a HUGE amount of bad such with the Lasombra losing Obtenebration for some tenuous necromacy mixed into this new &quot;Oblivion&quot; and vice versa for the various Necromancy bloodlines. It's already scary that the Setites had their signature discipline going away to the wind. The only reason why no one fussed about it that much because the Setites aren't that popular, but its completely different for the Tzimisce. Protean for Vicissitude, for the Tzimisce? lolno. </div> </div> </div>You realize that it would still be in the game, right?<br /> <br /> In V5, it wouldn't be, &quot;Tzimisce now become bats and wolves.&quot; Or at least not completely.<br /> <br /> It would be, &quot;Protean users can now flesh-sculpt their bodies and enter Zulo form.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I'm confused why you keep acting like the power would disagree versus just becoming more available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T22:53:05-07:00","id":1393964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393961#post1393961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep and that's entirely valid as a matter of preference.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Blood Cults establishes that every individual cult has completely unique and unknown rituals.<br /> <br /> The Church of Cain have fire magic the Sabbat stole but no one else has (Lure of Flames but even better)<br /> <br /> The Setites have the Rituals related to the former Path of Corruption.<br /> <br /> The Path of Mithras have rituals related to Sunlight and War.<br /> <br /> So presumably the Kolduns have rituals no one else does.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if it is a clan discipline, then they aren't super rare, and if it's Blood Sorcery, it isn't something no one else has, it's something to be stolen soonest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T23:02:19-07:00","id":1393965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393959#post1393959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it IS. Vicissitude is its own entire thing, minute similarities would justify clobbering out such a classic discipline such as Vicissitude. Not only that its the SIGNATURE of the Tzimisce bare none. There have already been a HUGE amount of bad such with the Lasombra losing Obtenebration for some tenuous necromacy mixed into this new &quot;Oblivion&quot; and vice versa for the various Necromancy bloodlines. It's already scary that the Setites had their signature discipline going away to the wind. The only reason why no one fussed about it that much because the Setites aren't that popular, but its completely different for the Tzimisce. Protean for Vicissitude, for the Tzimisce? lolno.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except. As established in my post. It wasn't it's own thing. Just as Serpentis wasn't it's own thing. They were literally NPC powers that got changed into player powers while not actually fixing anything. Protean and Viss are both themed around shape shifting and evolution. Serpentis was protean and presence powers. Dementation was it's own thing and was the Malk's &quot;SIGNATURE&quot; power and yet somehow, most of the important stuff was converted in each case.<br /> <br /> The important part of Visscitude that people like: Flesh crafting. Dots 1-3 of the discipline. Could easily be made an amalgam of blood sorcery, Auspex, Dominate, or some other discipline that isn't Animalism, Fortitude, Presence, or Obfuscate. This means that Tzimisce still have their signature power because they will have the easiest time accessing it, other clans need to dip out of clan to get it which will always be easiest if you drink and learn from a Tzimisce. Even better as IF it's blood sorcery, that means that it REQUIRES that you have a teacher who knows it, so usually a Tzimisce to learn it.<br /> <br /> The issue with signature disciplines is that it works if and only if the game is designed around each clan having them, like Requiem did. VTM wasn't and so a lot of the &quot;Signature&quot; powers ended up having overlap with others. Somehow, mysteriously, the clans managed to keep most of their uniqueness without needing a separate discipline that was another discipline but better. The Ministry still has eyes of the serpent, and in most cases, they'll be the only ones with it. Malks still have dementation. Lasombra still have Arms of the Ahriman.<br /> <br /> Yes, there's been complaints about Oblivion and it's changes but. There's also been a lot of appreciation for those changes as well. At this point, people will complain about whatever changes are made but we can say for certain Viss has 0 chance of being it's own discipline. It breaks the design philosophy of the game for one, it could barely support the five power options in previous editions (See: It spread one power out across three), it also already fits into a discipline which matches it's primary theme. We also know that Tzimisce have protean from Chicago by night.<br /> <br /> Edit: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393958#post1393958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dislike the way amalgams are being handled, and the loss of identity and options that the removal of clan uniques is causing</div> </div> </div> </div>This is well. Definitely a valid opinion I suppose but it's not really causing a loss of options by any definition of the word. Loss of identity is also arguable. Let's take the easiest to get amalgam: Eyes of the Serpent. It requires Presence 1 and Protean 1. The only people who can get easy access to that are the Ministry. Anyone else has to have one of the two components in clan and then has to get the other through a predator type OR they have to... learn it from someone with the relevant power. Given it's a presence power, most people that are going to learn it have to build their character around it by either: A) Taking it at character creation via the previously mentioned method which is restrictive or B) Give up a higher level power for a level 1 power.<br /> <br /> If anything, amalgams have increased clan identity because now Brujah can get spark of rage, Nosferatu can get unliving hive, Tremere get Possession, Toreador get Unerring Aim, Malks get Dementation and Conceal, Ventrue can get Irresistible Voice, Gangrel get Enduring beasts. Each clan now has an amalgam that they can get easily because they have it in clan. Can other people learn these powers? Yes. Could you learn protean, dementation, obteneration, etc in older editions? Yes. It's just that now it's remotely possible to learn it without the help of another person with the investment of a very rare resource, otherwise you still have to drink the blood of another vampire to get it. Usually the one who's clan has it primarily for the easiest way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","user":"Necroticbinder","date":". 06-04-2020, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T23:06:30-07:00","id":1393966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393964#post1393964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But if it is a clan discipline, then they aren't super rare, and if it's Blood Sorcery, it isn't something no one else has, it's something to be stolen soonest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I think making it more widely available would be good because if the Assamites have it, then the Tzimisce should.<br /> <br /> I feel like the Tzimisce should be one of the big Blood Mages in the setting.<br /> <br /> But I understand if you disagree. Its a matter of preference.<br /> <br /> I also point out it might NOT be one of their Clan Disciplines. Modiphius might give them any combination of Disciplines. It could be Auspex, Vicissitude, and Animalism. Or it could be Blood Sorcery, Protean, and Auspex.<br /> <br /> Animalism, Blood Sorcery, and Protean is just my preference. Clearly not yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2020, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T23:28:59-07:00","id":1393968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with signature disciplines is that it works if and only if the game is designed around each clan having them, like Requiem did.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do signature disciplines don't work just because a few Clans don't have some? What does that mean? They worked perfectly before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protean and Viss are both themed around shape shifting and evolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, tenuous similarities don't mean they are the same at all. Vicissitude is more about biologicalism, while Protean is basically all about animals. The ONLY similarity is that they both extensively utilize supernatural change to physical forms. Beside that they have ZERO connections with eachother.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could easily be made an amalgam of blood sorcery, Auspex, Dominate, or some other discipline that isn't Animalism, Fortitude, Presence, or Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, just no. The amalgamation garbage has to stop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It breaks the design philosophy of the game for one</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the exact &quot;design philosophy&quot; are you referring to? If you mean the nerfs that were done in V5 as a whole- yeah I'd agree. That's what happens when you deliberately severe 6+ disciplines for people who played or wanted to play as Elders. Now that I think of it Vicissitude is DEFINITELY getting the boot for some ghetto Protean because of how they changed how disciplines worked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ministry</div> </div> </div> </div>Ministry? Never heard of it. I only recognize Setite. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-04-2020, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T23:44:43-07:00","id":1393974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393965#post1393965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> 1)Somehow, mysteriously, the clans managed to keep most of their uniqueness without needing a separate discipline that was another discipline but better.<br /> <br /> 2)Yes, there's been complaints about Oblivion and it's changes but. There's also been a lot of appreciation for those changes as well. At this point, people will complain about whatever changes are made but we can say for certain Viss has 0 chance of being it's own discipline. It breaks the design philosophy of the game for one, it could barely support the five power options in previous editions (See: It spread one power out across three), it also already fits into a discipline which matches it's primary theme. We also know that Tzimisce have protean from Chicago by night.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> 3)This is well. Definitely a valid opinion I suppose but it's not really causing a loss of options by any definition of the word. Loss of identity is also arguable. Let's take the easiest to get amalgam: Eyes of the Serpent. It requires Presence 1 and Protean 1. The only people who can get easy access to that are the Ministry. Anyone else has to have one of the two components in clan and then has to get the other through a predator type OR they have to... learn it from someone with the relevant power. Given it's a presence power, most people that are going to learn it have to build their character around it by either: A) Taking it at character creation via the previously mentioned method which is restrictive or B) Give up a higher level power for a level 1 power.<br /> <br /> 4)If anything, amalgams have increased clan identity because now Brujah can get spark of rage, Nosferatu can get unliving hive, Tremere get Possession, Toreador get Unerring Aim, Malks get Dementation and Conceal, Ventrue can get Irresistible Voice, Gangrel get Enduring beasts. Each clan now has an amalgam that they can get easily because they have it in clan. Can other people learn these powers? Yes. Could you learn protean, dementation, obteneration, etc in older editions? Yes. It's just that now it's remotely possible to learn it without the help of another person with the investment of a very rare resource, otherwise you still have to drink the blood of another vampire to get it. Usually the one who's clan has it primarily for the easiest way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Erm.. going to have to say, some of the clans do blur together, telling the difference between a Presence using ventrue and a presence using toreador is a crap shoot for instance. The aesthetics and disciplines of both clans over lap a lot. (for instance), now Lasombra are going to overlap with Hecata as well, in another mush. <br /> <br /> 2) Then it's lost what made it interesting, sadly.<br /> <br /> 3) and due to the idiotic 'amalgams count against you 5 power limit' characters utterly know that Followers of Set are just weird gangrel.<br /> <br /> 4)hard and complete diasgree. Especially again with the no more than 5 powers from any discipline, including amalgams (Does this mean amalgams take a slot in 2 disciplines btw?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-04-2020, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T23:49:56-07:00","id":1393975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, just no. The amalgamation garbage has to stop. </div> </div> </div>I think we're past that point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393968#post1393968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ministry? Never heard of it. I only recognize Setite. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A weird name for a clan that has numerous branches that don't worship Set as of Revised.<br /> <br /> Actually before since we have the Serpents of Light.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T00:06:11-07:00","id":1393978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393963#post1393963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1)Tzimisce = Inhuman Modern Day Noble.<br /> <br /> But different strokes for different folks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2)You realize that it would still be in the game, right?<br /> <br /> In V5, it wouldn't be, &quot;Tzimisce now become bats and wolves.&quot; Or at least not completely.<br /> <br /> It would be, &quot;Protean users can now flesh-sculpt their bodies and enter Zulo form.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I'm confused why you keep acting like the power would disagree versus just becoming more available.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Tzimisce = Inhuman modern day Cenobite, Pinhead with fangs. Inhuman Modern Day noble is a ventrue...or a lasombra..or a giovanni,..or a toreador...<br /> <br /> 2) But it would be this blurred mess that locked you out of ever, if you wanted to do so later, coming back to learn the other proteans. Without that only 5 powers including amalgams hard limit, it would be slightly less of an issue, I would still not like it, it would still make them feel like a gangrel bloodline, but it makes a little more sense than merging 'summoning the darkness from outside reality, the elder dark from between the stars' with 'summoning the dead'. Tzimisce having Blood sorcery as a clan discipline however is a hard nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T00:18:01-07:00","id":1393980,"title":"","content":"I think its very lazy put Serpentis, Vis and Protean in the same box lol. Using the same logic they could combine Dominate, Presence and Obfuscate, too. Its all about mind control, just separate it in alternate levels/amalg. Of course, if you wanted to make a vampire who control feelings AND control actions you would be tons out of luck because you can only have 5 powers per discipline, but who cares? So think very well if you will buy this very especific almalgam, dear player! Feelings are part of the brain; troughs too; perceptions too, so its the right thing merge the 3. Ladys and gentleman, Dominacensecate!!! with the alternative levels to you decide your expert area, baby!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","user":"blailton","date":". 06-04-2020, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T01:29:16-07:00","id":1393985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393943#post1393943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That actually MAKES the argument. God those are a terrible abomination, right up their with True Brujah and Blood Brothers on the 'oh no WW, why?!?!' list</div> </div> </div> </div>How dare you.<br /> The blood brothers are an underrated gem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393955#post1393955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly sure you could right &quot;fuck V5&quot; and get a bunch of likes from the haters that roam around it).</div> </div> </div> </div>From my experience, no, you can't. I've written a lot of poor anti-v5 posts and got nothing for it. Interestingly, a very constructive 'good idea for V5' post in the a V5 camarilla thread, and presumably got more reports than likes, because despite the content of the post I'd angered the tribe...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But really. Removing Viss for Protean isn't outrageous. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/dC9DTdqPmRnlS/giphy-downsized-medium.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Protean is about using the beast to manifest temporary physical changes. Serpentis does the same but through a lense of faith.<br /> Vicissitude is a discipline of sculpturing surgery with permanent results.<br /> If you're going to join them together, you might as well pair presence with dominate and obfuscate, potence with fortitude, Obtenebration and.... Nevermind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Old clan Tzmisce were the creations of the Dunning-Kruger effect. Change my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-04-2020, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T01:34:20-07:00","id":1393986,"title":"","content":"That gif was the exact same reaction I had when I first read that. lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T01:42:34-07:00","id":1393988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393985#post1393985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Protean is about using the beast to manifest temporary physical changes. Serpentis does the same but through a lense of faith.<br /> Vicissitude is a discipline of sculpturing surgery with permanent results.<br /> If you're going to join them together, you might as well pair presence with dominate and obfuscate, potence with fortitude, Obtenebration and.... Nevermind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a fair comparison, merging Presence and Dominate does make way more sense than Vis and Protean and Serpentis turning into this messy..thing that locks you out of the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T04:40:35-07:00","id":1394018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393988#post1393988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually a fair comparison, merging Presence and Dominate does make way more sense than Vis and Protean and Serpentis turning into this messy..thing that locks you out of the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>protean and serpentis merging does work,<br /> it was already the case in previous editions<br /> <br /> those two powers, as well as Daimonion were about manifesting powers and changing shapes framed by some theme or myth,<br /> daimonion and serpentis frame their powers/shapes around demonic/egyptian myths<br /> Protean has a &quot;nature&quot; theme going on<br /> <br /> one setite bloodline had protean as a discipline, but had different shapes (jaguar instead of wolves iirc), because they followed some Aztec myth, instead of egyptian myth<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is different however,<br /> their re-shaping aren't framed (locked) by some myth,<br /> you just mutate your body in whatever shape you want, each level pushes the limits a bit further, and breaking the limits imposed by vampiric stasis<br /> <br /> at Vici 1-3, you can roughly increase your physical aptitudes, but at the expense of another (you can increase strength but have to sacrifice health or dexterity etc)<br /> at Vici 4 (zulo shape), you can min-max your attributes without sacrificing health (+3 to str/dex/sta)<br /> zulo shapes may sound similar to protean war form, but the zulo shape isn't locked and can be further modified<br /> at Vici 5+, you've pretty much broken most limits to mutation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-04-2020, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T04:54:09-07:00","id":1394020,"title":"","content":"late to the conversation but i'm gonna throw my 2 cents in anyway.<br /> <br /> they probably gonna replace vis with protean and make fleshcrafting an amalgam.<br /> i don't think the removal of unique disciplines is the problem but rather the systems that they've replaced them with (both amalgams and loresheets) are just woefully inadequate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:06:04-07:00","id":1394033,"title":"","content":"For those who dislike V5's chthonic themed Obtenebration, what do you think its source should be or was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:12:17-07:00","id":1394035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394033#post1394033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who dislike V5's chthonic themed Obtenebration, what do you think its source should be or was?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> actually Chthonic, meaning from the far horizon, tapping into the power of the nephandic creatures beyond the umbra, who are older than creation and care not for humanity, the closest thing WoD has to the Mythos Gods. Not 'old and hungry ghosts'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:22:41-07:00","id":1394037,"title":"","content":"I think the Chthonic thing is fine, the Abyss is close enough. <br /> <br /> Making it the same as the shadowlands is bloody daft though.<br /> <br /> Like all the merging stuff, presence and dominate both control people, why weren't they merged?<br /> <br /> It seems like just trying to remove fun at every opportunity...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:25:04-07:00","id":1394038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394035#post1394035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> who are older than creation and care not for humanity,</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't recall any mention of discrete, indigenous creatures in V5's Abyss, that does sound like Shalim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:32:28-07:00","id":1394041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394038#post1394038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I don't recall any mention of discrete, indigenous creatures in V5's Abyss, that does sound like Shalim.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> unless they have totally changed the Abyss, it is the prison of The Fallen (except Lucifer), at the heart of the Shadowlands, which takes away all the Cosmic Horror you could play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:32:55-07:00","id":1394042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394037#post1394037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Chthonic thing is fine, the Abyss is close enough. <br /> <br /> Making it the same as the shadowlands is bloody daft though.<br /> <br /> Like all the merging stuff, presence and dominate both control people, why weren't they merged?<br /> <br /> It seems like just trying to remove fun at every opportunity...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because one is emotional control and because the other is direct control. Dominate has always been the hammer to Presences scalpel. And more importantly, each contributes to the themes of multiple clans. Unique disciplines work as an all or nothing affair. The arguments about why they &quot;define the clan&quot; for the ones got merged demonstrate exactly that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:39:58-07:00","id":1394044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394020#post1394020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">late to the conversation but i'm gonna throw my 2 cents in anyway.<br /> <br /> they probably gonna replace vis with protean and make fleshcrafting an amalgam.<br /> i don't think the removal of unique disciplines is the problem but rather the systems that they've replaced them with (both amalgams and loresheets) are just woefully inadequate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Serpentis, Thanatosis and Visceraticka can all comfortably be put under a label of weird protean.<br /> Vicissitude isn't.<br /> I mean, I think they'll do it, because they're absolute madmen/women, but It's think it's an atrocious idea.<br /> <br /> Oblivion is a dumb MakesNoSense merger. Necromancy was basically Death-themed Thaumaturgy, the only mechanical difference was the lack of willpower rolls; It had paths under the main discipline, it had plentiful rituals, you couldn't use it in frenzy and you couldn't use it if you had some kind of no-magic flaw. Obtenebreation was a discipline. Sure it had a mystical side to it, but it didn't have paths, it was just one discipline, and although it did have rituals they were few (and there's a few disciplines I think that could use rituals: Chimestry, Vicissitude, Spiritus... There are a few discipline powers that are basically rituals, though honestly that's too my chargrin and a discussion on their own). You could use Obtenebration in Frenzy, which is a no-no for Thaumaturges, Necromancers and Kolduns.<br /> <br /> Diamonion draws power from demons, but it isn't Dark Thaumaturgy. Just because something has a similar source doesn't mean they should come together as disciplines. Thanatosis isn't necromancy. Quietus may involve turning your blood into different kinds of poisons but it isn't about burning blood to channel your will into the creation of miracles...<br /> <br /> It's... V5's discipline amalgamations are well and truly the offspring of the Dunning Krueger effect: When someone knows a little bit about something, they'll be far more willing to share their knowledge and views to impress than someone who knows a good deal about something. Oblivion is the result of someone reading hints that the Abyss might be something to do with the oblivion of the underworld, and they've gone all-in on that idea without knowing much else about either Necromancy or Obtenebration. <b>The thing with Occult knowledge is that you're supposed to emphasize how little we truly know, not take the first theory we read as fact.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:42:24-07:00","id":1394046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394041#post1394041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> unless they have totally changed the Abyss, it is the prison of The Fallen (except Lucifer), at the heart of the Shadowlands, which takes away all the Cosmic Horror you could play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's to say that other worlds don't exist across the Abyss? It's allegedly infinite. Although it would be implied that those worlds are subject the same process of decay as &quot;ours&quot; and I suppose that could be seen as form of kinship, which may be at odds with the principles of Qlippoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 06-04-2020, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:44:43-07:00","id":1394049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394046#post1394046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who's to say that other worlds don't exist across the Abyss? It's allegedly infinite. Although it would be implied that those worlds are subject the same process of decay as &quot;ours&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> we are obviously thinking about different abyss..because I am thinking about the one in the Shadowlands, created by god (and hence not Chthonic) as a prison for the fallen, the one tied to necromancy which one are you thinking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-04-2020, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:59:16-07:00","id":1394053,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Hey folks,<br /> <br /> This is on me and I would give myself a warning if I could. We're falling into old habits, though. A reminder that everyone here is allowed to love different parts of vampire and there are some people who are just going to prefer different rules interpretations. That means some people prefer Blood Brothers, some people prefer Old Clan Tzimisce, and some people prefer Modern ones. Same for people who like combining disciplines vs. keeping them separate. Neither is &quot;right&quot; because it's all a matter of preference and taste.<br /> <br /> Please keep this in mind when addressing issues that there's no &quot;right&quot; way to enjoy vampire.<br /> <br /> My bad.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:14:36-07:00","id":1394057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394049#post1394049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> we are obviously thinking about different abyss..because I am thinking about the one in the Shadowlands, created by god (and hence not Chthonic) as a prison for the fallen, the one tied to necromancy which one are you thinking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about the one in <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i>. A Samedi recounts a sort of guided tour he was given by a loa. He went through the part of the Shadowlands where old buildings exist, then &quot;a place of perpetual storm&quot;, then a &quot;maze&quot;, then he was shown &quot;the infinite abyss that yawns before Oblivion&quot;. He compared Oblivion itself to &quot;a black hole with a will&quot;. He said that standing before the Abyss felt like being touched by Lasombra powers, although he heard &quot;whispers&quot; and &quot;one unending scream&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just reread about the &quot;Pit of Contemplation&quot; ritual, which opens a door to Oblivion. It consistently refers that place as &quot;Oblivion&quot; and unlike the border between the Abyss and the Labyrinth, it's silent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:18:53-07:00","id":1394058,"title":"","content":"We weren't saying OCTzmisce were terrible horrible worst things ever and that you're bad for playing them. I know people that love OCT and would never dream of denying them from my games. I like Tzmisce with Auspex, Animalism and Dominate; That's a really fun spread that really fits a 'lord of the land' character. <br /> <br /> However, I think a lot of issues with Tzmisce are due to that Dracula guy. People love Dracula, yet Dracula is Tzmisce and that's totally different from the Dracula they were thinking off... And therein some cognitive disonance occurs. <br /> <br /> Weren't OCT, like True Brujah, Meant to be pretentious pretenders that just rejected some main-clan stuff and then made up a history of them being superior to back them up anyways? <br /> <br /> Ironically, I think giving Tzmisce Protean instead of Vicissitude will be enforcing that 'Right' way to play Tzmisce on others. It's like saying &quot;no, you can't have your weird fleshy discipline to get obsessed with and for us to be afraid of, you need to be a <i>normal</i> vampire.&quot; <br /> <br /> The oblivion thing's much the same. Don't dedicate yourself to exploring the once unknowable Abyss, it's just a weird cousin of necromancy. Don't go all in on your clan specific we're all supposed to be conventional vampires who are normal....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:18:57-07:00","id":1394059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394057#post1394057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm talking about the one in <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i>. A Samedi recounts a sort of guided tour he was given by a loa. He went through the part of the Shadowlands where old buildings exist, then &quot;a place of perpetual storm&quot;, then a &quot;maze&quot;, then he was shown &quot;the infinite abyss that yawns before Oblivion&quot;. He compared Oblivion itself to &quot;a black hole with a will&quot;. He said that standing before the Abyss felt like being touched by Lasombra powers, although he heard &quot;whispers&quot; and &quot;one unending scream&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just reread about the &quot;Pit of Contemplation&quot; ritual, which opens a door to Oblivion. It consistently refers that place as &quot;Oblivion&quot; and unlike the border between the Abyss and the Labyrinth, it's silent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup,. the totally not Chthonic one then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:28:56-07:00","id":1394062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394058#post1394058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't OCT, like True Brujah, Meant to be pretentious pretenders that just rejected some main-clan stuff and then made up a history of them being superior to back them up anyways?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, Justin Achilli hated the Black Hand and tried to say everything they believed was wrong. Then V20 brought the Black Hand back and established that both the True Brujah and Old Clan Tzimisce may not have been 100% right but they were probably about 80%.<br /> <br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary:<br /> <br /> * Establishing the True Hand as taking over a large part of Africa. Establishing the True Brujah were real and making the Tik Tok Man.<br /> * Dracula has a huge section of the book where he's going to kill Kupala to free his Clan from thousands of years of slavery.<br /> <br /> The Old Clan Tzimisce having the original Tzimisce culture (Vicissitude or not) as established in Dark Ages. It's just that the &quot;Soul eater&quot; was actually the Eldest of their kind, eating and warping the Clan from within. Which is a terrible thing for Antediluvian worshipers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:31:33-07:00","id":1394063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394059#post1394059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yup,. the totally not Chthonic one then</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm getting that V5's Obtenebration place is beneath creation and yours is outside it. Is that different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:39:21-07:00","id":1394065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394058#post1394058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We weren't saying OCTzmisce were terrible horrible worst things ever and that you're bad for playing them. I know people that love OCT and would never dream of denying them from my games. I like Tzmisce with Auspex, Animalism and Dominate; That's a really fun spread that really fits a 'lord of the land' character.<br /> <br /> However, I think a lot of issues with Tzmisce are due to that Dracula guy. People love Dracula, yet Dracula is Tzmisce and that's totally different from the Dracula they were thinking off... And therein some cognitive disonance occurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the issue is that I became a fan of Clan Tzimisce due to TRANSYLVANIA CHRONICLES and VAMPIRE: THE DARK AGES over the Modern interpretation. For me, I just absolutely loved TRANSYLVANIA BY NIGHT and it is one of my all-time favorite supplements for the game. Like I said, I don't hate Vicissitude, that's very important to creating the armies of deformed monsters that serve the Tzimisce and things like Yorak the Elder. I just am a much bigger fan of things like the Omen War, Vladimir Rustovich, and the complicated web of politics that existed between the voivodes.<br /> <br /> As stated, it plays into my &quot;Hollywood Dracula&quot; enjoyment of the clan because the Tzimisce of the Dark Ages predate the historical Dracula joining their ranks but has all of the trappings of him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ironically, I think giving Tzmisce Protean instead of Vicissitude will be enforcing that 'Right' way to play Tzmisce on others. It's like saying &quot;no, you can't have your weird fleshy discipline to get obsessed with and for us to be afraid of, you need to be a <i>normal</i> vampire.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I think the issue would be that the Weird Fleshy DisciplineTM part would just be alternate powers of Protean. The big change is as someone else said in this thread, &quot;Vicissitude effects others and is permanent.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that will be changed because that's greatly overpowered versus Protean. Which is why it would be a Combo Discipline.<br /> <br /> Personally, though, I think they need to houserule the limits. I see no reason that a vampire shouldn't be able to have dozens of Alternate Powers of a Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Make them like Rotes for Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2020, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:54:43-07:00","id":1394070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394063#post1394063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm getting that V5's Obtenebration place is beneath creation and yours is outside it. Is that different?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, in the same way that the Chthullu Mythos and Dantes inferno are different. I want the Chthullu vibes, not the borders of hell vibes, the totally alien and unknowable, vs the bit weird but still part of creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:57:34-07:00","id":1394071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394070#post1394070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, in the same way that the Chthullu Mythos and Dantes inferno are different. I want the Chthullu vibes, not the borders of hell vibes, the totally alien and unknowable, vs the bit weird but still part of creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its an uneasy combination, making the Baali's Children (meant to be Cthulhu Old Ones) the same as the Earthbound with Belial described as a giant dragon squid-thing.<br /> <br /> Honestly, alien inhuman monsters should be more like Werewolves things with the Banetenders.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:58:21-07:00","id":1394072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394065#post1394065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of the issue is that I became a fan of Clan Tzimisce due to TRANSYLVANIA CHRONICLES and VAMPIRE: THE DARK AGES over the Modern interpretation. For me, I just absolutely loved TRANSYLVANIA BY NIGHT and it is one of my all-time favorite supplements for the game. Like I said, I don't hate Vicissitude, that's very important to creating the armies of deformed monsters that serve the Tzimisce and things like Yorak the Elder. I just am a much bigger fan of things like the Omen War, Vladimir Rustovich, and the complicated web of politics that existed between the voivodes.<br /> <br /> As stated, it plays into my &quot;Hollywood Dracula&quot; enjoyment of the clan because the Tzimisce of the Dark Ages predate the historical Dracula joining their ranks but has all of the trappings of him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the issue would be that the Weird Fleshy DisciplineTM part would just be alternate powers of Protean. The big change is as someone else said in this thread, &quot;Vicissitude effects others and is permanent.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that will be changed because that's greatly overpowered versus Protean. Which is why it would be a Combo Discipline.<br /> <br /> Personally, though, I think they need to houserule the limits. I see no reason that a vampire shouldn't be able to have dozens of Alternate Powers of a Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Make them like Rotes for Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I came to them via the 2e Guide to the Sabbat, so the version I first encountered was the Metamorphosis/Death and the Soul version of flesh warping posthuman monsters, before they got any sorcery at all, so any rituals and spells feel like an add on. The DA version is cool....in DA, as a precursor to what they later transcend to, if a bit to similar to the Ventrue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-04-2020, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T10:00:46-07:00","id":1394073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394071#post1394071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its an uneasy combination, making the Baali's Children (meant to be Cthulhu Old Ones) the same as the Earthbound with Belial described as a giant dragon squid-thing.<br /> <br /> Honestly, alien inhuman monsters should be more like Werewolves things with the Banetenders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea, I kind of don't want a unified cosmology, I like the feeling that no one really properly understands what is actually going on, everyone is 'the blind man and the elephant', the mages feel the leg, vampires have an ear, wraiths have a tusk etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T10:35:33-07:00","id":1394081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394073#post1394073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I kind of don't want a unified cosmology, I like the feeling that no one really properly understands what is actually going on, everyone is 'the blind man and the elephant', the mages feel the leg, vampires have an ear, wraiths have a tusk etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love that, but that hasn't been what the WoD cosmology is like for a long while now. Before V5, it was taken as a universally-known truth that the Abrahamic God actually exists and created vampires. And when everyone agrees on the pure and undeniable truth about the nature of God, what mysteries can really remain?<br /> <br /> I much prefer V5's attempts to walk that back, putting more spotlight on alternate cosmologies and emphasizing that the Caine myth is, well, a myth, not proven fact. Revised tried to do the same thing earlier, with limited success, as did Demon with its &quot;layers&quot; cosmology. But, well, look at how fans reacted when someone suggested using Kindred rules for the Wan Kuei. I'm not sure the World of Darkness can ever really be &quot;blind man and the elephant&quot; given how attached people are to its history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T10:46:04-07:00","id":1394082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394081#post1394081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would love that, but that hasn't been what the WoD cosmology is like for a long while now. Before V5, it was taken as a universally-known truth that the Abrahamic God actually exists and created vampires. And when everyone agrees on the pure and undeniable truth about the nature of God, what mysteries can really remain?<br /> <br /> I much prefer V5's attempts to walk that back, putting more spotlight on alternate cosmologies and emphasizing that the Caine myth is, well, a myth, not proven fact. Revised tried to do the same thing earlier, with limited success, as did Demon with its &quot;layers&quot; cosmology. But, well, look at how fans reacted when someone suggested using Kindred rules for the Wan Kuei. I'm not sure the World of Darkness can ever really be &quot;blind man and the elephant&quot; given how attached people are to its history.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My objection to using Cainites rules for the Wan Kuei is that it makes them delusional descendants of a creature created by Yhwh, rather than something totally other, showing that the cosmology is more complicated than that. When you have Kindred/cainites being descendants of Caine...but also the Wan Kuei being subject to the Celestial Court, and the Yama Kings, and the Naphandi worshipping what is basically the Mythos..it looks like the Elephant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T10:53:00-07:00","id":1394084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394070#post1394070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, in the same way that the Chthullu Mythos and Dantes inferno are different. I want the Chthullu vibes, not the borders of hell vibes, the totally alien and unknowable, vs the bit weird but still part of creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394081#post1394081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love that, but that hasn't been what the WoD cosmology is like for a long while now. Before V5, it was taken as a universally-known truth that the Abrahamic God actually exists and created vampires. And when everyone agrees on the pure and undeniable truth about the nature of God, what mysteries can really remain?<br /> <br /> I much prefer V5's attempts to walk that back, putting more spotlight on alternate cosmologies and emphasizing that the Caine myth is, well, a myth, not proven fact. Revised tried to do the same thing earlier, with limited success, as did Demon with its &quot;layers&quot; cosmology. But, well, look at how fans reacted when someone suggested using Kindred rules for the Wan Kuei. I'm not sure the World of Darkness can ever really be &quot;blind man and the elephant&quot; given how attached people are to its history.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I don't get Oblivion being compared to Dante's Inferno or considered part of creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T10:55:59-07:00","id":1394086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394072#post1394072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came to them via the 2e Guide to the Sabbat, so the version I first encountered was the Metamorphosis/Death and the Soul version of flesh warping posthuman monsters, before they got any sorcery at all, so any rituals and spells feel like an add on. The DA version is cool....in DA, as a precursor to what they later transcend to, if a bit to similar to the Ventrue</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, in the first Tzimisce Clanbook, they had Neo-Feudalists and other people who were still ultra-polite noblemen. It's not a new element for even the Modern One too.<br /> <br /> Also, the Tzimisce did being feudal lords<i><b> better </b></i>than the Ventrue. The modern day Ventrue are MERCHANTS. *hock spit*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2020, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T10:56:45-07:00","id":1394087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394044#post1394044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oblivion is a dumb MakesNoSense merger. Necromancy was basically Death-themed Thaumaturgy, the only mechanical difference was the lack of willpower rolls; It had paths under the main discipline, it had plentiful rituals, you couldn't use it in frenzy and you couldn't use it if you had some kind of no-magic flaw. Obtenebreation was a discipline. Sure it had a mystical side to it, but it didn't have paths, it was just one discipline, and although it did have rituals they were few (and there's a few disciplines I think that could use rituals: Chimestry, Vicissitude, Spiritus... There are a few discipline powers that are basically rituals, though honestly that's too my chargrin and a discussion on their own). You could use Obtenebration in Frenzy, which is a no-no for Thaumaturges, Necromancers and Kolduns.<br /> <br /> Diamonion draws power from demons, but it isn't Dark Thaumaturgy. Just because something has a similar source doesn't mean they should come together as disciplines. Thanatosis isn't necromancy. Quietus may involve turning your blood into different kinds of poisons but it isn't about burning blood to channel your will into the creation of miracles...<br /> <br /> It's... V5's discipline amalgamations are well and truly the offspring of the Dunning Krueger effect: When someone knows a little bit about something, they'll be far more willing to share their knowledge and views to impress than someone who knows a good deal about something. Oblivion is the result of someone reading hints that the Abyss might be something to do with the oblivion of the underworld, and they've gone all-in on that idea without knowing much else about either Necromancy or Obtenebration. <b>The thing with Occult knowledge is that you're supposed to emphasize how little we truly know, not take the first theory we read as fact.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>i want to clarify that what i said is the main issue in my eyes but it isn't the only mistake they made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T11:02:35-07:00","id":1394088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394084#post1394084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> This is why I don't get Oblivion being compared to Dante's Inferno or considered part of creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Demon the Fallen made it the Accretion disk of the Abyss, which was the prison of the fallen, aka hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T11:10:13-07:00","id":1394089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394088#post1394088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Demon the Fallen made it the Accretion disk of the Abyss, which was the prison of the fallen, aka hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the issue is with Demon: The Fallen. Assuming that the V5 universe works the same way as Demon: The Fallen is like assuming that Wan Kuei are as they were originally written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T11:31:27-07:00","id":1394097,"title":"","content":"It is slightly tiring and increasingly annoying to have to say again and again that nowhere, nowhere except in Demon: the Fallen (and not even there), has been absolutely established in-universe that Caine's story is truth and not myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T11:35:36-07:00","id":1394098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394097#post1394097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is slightly tiring and increasingly annoying to have to say again and again that nowhere, nowhere except in Demon: the Fallen (and not even there), has been absolutely established in-universe that Caine's story is truth and not myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it a bad thing for it to be 100% true in the Vampire line? Because the Werewolves know their gods are 100% real. So do the Mages that know their cosmology is true.<br /> <br /> So do the Kuei Jin.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T11:47:58-07:00","id":1394100,"title":"","content":"Uhmmm... no, it's wouldn't be a bad thing, but I don't find it anywhere to be 100% true, according to published sources. It is different with the Werewolves (who have true spiritual and animistic experiences) and the Mages. According to Kindred of the East, I don't think there are any Ancestors awaken nowadays who remember the days of the Wan Kuei...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:00:13-07:00","id":1394103,"title":"","content":"I must be one of the exceptions, but I really like the Tzimisce Clan, but only as the only Clan. I don't like the new Sabbat version of the Clan as much. I like the old land bound nobles who cruel and yet honorable. Having them in the Sabbat undermines what makes them interesting for me. Then again, I kind of feel that way the Lasombra as well. I'm also intrigued by the idea of combining Vicissitude with Protean, or rather recreating it with a mix of Blood Sorcery and Protean. Animalism, Blood Sorcery, and Protean... that could potentially be cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1393500#post1393500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I feel like the Camarilla being champions of Humanity was always stupid and I wish in Revised they'd had Roads and Paths be a thing more Elders are on. The Camarilla is corrupt, vicious, and inhuman in ways that only Sabbat Elders could hope to match. I can't imagine them caring about Humanity and keeping vampires on it unless it's part of some larger plan to cripple the Neonates and keep them weak. Which is possible but not the way they're presnted. If I'd rebooted the Camarilla I'd make Roads and Gehenna Cults go hand in hand.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's LAUGHABLE that the Camarilla would give a shit about humanity. They're the boot on humanity's face and the reason the world sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always though this, at least ever since this idea arose about the Camarilla supporting Humanity or supposedly being the nice guys. The Camarilla rulers are monsters, they are just more controlled than the Sabbat. Camarilla leaders use their power over mortals and mortal institutions to undermine democracy, to increase crime, poverty, and corruption, to make themselves wealthier at the expense of everyone else, to literally enslave the minds of humans. The Camarilla probably cause more human death just from humans killing each other in Camarilla territory than the Sabbat vampires kill in their frenzies and blood baths.<br /> <br /> That is why the Lasombra need to get in on that action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 06-04-2020, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:04:37-07:00","id":1394105,"title":"","content":"Werewolves... Can you define God for me? A Celestial level spirit's status as a God is somewhat subjective. Definetly something to look up to but it doesn't really say much about the existence of an almighty. Remember, &quot;demon&quot; roughly translates to &quot;any manner of supernatural entities that we do not like&quot; and God is an even looser term. Anything from Jaggling all the way to &quot;The one above all&quot; can claim the title. The Werewolves know their Celestials are there, but they've got tunnel vision and don't really know what else is out there or how it applies to them. <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, with Dracula, If the game said he was a Malk, Nos, Toreador, Ravnos or Ventrue who had access to his own off-brand Thaumaturgy, I'd swallow it up. Other clans can manifest the &quot;Jar of Dirt&quot; weeakness, just as anyone can get &quot;repelled by crosses&quot; or &quot;Cast no Reflection&quot;. <br /> <br /> But also Dracula Bullshitted himself into a book so If he was actually something you'd totally not expect I'd totally roll with it. Dracula throwing all the clan weaknesses and stereotypes onto his fictional self is something I personally would totally do if I was in his shoes. <br /> <br /> Fuedalism can be done well by any other clan. Seems a bit racist that we want to view the eastern european one as the backwards fuedal lords who are out of the times even by vampire standards. Maybe it's a soviet/post soviet thing for american writers or something. It's less explicitly racist than what the Assamites got (and eastern europeans are white so racism to them isn't bad amrite) but I think it's pretty racist/not all that reflective of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:17:55-07:00","id":1394110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394105#post1394105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves... Can you define God for me? A Celestial level spirit's status as a God is somewhat subjective. Definetly something to look up to but it doesn't really say much about the existence of an almighty. Remember, &quot;demon&quot; roughly translates to &quot;any manner of supernatural entities that we do not like&quot; and God is an even looser term. Anything from Jaggling all the way to &quot;The one above all&quot; can claim the title. The Werewolves know their Celestials are there, but they've got tunnel vision and don't really know what else is out there or how it applies to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the Garou Nation is a religious military sect that venerates Gaia as their supreme being and the one they war in the name of. They're polytheistic and also venerate their Totems.<br /> <br /> There's no ambiguity that Gaia is someone you are to kill and die for.<br /> <br /> She's the capital G God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:22:54-07:00","id":1394112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394097#post1394097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is slightly tiring and increasingly annoying to have to say again and again that nowhere, nowhere except in Demon: the Fallen (and not even there), has been absolutely established in-universe that Caine's story is truth and not myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It shows up in one or two of the Mage books at least, explaining OOC that turning a vampire mortal again requires rolling more successes than Y##H (which is why it can't be done). That's the sort of thing I'm talking about wrt confirmation of the myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:26:25-07:00","id":1394113,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fuedalism can be done well by any other clan. Seems a bit racist that we want to view the eastern european one as the backwards fuedal lords who are out of the times even by vampire standards. Maybe it's a soviet/post soviet thing for american writers or something. It's less explicitly racist than what the Assamites got (and eastern europeans are white so racism to them isn't bad amrite) but I think it's pretty racist/not all that reflective of reality. </div> </div> </div>I find defending feudalism to be a poor use of fan efforts. It's a despicable system. There's no reason not to attack feudal lords as a class, Eastern European or Western. It's why I support things like the depiction of the Toreador in the French Revolution as engaged in unimaginable sick atrocities. Attacking class divides and divisions is a stand I support vampirism in. Part of why I love Vampire is that it attacks the &quot;monarch love&quot; that underpins a lot of fantasy and Dungeons and Dragons-esque attitudes.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, the aristocracy are evil parasites and fuck them.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I find the Tzimisce superior a representation of vampire lords than Ventrue due to having far more &quot;cool&quot; things about them. A Tzimisce lord is superior in intelligence, honor, and class than any Ventrue. Bluntly the Ventrue are just so....generic...by comparison to the Tzimisce voivodes. It's hard to take them seriously by comparison.<br /> <br /> I admit, I wouldn't mind moving them solely from Eastern Europe, though. The Tzimisce having a Scottish branch would be fucking awesome because the Clans would perfectly fit among them. Imagine the Black Dinner as a Tzimisce betrayal.<br /> <br /> No clan should be tied down to any specific region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2020, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:34:45-07:00","id":1394116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394112#post1394112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It shows up in one or two of the Mage books at least, explaining OOC that turning a vampire mortal again requires rolling more successes than Y##H (which is why it can't be done). That's the sort of thing I'm talking about wrt confirmation of the myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that\u2019s the Kruger-Dunning Effect again... because that was written in a Mage book by the Mage writing team that was not the same as the Vampire writing team and not as familiar with all the ins-and-outs of Vampire lore.<br /> <br /> They probably knew the gost of the default Caine myth (because let\u2019s face it, it is definitely one of the more evocative Vampire origin myths... certainly better than, say, Underworld\u2019s immortality virus + bat bite) and just presumed it was true without really questioning it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:36:51-07:00","id":1394117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394081#post1394081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before V5, it was taken as a universally-known truth that the Abrahamic God actually exists and created vampires. And when everyone agrees on the pure and undeniable truth about the nature of God, what mysteries can really remain?<br /> <br /> I much prefer V5's attempts to walk that back, putting more spotlight on alternate cosmologies and emphasizing that the Caine myth is, well, a myth, not proven fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Caine myth has been explicitly presented as a myth since the 1e core book in 1991. There has been no point in the history of the line when it wasn\u2019t presented as something many vampires believe, but the truth of which is unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:46:12-07:00","id":1394121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394098#post1394098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it a bad thing for it to be 100% true in the Vampire line? Because the Werewolves know their gods are 100% real. So do the Mages that know their cosmology is true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves know spirits are real. What counts as a god is a matter of perspective. <br /> <br /> And no, mages do not even have a coherent cosmology to confirm. Insofar as the Traditions have sort of worked on out, it\u2019s just another paradigm. The way mages work, truth is a relative concept to begin with, and certainty is more of an attitude than anything. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So do the Kuei Jin. </div> </div> </div>Not even gonna touch that one.<br /> <br /> But I will say, yes, it would hurt Vampire for it to be objectively true, as it would kill one of the core themes of the game, which is how corrupt power structures construct self-serving narratives to justify their existence, and how even people who aren\u2019t served by them end up having to use those narratives in order to fit in. It\u2019s also key to how Vampire culture changes over time and space, and it\u2019s crucial that different cults exist and be in conflict without most of them being simply deluded (or at least not more deluded than any others). <br /> <br /> The WoD isn\u2019t a land of absolute truth. It\u2019s too postmodern for that. If you think you\u2019ve found it, you\u2019re falling for the in-character perspectives (which, to be fair, I think some of the authors have also done at times).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:50:27-07:00","id":1394124,"title":"","content":"The Caine origin story has always been presented as the tale most vampires believed to be true about their race\u2019s origin and a lot of books implied it to be true. Of course storytellers were left to decide if it was true for their games.<br /> Demon the Fallen actually states that \u201cCaine\u201d existed and the first murder had a cosmically significant effect in creation itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:58:27-07:00","id":1394126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394116#post1394116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>And that\u2019s the Kruger-Dunning Effect again..</b>. because that was written in a Mage book by the Mage writing team that was not the same as the Vampire writing team and not as familiar with all the ins-and-outs of Vampire lore.<br /> <br /> They probably knew the gost of the default Caine myth (because let\u2019s face it, it is definitely one of the more evocative Vampire origin myths... certainly better than, say, Underworld\u2019s immortality virus + bat bite) and just presumed it was true without really questioning it.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Given I know what that means, I consider that an attack on developers and no one should ever use that to refer to them.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:59:30-07:00","id":1394127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394103#post1394103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always though this, at least ever since this idea arose about the Camarilla supporting Humanity or supposedly being the nice guys. The Camarilla rulers are monsters, they are just more controlled than the Sabbat. Camarilla leaders use their power over mortals and mortal institutions to undermine democracy, to increase crime, poverty, and corruption, to make themselves wealthier at the expense of everyone else, to literally enslave the minds of humans. The Camarilla probably cause more human death just from humans killing each other in Camarilla territory than the Sabbat vampires kill in their frenzies and blood baths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the only reason the Camarilla promotes the Path of Humanity is that it is the easiest path for vampires while maintaining the Masquerade. Too many other paths lead to such deviant behavior that the Masquerade becomes untenable. At the very least, such vampires should attract hunters to those specific vampires even if it does not lead to a general breakdown. The Camarilla is probably fine about some of the less conspicuous Paths though they may dislike them on general principle because if people realize there are alternatives to Humanity, then it leads some to them eventually to consider some of the more bizarre paths as legitimate. So it's just safer to keep things to Humanity.<br /> <br /> So I think that rule is less &quot;we care about Humanity&quot; as opposed to &quot;stop crapping on the lawn in front of the neighbors; they're going to call the cops&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:59:34-07:00","id":1394128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394117#post1394117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caine myth has been explicitly presented as a myth since the 1e core book in 1991. There has been no point in the history of the line when it wasn\u2019t presented as something many vampires believe, but the truth of which is unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Gehenna.<br /> <br /> But speaking as a huge fan of Noddism, I support 100% Caine being the true origin of vampire. Why should it be different than other gamelines?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <b>What do I think of the Tzimisce</b><br /> <br /> I admit, my fanboyism of the Tzimisce affects me when discussing them. If I had to choose to get rid of a clan and I had a choice between the Ventrue or the Tzimisce, I would 100% choose to get rid of the Ventrue. The Tzimisce do everything the Ventrue do but better. They are the embodiment of rulership, nobility, and absolute dominion over their holdings. As much as I love the Anarchs, I don't think the Tzimisce could ever join them. Every Tzimisce is a leader and born to rule over those surrounding them. I can't imagine them ever submitting to the egalitarian principles the Anarchs nominally support.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra ain't got shit on them.<br /> <br /> I figure the Tzimisce just let them THINK they were leaders of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2020, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:01:35-07:00","id":1394129,"title":"","content":"Please, let Requiem be Requiem, and let Masquerade be Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The game without the truth about vampire origins already exists: VtR.<br /> <br /> When we play Masquerade, we want Generations, Caine, Enoch and Second City. <br /> <br /> Now I gonna tell you something if you start adopting a agnostic scenario this forum will became the same as the VtR requiem: one thread for year because no one have motives to discuss anything because everything is 100% different in each game group, so no motives/awnsers to be made in those abandoned foruns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:07:40-07:00","id":1394131,"title":"","content":"I think Noddism is PROBABLY correct in the setting but I do think the mystery will never be confirmed the way that it is in Werewolf or Mage.<br /> <br /> Because vampire has a lot of things that DEPEND on the ambiguity.<br /> <br /> Even if it's still 80% certain SOMETHING similar to Caine existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:10:41-07:00","id":1394133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394112#post1394112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It shows up in one or two of the Mage books at least, explaining OOC that turning a vampire mortal again requires rolling more successes than Y##H (which is why it can't be done). That's the sort of thing I'm talking about wrt confirmation of the myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s a Vampire book that gives you several options to turn a vampire mortal again. It\u2019s called the Red Sign. Some options involve mages but not all of them.<br /> <br /> The point of the \u201ccan you roll more successes than God?\u201d Rethorical question is simply that stuff like turning a vampire back to human should never be achieved through mechanical solutions alone. You don\u2019t just solve that kind of problems by rolling dices. You build chronicles to find ways to do so. <br /> That may range from rediscovering an ancient and powerful ritual that still works in the current age, to track down Moses Maimonides through the planes (and possibly travel back in time as well) and convince him to perform that kind of magic on you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:14:12-07:00","id":1394134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394128#post1394128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Gehenna.<br /> <br /> But speaking as a huge fan of Noddism, I support 100% Caine being the true origin of vampire. Why should it be different than other gamelines?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <b>What do I think of the Tzimisce</b><br /> <br /> I admit, my fanboyism of the Tzimisce affects me when discussing them. If I had to choose to get rid of a clan and I had a choice between the Ventrue or the Tzimisce, I would 100% choose to get rid of the Ventrue. The Tzimisce do everything the Ventrue do but better. They are the embodiment of rulership, nobility, and absolute dominion over their holdings. As much as I love the Anarchs, I don't think the Tzimisce could ever join them. Every Tzimisce is a leader and born to rule over those surrounding them. I can't imagine them ever submitting to the egalitarian principles the Anarchs nominally support.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra ain't got shit on them.<br /> <br /> I figure the Tzimisce just let them THINK they were leaders of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the idea of eliminating the Venture in favor of the Tzimisce (and maybe the Lasombra) is actually kind of cool. When they came out with V:tR, they did away with the Lasombra and Tzimisce, perhaps with the implication that those concepts should fit into the new Ventrue Clan. Though that just makes everything a bit too generic. It V:tM is to be streamlined, maybe it would be cooler to get rid of the Ventrue in exchange for two leadership Clans, the Tzimisce and the Lasombra. Tzimisce to represent old fashioned leadership with a strict sense of honor, a tie to the land, and so on; while the Lasombra are the ruthless social darwinists who have no honor or adherence to any strict hierarchy, anyone who earns it has a place on top. Having those two archetypes actually lessons the need for a generic leadership Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:30:01-07:00","id":1394135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394131#post1394131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Noddism is PROBABLY correct in the setting but I do think the mystery will never be confirmed the way that it is in Werewolf or Mage.<br /> <br /> Because vampire has a lot of things that DEPEND on the ambiguity.<br /> <br /> Even if it's still 80% certain SOMETHING similar to Caine existed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I want Caine to have existed, and been cursed by SOMETHING, that is powerful enough to do an impression of omnipotence, something of the order of one of the Incarna, but for the KotE to have their origin also be the same amount of true, (this is why I prefer the God Machine version of Demons to the Fallen version of demons.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:33:31-07:00","id":1394136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394129#post1394129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, let Requiem be Requiem, and let Masquerade be Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The game without the truth about vampire origins already exists: VtR.<br /> <br /> When we play Masquerade, we want Generations, Caine, Enoch and Second City.<br /> <br /> Now I gonna tell you something if you start adopting a agnostic scenario this forum will became the same as the VtR requiem: one thread for year because no one have motives to discuss anything because everything is 100% different in each game group, so no motives/awnsers to be made in those abandoned foruns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once more, with feeling: Masquerade has <i>always </i>presented the truth as uncertain, since the very first book. Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary actually does a good job of closing the ring with some things from the 1st edition book that people had forgotten about, and it pretty well blows up the idea of any sort of certainty. <br /> <br /> People don\u2019t need certainty and canon to have discussions. If anything, certainty makes discussion pointless. <br /> <br /> And Requiem does have a known origin for vampires at this point. The only reason it didn\u2019t initially, I think, is because Achilli got really frustrated with people treating the Caine myth in a fundamentalist fashion, so he was like \u201cFuck it, we\u2019re not giving you anything this time.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:33:43-07:00","id":1394137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394135#post1394135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I want Caine to have existed, and been cursed by SOMETHING, that is powerful enough to do an impression of omnipotence, something of the order of one of the Incarna, but for the KotE to have their origin also be the same amount of true, (this is why I prefer the God Machine version of Demons to the Fallen version of demons.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In my shared WOD games, I've admittedly had Caine cursed by the Sun God Helios rather than God-God.<br /> <br /> Other texts translated it as God, Ra, Marduk, and Lucifer-Demiurgus.<br /> <br /> But we know the truth, it was Sol Invictus for ruining his turn at the Games of Divinity.<br /> <br /> DUN DUN DUN","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:37:10-07:00","id":1394138,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <br /> <br /> It's very interesting how you fanboy over certain clans in ways that are completely anathema to the way many fanboy over clans. Any other clans you got... ideas about? <br /> <br /> I think Ventrue are <i>good </i>because they're <i>boring</i>. Or, at least, the Ventrue are familiar, you're exposed to many of the ideas that compose the ventrue, even if you don't know the clan all that well. <br /> <br /> The Tzmisce, by comparison, are nuts. They're exotic: No matter if they're sabbat, viovodes, koldun or 'Old clan&quot;, they're really colourful, eccentric characters. Ventrue on the otherhand do their absolute best to be boring. I might be saying too much, but the Ventrue are playing Vampire: the masquerade whilst Tzmisce are playing Vampire: Carnival. Ventrue are subtle, Tzmisce are outrageous. Lasombra are outrageous. Not to say Ventrue don't possess flair or pizaz or whatever you want to call it, after all they're a clan with presence, but Ventrue are the Establishment whilst Lasombra/Tzmisce are trying to be the establishment. Ventrue could be regarded as passive characters, Lasombra are active characters and Tzmisce are... reactive I'd say. Explody characters are more interesting, but it's the ventrue that will more often remain standing when things go wrong. <br /> <br /> The Lasombra is looking for your weakness, The Tzmisce is waiting for your weakness, The Ventrue is just confident that he can build strength faster than you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:39:08-07:00","id":1394139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394131#post1394131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Noddism is PROBABLY correct in the setting but I do think the mystery will never be confirmed the way that it is in Werewolf or Mage.<br /> <br /> Because vampire has a lot of things that DEPEND on the ambiguity.<br /> <br /> Even if it's still 80% certain SOMETHING similar to Caine existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of those lines has an objective truth behind its myths and paradigms. Mage\u2019s entire point is that there can be no objective certainty because perception of reality is always predicated on conceptual biases. Even Werewolf makes a bid deal out of stuff that can\u2019t be demonstrated to be true in the literal sense, such as the Triat. <br /> <br /> Nor, as you suggested earlier, is Gehenna proof of the Noddist myth. It\u2019s just proof of the existence of some very ancient vampires. <br /> <br /> Folks, none of this is new. The idea that these things are the objective truth of the setting is on the level of internet rumor. It was never the reality nor the intent, and there\u2019s no reason to change that now just to be different from CoD, which is already plenty different to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:50:38-07:00","id":1394141,"title":"","content":"I disagree that the Ventrue are boring or banal. But they do represent a different style of rule from the Lasombra and the Tzimisces (they really should have kept the -s on the end of that). Of the three, the Tzimisce are the one without a natural inclination towards a social discipline. Being less prone to inspire or awe their subjects, or to simply dominate their minds, they\u2019ve gravitated towards other forms of motivation. <br /> <br /> Its actually why I <i>don\u2019t </i>think they should have Dominate as a clan discipline, though I\u2019ve always thought Protean made sense. <br /> <br /> Interestingly, what \u201cOld Clan\u201d means has shifted in different editions. In 2e they didn\u2019t have Vicissitude and were involved with the Tal\u2019mahe\u2019ra. In 3e (and presumably 4e) they had Vicissitude because all Tzimisce did, and the Old Clan were just the ones that never joined the Sabbat. I expect 5e will follow that model, minus the unique discipline. There\u2019s a line in Chicago by Night that implies any Camarilla Tzimisce would be considered Old Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:52:10-07:00","id":1394142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394138#post1394138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a><br /> <br /> It's very interesting how you fanboy over certain clans in ways that are completely anathema to the way many fanboy over clans. Any other clans you got... ideas about?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I've been playing since 1994, I have opinions on all of the Clans.<br /> <br /> Usually, I think my ideas are the normal ones. Like I said, I was all for the Dark Ages knightly lord and ladies Tzimisce. I was surprised to find people liked the crazy inhuman ones over these.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T13:55:00-07:00","id":1394143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394136#post1394136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once more, with feeling: Masquerade has <i>always </i>presented the truth as uncertain, since the very first book. Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary actually does a good job of closing the ring with some things from the 1st edition book that people had forgotten about, and it pretty well blows up the idea of any sort of certainty. <br /> <br /> People don\u2019t need certainty and canon to have discussions. If anything, certainty makes discussion pointless. <br /> <br /> And Requiem does have a known origin for vampires at this point. The only reason it didn\u2019t initially, I think, is because Achilli got really frustrated with people treating the Caine myth in a fundamentalist fashion, so he was like \u201cFuck it, we\u2019re not giving you anything this time.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you say that, the VtR foruns in this own website were left with flys. No one have a motive to start a topic, whatever reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T14:08:33-07:00","id":1394147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394142#post1394142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I've been playing since 1994, I have opinions on all of the Clans.<br /> <br /> Usually, I think my ideas are the normal ones. Like I said, I was all for the Dark Ages knightly lord and ladies Tzimisce. I was surprised to find people liked the crazy inhuman ones over these.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019ve always had an edge to them, but 500 years of being aligned with the Sabbat hasn\u2019t done them any favors. I think it\u2019s meant to be pretty clear they\u2019ve fallen into extreme decadence in the modern nights. <br /> <br /> But be that as it may, for a lot of people their appeal really does begin and end with the body horror. But in order to be a proper clan they do need more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T14:16:58-07:00","id":1394149,"title":"","content":"I probably think my Tremere, Malkavian, and Thin Bloods are the most extreme.<br /> <br /> I also have a very interesting belief on the Followers of Set vs. Lasombra regarding religion but that's something that's just my preference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2020, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T14:49:51-07:00","id":1394152,"title":"","content":"Vicissitude is the most interesting discipline in the game, bar Thaumaturgy if you start looking up the theory. Offering the elderly their youths back, provided they agree to a life of servitude. Giving a rapist a sex change, providing collector's items for exotic aquariums, falsifying marks of infernalism... You can do some wonderfully weird things with Vicissitude. Vicissitude, like dominate, is good, but in the hands of a creative player, it's godly fun. It's also super interesting in that there's a moral argument for it with some thinking it's just an evil-alien-societal menace and another progressive line of thought. <br /> <br /> Vicissitude is a discipline you can build a character around. Aside from sorcerers and a few lasombra that go all-in on the abyss weirdness, most clan specifics are highly specialised abilities that are useful but not core to a character; An Assamite doesn't need Quietus to poison folk, a Ravnos doesn't need chimestry to decieve, A Gangrel doesn't really need potence to survive the woods, it just makes it easier. A vampire surgeon can't do anything to another vampire, and they'd need centuries to be able to do the things they'd be able to do with vicissitude after a decade. Vicissitude lets anyone be an artist, a transhumanist... Like, sure, mundane skills are super helpful and at times necessary, but Vicissitude is like photoshop in a world where doctors can only fingerpaint (What an Ironic analogy)<br /> <br /> Tzmisce are weird doctors that forgo regular equipment for a jar of dirt. That to me is very much more interesting than Ventrue B<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T14:50:43-07:00","id":1394153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394142#post1394142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I've been playing since 1994, I have opinions on all of the Clans.<br /> <br /> Usually, I think my ideas are the normal ones. Like I said, I was all for the Dark Ages knightly lord and ladies Tzimisce. I was surprised to find people liked the crazy inhuman ones over these.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the crazy inhuman ones where new (at least to me, found Necroscope after I had been playing VtM for years) every other clan was a story I knew, apart from the Tzim, and to an extent the Lasombra, so to me those were the VtM clans, I later found Necroscope for the Tzims inspiration, but they still had this warped Transhumanism going on, and mad scientist vibe, and since I love Transhumanism and Futurism, seeing a messed up Vampiric version was cool, and a story hook I could really get my teeth into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:08:09-07:00","id":1394157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394153#post1394153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because the crazy inhuman ones where new (at least to me, found Necroscope after I had been playing VtM for years) every other clan was a story I knew, apart from the Tzim, and to an extent the Lasombra, so to me those were the VtM clans, I later found Necroscope for the Tzims inspiration, but they still had this warped Transhumanism going on, and mad scientist vibe, and since I love Transhumanism and Futurism, seeing a messed up Vampiric version was cool, and a story hook I could really get my teeth into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly valid, Taggie.<br /> <br /> In my case, when I first played V:TM, I wanted to play a vampire who was an Old World aristocrat and all manner of creepy yet honorable. None of the Clans could really pull off what I wanted from them and I was disappointed to find out the Tzimisce were even less prevalant in the Camarilla than the Lasombra. It wasn't until Vampire: The Dark Ages that I really got to cut loose with the kind of dark and supernatural nobleman that I wanted to be.<br /> <br /> Which is the point of the Clans really.<br /> <br /> Something for everyone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:13:20-07:00","id":1394159,"title":"","content":"You can play a creepy yet honourable old world Aristocrat with literally every clan (The Ravnos may be a challenge)<br /> But I'm glad that you found your very specific niche in a very specifically set up clan.<br /> <br /> Edit: <br /> The Core clans are nonspecific enough that you can cover basically any kind of person with one of them. Your only problem is specific powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-04-2020, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:20:37-07:00","id":1394162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394159#post1394159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can play a creepy yet honourable old world Aristocrat with literally every clan (The Ravnos may be a challenge)<br /> But I'm glad that you found your very specific niche in a very specifically set up clan.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> The Core clans are nonspecific enough that you can cover basically any kind of person with one of them. Your only problem is specific powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and you could have Vicissitude as done by a Toreador or Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> That isn't the same from your perspective anymore than the reverse for me.<br /> <br /> My opinion, and JUST MY OPINION, is that the Clan Culture is the most important element of any clan. What kind of Kine does this Clan Embrace, what kind of people do they support, how do they interact, and how do you fit into the larger community? Disciplines are secondary to that because any vampire can learn any discipline eventually.<br /> <br /> A Nosferatu Voivode will always be different from a Ventrue, Toreador, or Tzimisce one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2020, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:21:19-07:00","id":1394163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394157#post1394157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perfectly valid, Taggie.<br /> <br /> In my case, when I first played V:TM, I wanted to play a vampire who was an Old World aristocrat and all manner of creepy yet honorable. None of the Clans could really pull off what I wanted from them and I was disappointed to find out the Tzimisce were even less prevalant in the Camarilla than the Lasombra. It wasn't until Vampire: The Dark Ages that I really got to cut loose with the kind of dark and supernatural nobleman that I wanted to be.<br /> <br /> Which is the point of the Clans really.<br /> <br /> Something for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have done Tzim nobles in DA. Road of the Adversary/Devil for a particular fun character, was an utter asshole focused on bringing enlightenment and freedom to the world...he was also 6th Generation, and had been a Knight, so could argue like a scholar,or cut you to dog food, your choice. (The ST made everyone 6th had us agree a clan, made our sire, and off we tore through the Translyvania Chronicles, he picked 6th so we wouldn't be looking to diablerie as a career path)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:26:38-07:00","id":1394166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394163#post1394163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have done Tzim nobles in DA. Road of the Adversary/Devil for a particular fun character, was an utter asshole focused on bringing enlightenment and freedom to the world...he was also 6th Generation, and had been a Knight, so could argue like a scholar,or cut you to dog food, your choice. (The ST made everyone 6th had us agree a clan, made our sire, and off we tore through the Translyvania Chronicles, he picked 6th so we wouldn't be looking to diablerie as a career path)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a fascinating character. Interestingly, one of the PCs in our current game (that I'm STing) is a Tzimisce Ninja and the Toreador Doctor is begging her to teach him Vicissitude so he can use it to save lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:29:56-07:00","id":1394167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394134#post1394134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the idea of eliminating the Venture in favor of the Tzimisce (and maybe the Lasombra) is actually kind of cool. When they came out with V:tR, they did away with the Lasombra and Tzimisce, perhaps with the implication that those concepts should fit into the new Ventrue Clan. Though that just makes everything a bit too generic. It V:tM is to be streamlined, maybe it would be cooler to get rid of the Ventrue in exchange for two leadership Clans, the Tzimisce and the Lasombra. Tzimisce to represent old fashioned leadership with a strict sense of honor, a tie to the land, and so on; while the Lasombra are the ruthless social darwinists who have no honor or adherence to any strict hierarchy, anyone who earns it has a place on top. Having those two archetypes actually lessons the need for a generic leadership Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see Requiem's Ventrue as a fairly even mixture of Lasombra, Tzimisce and Ventrue without the weirder disciplines. It's been said that their raison d'etre isn't so much about ruling as winning. As blank as Ventrue look next to Sabbat and Independent clans, they do have a relatively tightly knit culture, which isn't how any Requiem clan functions. They aren't the clan with Majesty, so they lack the personal appeal of VtM Ventrue, but they do have Animalism, bringing them closer to the pre-bourgeois landed gentry concept. Speaking of which, I wouldn't reserve that concept for a single clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 06-04-2020, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:34:52-07:00","id":1394168,"title":"","content":"Um... if people don\u2019t think the Tzimisce stuff can be accomplished with Blood Sorcery, then consider the shit the Tremere have twisted other vampires into. Gargoyles, anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:39:45-07:00","id":1394171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394162#post1394162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and you could have Vicissitude as done by a Toreador or Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> That isn't the same from your perspective anymore than the reverse for me.<br /> <br /> My opinion, and JUST MY OPINION, is that the Clan Culture is the most important element of any clan. What kind of Kine does this Clan Embrace, what kind of people do they support, how do they interact, and how do you fit into the larger community? Disciplines are secondary to that because any vampire can learn any discipline eventually.<br /> <br /> A Nosferatu Voivode will always be different from a Ventrue, Toreador, or Tzimisce one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now, alright, this may kinda be wrong here because of the whole international conspiracy thing, but do you think Ventrue are the same all over the world? Do you imagine their manners are all the same? Their Rome Hardon is the same? The Ventrue of Ireland act precisely like the Ventrue of Bulgaria? I don't see why you wouldn't be able to adapt Tzmisce noble sensibilities to local ventrue. <br /> <br /> As for what kind of people they embrace? <br /> Tzmisce as a clan around Vicissitude would indeed develop their own culture. Clan disciplines and weaknesses help create and strengthen clan cultures. They would sire the intelegent, people who respect privacy or another's workspace, people who have an interest in... You can easily build a culture around Tzmisce-as-Doctors, just as easily as you can build a culture of Ventrue-As-Eastern europeans. It's a much better plan than Tzmisce as classy racist-stereotype/Ventrue as magical surgeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:41:04-07:00","id":1394172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394168#post1394168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... if people don\u2019t think the Tzimisce stuff can be accomplished with Blood Sorcery, then consider the shit the Tremere have twisted other vampires into. Gargoyles, anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Said blood sorcery literally works by capitalizing on the shape changing abilities of the three clans used in Gargoyle creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:45:40-07:00","id":1394173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394171#post1394171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now, alright, this may kinda be wrong here because of the whole international conspiracy thing, but do you think Ventrue are the same all over the world? Do you imagine their manners are all the same? Their Rome Hardon is the same? The Ventrue of Ireland act precisely like the Ventrue of Bulgaria? I don't see why you wouldn't be able to adapt Tzmisce noble sensibilities to local ventrue.<br /> <br /> As for what kind of people they embrace?<br /> Tzmisce as a clan around Vicissitude would indeed develop their own culture. Clan disciplines and weaknesses help create and strengthen clan cultures. They would sire the intelegent, people who respect privacy or another's workspace, people who have an interest in... You can easily build a culture around Tzmisce-as-Doctors, just as easily as you can build a culture of Ventrue-As-Eastern europeans.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, any given group of vampires can be different and have their own internal local culture.<br /> <br /> Take note of the Tzimisce Ninja I just mentioned. They're from Oda Nobunaga's lineage in my games.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, that requires a bunch of extra work you don't need if there's already a Clan that embodies the kind of character you want and need--like, say, the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a much better plan than Tzmisce as classy racist-stereotype/Ventrue as magical surgeon. </div> </div> </div>No Ventrue would be as awesome a nobleman as what's already written for the Tzimisce. They're just incapable of having that level of kewl. I mean, I could write them with ghoul families, ancient feuds between bloodlines and rival houses, a pagan religious history, and a slow decay from rulership of the region to a remnant of themselves....but I already have the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Mind you, you should probably just go ahead and admit that sinister Tzimisce noblemen is already a thing in the setting. It seems like you REALLY wish they weren't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Including Dracula being one of them canonically.<br /> <br /> Tell me if I'm wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2020, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:48:24-07:00","id":1394174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394168#post1394168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... if people don\u2019t think the Tzimisce stuff can be accomplished with Blood Sorcery, then consider the shit the Tremere have twisted other vampires into. Gargoyles, anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not that it could not be, that Tzimisce is Sorcery should be rare, weird and terrifying Kolduns, not every Tzimisce, also what do they loose for it? Animalism? Well their goes the command of wolves, bars etc if the Dracula myth. Auspex? Well their goes the Lord in his castle listening to rumours on the wind and reading minds, and also the Death and the Soul adherent watching for the precise point the Aura dies. So which version of Tzimisce gets thrown under the bus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:50:40-07:00","id":1394175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394174#post1394174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that it could not be, that Tzimisce is Sorcery should be rare, weird and terrifying Kolduns, not every Tzimisce, also what do they loose for it? Animalism? Well their goes the command of wolves, bars etc if the Dracula myth. Auspex? Well their goes the Lord in his castle listening to rumours on the wind and reading minds, and also the Death and the Soul adherent watching for the precise point the Aura dies. So which version of Tzimisce gets thrown under the bus?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Auspex should be the one to go. Auspex is not a power very often associated with Dracula compared to Sorcery or Animalism or Protean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T16:10:37-07:00","id":1394178,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Ventrue lack Revenants which make the Tzmisce far more interesting.<br /> But that's part of them being eugenicists<br /> <br /> Ventrue keeping highly specific herds is somewhat comparable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T18:12:54-07:00","id":1394199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394174#post1394174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that it could not be, that Tzimisce is Sorcery should be rare, weird and terrifying Kolduns, not every Tzimisce, also what do they loose for it? Animalism? Well their goes the command of wolves, bars etc if the Dracula myth. Auspex? Well their goes the Lord in his castle listening to rumours on the wind and reading minds, and also the Death and the Soul adherent watching for the precise point the Aura dies. So which version of Tzimisce gets thrown under the bus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex is dispensable. Honestly I expect they only had it because it\u2019s what they used to give all the magical clans before they just let them have blood sorcery. Nor are Paths of Enlightenment likely to be in this edition anyway. They very nearly didn\u2019t even make it into 3rd, since Achilli hated them and thought they ruined the game. They\u2019re basically a 2e contrivance that\u2019s been bedeviling developers ever since. <br /> <br /> As for Kolduns being rare, I don\u2019t think that\u2019s necessary from a design standpoint. Nor do I think you can keep setting aside rare and scary subsets of groups that are rare and scary subsets of other groups that are supposed to be rare and scary to begin with, infinitely, without it becoming a joke. A typical way of dealing with that is to generalize traits of a subgroup to the entire group. And in any case, V5 is a soft reboot, and clan-related stuff is (and has always been) prime candidate for retconning. There\u2019s zero reason to slavishly adhere to what was done previously (which itself was probably a retcon of something before it, if we\u2019re being honest).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T20:25:26-07:00","id":1394224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394199#post1394199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Auspex is dispensable. Honestly I expect they only had it because it\u2019s what they used to give all the magical clans before they just let them have blood sorcery. Nor are Paths of Enlightenment likely to be in this edition anyway. They very nearly didn\u2019t even make it into 3rd, since Achilli hated them and thought they ruined the game. They\u2019re basically a 2e contrivance that\u2019s been bedeviling developers ever since. <br /> <br /> As for Kolduns being rare, I don\u2019t think that\u2019s necessary from a design standpoint. Nor do I think you can keep setting aside rare and scary subsets of groups that are rare and scary subsets of other groups that are supposed to be rare and scary to begin with, infinitely, without it becoming a joke. A typical way of dealing with that is to generalize traits of a subgroup to the entire group. And in any case, V5 is a soft reboot, and clan-related stuff is (and has always been) prime candidate for retconning. There\u2019s zero reason to slavishly adhere to what was done previously (which itself was probably a retcon of something before it, if we\u2019re being honest).</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Paths are the main thing I like about this setting, and their lack is why I didn't move to VtR (among other things, but largest part was the Paths) I hope you are wrong. I also like the idea that sorcery isn't handed out like candy, but oh well. Guess I'll have to wait and see","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T21:32:25-07:00","id":1394233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394224#post1394224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since Paths are the main thing I like about this setting, and their lack is why I didn't move to VtR (among other things, but largest part was the Paths) I hope you are wrong. I also like the idea that sorcery isn't handed out like candy, but oh well. Guess I'll have to wait and see</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. At this point the only thing paths would (Or need) to do is replace human touchstones with something else. They do not fit the current morality system as needing a complete overhaul, and cults shows us quite well that they won't really be a thing. Like. If they were ever coming back like they were, cults would have been the book to do it as we have the Church of Caine in there. Church of Caine sample convictions include: &quot;Let nobody prevent you from growing closer to Caine&quot; which is pretty close to the level 2 of the path. &quot;Never unwillingly allow the Beast to take over&quot; level 6. &quot;Never succumb to fear&quot; Level 5. &quot;Do not consort with the lowest beings of hell&quot; Close to the level 8 sin. We literally have a cult with convictions that replicate the path of Caine. Paths are in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T21:36:47-07:00","id":1394235,"title":"","content":"I've never really associated Auspex with the Tzimisce, despite it being one of their Disciplines since forever. I'd favor Animalism, Blood Sorcery, and Protean as well - of course with their own unique Protean powers combined with Blood Sorcery to emulate some interesting Vicissitude powers. <br /> <br /> Revenants are indeed one of the things I like the most about the Tzimisce, they really fascinate me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T21:49:44-07:00","id":1394238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394233#post1394233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean. At this point the only thing paths would (Or need) to do is replace human touchstones with something else. They do not fit the current morality system as needing a complete overhaul, and cults shows us quite well that they won't really be a thing. Like. If they were ever coming back like they were, cults would have been the book to do it as we have the Church of Caine in there. Church of Caine sample convictions include: &quot;Let nobody prevent you from growing closer to Caine&quot; which is pretty close to the level 2 of the path. &quot;Never unwillingly allow the Beast to take over&quot; level 6. &quot;Never succumb to fear&quot; Level 5. &quot;Do not consort with the lowest beings of hell&quot; Close to the level 8 sin. We literally have a cult with convictions that replicate the path of Caine. Paths are in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they want to win over <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a> then they'll probably have to say you can substitute your homebrewed Path and its Convictions for Humanity. But I wouldn't be surprised if they did that with a full Touchstone overhaul in the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> Take up to 5 Convictions or so and have Touchstones that can be vampires, supes, places, and objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T21:57:05-07:00","id":1394239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394149#post1394149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably think my Tremere, Malkavian, and Thin Bloods are the most extreme.<br /> <br /> I also have a very interesting belief on the Followers of Set vs. Lasombra regarding religion but that's something that's just my preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm curious. What is your interpretation of those Clans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:18:53-07:00","id":1394241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394239#post1394239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now I'm curious. What is your interpretation of those Clans?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><u>Take note this is only true in my home games and I never would argue this is true in canon. Let's head off any worries I'm misinterpreting these clans on these forums. I do not bring my fanon into my canon discussions.</u></b></span><br /> <br /> 1. <b>Tremere</b>: I generally treated the Tremere as a ticking time bomb of intrigue, infighting, and suppressed rage in the Pre-V5 universe. They are constantly jockeying for power, fighting duels, plotting against one another, and following a Social Darwinist philosophy imposed by the Council of Seven. They're all Blood Bound to the 7 and the 7 have the power to destroy you at any time because they have samples of your blood like in Dragon Age. Their superiors also regularly use Dominate on their lessers and condition them to obey unlike the majority of Kindred. Expect to have your thoughts read regularly too. It's really a kind of hellish existence and it's severely lacking in freedom. I draw from Psi-Corp in Babylon Five and the Sith from The Old Republic. &quot;I have no mouth but I must scream&quot; is painted on the souls of any Tremere who would resist their superior.<br /> <br /> It was, in simple terms, a cult in the classical sense that broke you down and rebuilt you -- whether you wanted it to or not.<br /> <br /> So when the Council of Seven were destroyed, it was an explosion of in-fighting, Civil War, and settling old debts as well as people who were like, &quot;I AM FREE AT LAST! FREE!&quot; Sometimes people who you would have never suspected were chomping at the bit themselves. The Tremere are now rebuilding but are a little confused, really, because so many of them aren't the same sorts of people without the Blood Bond (plus excessive use of Dominate) dominating their every thought. It's left them weak politically and disunited but they're now expanding and far more willing to fight than they once were. Its honestly shocked a lot of vampires too because so few of them realized what was festering under their robes.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Malkavians</b>: I tend to go with the view that Malkavians are not often as overtly insane as many appear but they're actually just &quot;weird&quot; and that is confused as insanity. A large percentage (maybe 40%) Malkavian derangements are some combination of emotional instability, paranoia, narcissism, sanguinary obsession, and psychopathic lack of empathy. The thing is that actually just means they're not that different from a typical Elder. So almost half of the clan is NOT insane from the perspective of your typical vampire. A Malkavian with rage issues is basically indistinguishable from a Brujah. The other 60% may have hallucinations, schizophrenia, and multiple personalities but they are normal &quot;most&quot; of the time.<br /> <br /> Malkavian CLAN CULTURE on the other hand is based around gestalt consciousness, prophecy, religious ecstasy, pushing the boundaries of consciousness, and serving as the gadfly of Kindred society. This is what Kindred assume is the Malkavian derangements when it's actually their culture of being a bunch of psychedelic hippies as well as religious mystics.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Thin Bloods</b>: I heavily emphasize that Thin Bloods are humans with fangs. They are a subject of both envy and loathing of other vampires. Whatever the Curse of Caine has done to vampires, torturing their souls and leaving them shells of who they were, Thin Bloods are...not. They are people with more or less the same spirits and souls they had in life. Hell, they aren't even undead. Not really. This means that they can maintain the Humanity of regular people and live the normal life a Kindred can't. It means that other Kindred may want to protect them to save what little remains of their souls or destroy them because of jealousy. They're perfect for being Friendly Neighborhood Vampires because they're the only vampires who can be really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:33:48-07:00","id":1394243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game without the truth about vampire origins already exists: VtR.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's ONE of the things that VTR got right. The whole Caine stuff with the Abrahamic themes is annoying nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:34:42-07:00","id":1394244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394243#post1394243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's ONE of the things that VTR got right. The whole Caine stuff with the Abrahamic themes is annoying nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's, of course, one of my favorite parts.<br /> <br /> Let me guess, you're not a big fan of a game being about being damned and tortured by the weight of your sins either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:44:08-07:00","id":1394245,"title":"","content":"No, I'm not a fan of the entire line being bogged down to a point where Vampires get like this due to the &quot;generation&quot; shtick:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're perfect for being Friendly Neighborhood Vampires because they're the only vampires who can be really.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the meta edging closer and closer in the Modern Nights to have PC characters be such high generations like that? Might as well play Sims 3. It's not even a curse anymore, just Twilight.<br /> <br /> The whole Caine thing is really annoying. Basically Caine is the main character of VTM. The only thing he has going for him is the he's a &quot;le biblique character xDDDDD&quot; and nothing else, and that he is the &quot;first murderer&quot;. Caine being the center of Vampires when I got first introduced into VTM was cool. Then the effect wore off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-05-2020, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:45:57-07:00","id":1394246,"title":"","content":"Oh, someone asked me what my difference between Lasombra and Followers of Set were. Since this WAS a Lasombra thread, I'll share it.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra vs. Followers of Set</b><br /> <br /> <u>At my home table</u> these are the two &quot;Clans of Faith&quot; and come at it from very different perspectives. So much so that the two have almost nothing in common once you get down to it.<br /> <br /> For the Lasombra, Faith is a tool. They manipulate it, weave it, and export it. Lasombra are involved in televangelism, megachurches, Faith-based lobbying, and behind every single Catholic Priest who has a dirty little secret. They love creating cults but they are cults that exist solely to make sure that young beautiful vessels service the leader while older members empty their pocket-books. Some Lasombra sincerely believe but for the vast majority of them, religion is very much the opiate of the masses. It's a scam that they milk for all of its worth.<br /> <br /> This is, to an extent part of their problem in V5 because the Sabbat is their magnum opus for creating a religion that is complete bullshit as far as 80% of the Lasombra is concerned. They don't believe in Caine, are quite confidant Gehenna is a lie (they killed their Antediluvian after all), and use the Antitribu as a bunch of cannon fodder. Because that's what they are. The Tzimisce are the only clan they even remotely respect and the Lasombra assumed they were in on the scam.<br /> <br /> That's why the Gehenna Crusade horrified them, not necessarily because of the fact that it happened. The Lasombra were expecting to head to the desert, kill some Ashirra, dig up some temples, and call it a day. No, the problem was THEY FOUND OUT THEIR RELIGION WAS REAL and it has TERRIFIED them.<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set/Ministry have a very simple difference from the Lasombra in this respect. <u>They believe</u>. The Followers of Set will set up a cult, they will fill it with blood bonds, sexual drug orgies, and they will set themselves up as gods to be worshiped with sex slaves as well as cash. Just like the Lasombra. The thing is the FoS are of the mind that they are doing this for the greater glory of whatever god they venerate. It's a means to an end of enlightenment that they would drop if they didn't feel it was working. The Followers of Set all start at the bottom of their cults and they work their way up. Some faster than others but their worshipers aren't rubes. They are actual members of the flock.<br /> <br /> The scary thing that the Followers of Set provide that almost no other Kindred Clan does is certainty and genuine community. They are prepared to give their unlives for the Cause, just like the Sabbat, and its with full knowledge that it is for the greater Kingdom of Darkness ahead.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons why making a deal with the Setites is so dangerous. Because they're not actually trying to scam you. When you're lost, alone, and don't have a friend in the world--the Setites will be there for you. Not because they're trying to trick or entrap you but because they KNOW their unlife is better and want to share it with you.<br /> <br /> It's just that the thing they're sharing is the god the Devil prays to.<br /> <br /> Lasombra are Jim Baker and Falwell, Followers of Set are Masada zealots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:48:49-07:00","id":1394247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394245#post1394245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the meta edging closer and closer in the Modern Nights to have PC characters be such high generations like that? Might as well play Sims 3. It's not even a curse anymore, just Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you don't get to have any of that sweet sweet immortality with the benefit of still being able to enjoy sunlight [or at least awake during the day], love, and family. You are stuck being a lower generation damned corpse.<br /> <br /> Hence the contrast.<br /> <br /> The Thin Bloods, by contrast, are Almost Human and that means their lives are subject to constant hunting by regular Kindred who want to exterminate them. They can ally with sympathetic Kindred but--really--they're a bunch of damned corpses themselves still.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole Caine thing is really annoying. Basically Caine is the main character of VTM. The only thing he has going for him is the he's a &quot;le biblique character xDDDDD&quot; and nothing else, and that he is the &quot;first murderer&quot;. Caine being the center of Vampires when I got first introduced into VTM was cool. Then the effect wore off. </div> </div> </div>I love the Caine of THE BOOK OF NOD because his story is much-much deeper and longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:50:02-07:00","id":1394248,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks. I'm always interesting in seeing alternative takes on official settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:50:31-07:00","id":1394249,"title":"","content":"Wait, what are you talking about? Your talking about Vampires, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thin Bloods, by contrast, are Almost Human and that means their lives are subject to constant hunting by regular Kindred who want to exterminate them. They can ally with sympathetic Kindred but--really--they're a bunch of damned corpses themselves still.</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Oh you edited in your reply. To respond: No, just no. When ANY Vampire setting gets to the &quot;almost human&quot; stage anywhere, it becomes trash. Thin-Bloods aren't interesting. They add nothing to the game. Thin-Blood Alchemy was only ever added in to make them palpable.. for the some who even bother to play them. They aren't even supposed to be viable by any circumstance Pre-V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-05-2020, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:55:10-07:00","id":1394252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394249#post1394249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what are you talking about? Your talking about Vampires, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rephrased:<br /> <br /> * Thin Bloods have very few vampire powers but far less of the weaknesses. They are able to live mostly normal lives. This means other vampires hunt them relentlessly and try to destroy them or feed on them.<br /> * Regular vampires are possessed of far worse weaknesses and a much stronger Beast. They can never live normal lives and this means Thin Bloods piss them off. They also have a variety of reasons to hunt them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394249#post1394249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what are you talking about? Your talking about Vampires, right?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh you edited in your reply. To respond: No, just no. When ANY Vampire setting gets to the &quot;almost human&quot; stage anywhere, it becomes trash. Thin-Bloods aren't interesting. They add nothing to the game. Thin-Blood Alchemy was only ever added in to make them palpable.. for the some who even bother to play them. They aren't even supposed to be viable by any circumstance Pre-V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you don't get what I'm going for with them. But you may just not like it. Suit yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T23:10:58-07:00","id":1394255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394097#post1394097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is slightly tiring and increasingly annoying to have to say again and again that nowhere, nowhere except in Demon: the Fallen (and not even there), has been absolutely established in-universe that Caine's story is truth and not myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about? Did you even read the DTF Core? The Narrator of the story part of the book is literally a Demon. Not only that Caine was the cataclyst for the Demons being able to fight fully &quot;instead of multiple layer reality fighting&quot; (lol) where on multiple layers they could &quot;pre-predict&quot; on who would win a bout with one another just from angling their swords (lmao).<br /> <br /> The Core, EXPLICITLY SAYS the act of Caine killing &quot;liberalized&quot; them to begin fighting for real. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Fallen, Chapter 2, pg. 51</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sheer savagery of the assault stunned the Host. Many of its highest generals, Michael, Gabriel, Uriel and Raphael, were absent, sent by God to punish Caine for his sin. But this was not all. The death of Abel had washed over the Host much like it had among the fallen. Yet, where it seemed to have liberated us, it had paralyzed the angels. They were unable to comprehend the evil that had been unleashed before them. This proved to be their undoing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah, who would've thought that the entire gameline focusing on hamfisting Abrahamic style Demons into oWoD would canonize Caine? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T23:19:51-07:00","id":1394256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394255#post1394255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, who would've thought that the entire gameline focusing on hamfisting Abrahamic style Demons into oWoD would canonize Caine?</div> </div> </div> </div>I felt he was canonized by the fact he shows up as a taxi driver in Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> And hamfisting?<br /> <br /> Demons have been a major part of the WOD since 1st Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T23:20:32-07:00","id":1394257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394233#post1394233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean. At this point the only thing paths would (Or need) to do is replace human touchstones with something else. They do not fit the current morality system as needing a complete overhaul, and cults shows us quite well that they won't really be a thing. Like. If they were ever coming back like they were, cults would have been the book to do it as we have the Church of Caine in there. Church of Caine sample convictions include: &amp;quot;Let nobody prevent you from growing closer to Caine&amp;quot; which is pretty close to the level 2 of the path. &amp;quot;Never unwillingly allow the Beast to take over&amp;quot; level 6. &amp;quot;Never succumb to fear&amp;quot; Level 5. &amp;quot;Do not consort with the lowest beings of hell&amp;quot; Close to the level 8 sin. We literally have a cult with convictions that replicate the path of Caine. Paths are in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not granular enough, not hard enough, no degeneration track, 3 convictions isn't enough, Touchstones are a major flaw. So no, in no way do the cults as described come anywhere near the Paths . They sound.flat, simple and uninteresting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T23:22:08-07:00","id":1394258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394257#post1394257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not granular enough, not hard enough, no degeneration track, 3 convictions isn't enough, Touchstones are a major flaw. So no, in no way do the cults as described come anywhere near the Paths . <b>They sound.flat, simple and uninteresting</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a rather large assumption to make given he was listing tenets from Paths and the fact you haven't read the book. You don't have to read them but please don't comment on them until you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath