ess of a concrete answer than other lines.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T01:45:37-07:00","id":1394285,"title":"","content":"As I said, that is right too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T01:51:10-07:00","id":1394286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394276#post1394276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Up to you. I just don't see any reason why vampires would have less of a concrete answer than other lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it for five minutes, while I make a pause between correcting an exam and the next one, I would say that I like that option because we, as human players, don't have a bona-fide 100% knowledge of 'who' or 'what' created us, and vampires shouldn't be any different.<br /> <br /> In fact, one could argue that even Werewolves could have been deluded by the Wyrm for millennia and everything in the World of Darkness is a huge cosmic joke played on humanity by Coyote...<br /> But that way lies the lying god of Descartes, the Demiurge, and madness and skepticism... ok, I'm ranting now.<br /> <br /> (Wow... this thread has gone a long way away from the Lasombra... I wouldn't say it isn't being hugely interesting, however...)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T02:27:29-07:00","id":1394288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394199#post1394199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex is dispensable. Honestly I expect they only had it because it\u2019s what they used to give all the magical clans before they just let them have blood sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex was there because the <i>Necroscope</i> Wamphyri are telepathic.<br /> <br /> I suppose I sound like a broken record at this point. It's just strange to me how people don't seem to care why something was designed the way that it was. It's typical for any long-standing game line: Just keep repurposing, readjusting, and regurgitating elements of the game while completely losing the reason why something was put in the game in the first place. I honestly don't get why someone would insist on using the Tzimisce in the game, only to completely ditch their original identity and repurpose them as the &quot;Dracula Clan.&quot; That dude doesn't <i>need</i> a clan. It's obvious that Dracula's classic powers were split between the 10 original 1st Edition disciplines. You can do Dracula with just about any existing clan, from Ventrue to Gangrel to Tremere.<br /> <br /> (Of course I know that Dracula was pegged as Tzimisce in 1992's <i>Children of the Inquisition.</i> But the dude didn't <i>define</i> the clan. He was explicitly presented as an independent rebel who went against typical Tzimisce conventions and behavior. And even <i>that</i> Dracula was only the second interpretation of the guy in the game line. The penitent Dracula who writes to Mina Harker in the introduction of the 1st Edition core book <i>barely even knows what shape-shifting is.</i> He's heard stories, but that's all. Not exactly the vampire superstar of 1999's <i>Children of the Night,</i> with his big dick swagger of 34 points in various disciplines, including Protean, Vicissitude, <i>and</i> Thaumaturgy.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T02:49:42-07:00","id":1394289,"title":"","content":"I feel the big Tzmisce discussion is basically the Lasombra discussion but for a different clan. The Tzmisce discussion is almost perfectly allegorical for the Lasombra. They mirror eachother in many ways, and unfortunately will likely continue to mirror eachother in V5. The two clans are like non-identical twins and where one goes, the other will move in parralel. As I don't like the direction they've taken with the lasombra, I probably won't like the direction they'll take with the Tzmisce. We have a rough idea of what's happening with the Sabbat who both clans are heavily tied to, and although I can justify it with a conspiracy theory, it's still not a good thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1190_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1190\" data-vbnamecard=\"1190\">Elphilm</a> <br /> Auspex just seems like a really good thing for a vampire surgeon to have. It also seems like a really good thing for someone who's obsessed with privacy and hospitality who doesn't want anything out of place. Whatever the Wamphyri are is irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-05-2020, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T04:10:01-07:00","id":1394294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394289#post1394289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the big Tzmisce discussion is basically the Lasombra discussion but for a different clan. The Tzmisce discussion is almost perfectly allegorical for the Lasombra. They mirror eachother in many ways, and unfortunately will likely continue to mirror eachother in V5. The two clans are like non-identical twins and where one goes, the other will move in parralel. As I don't like the direction they've taken with the lasombra, I probably won't like the direction they'll take with the Tzmisce. We have a rough idea of what's happening with the Sabbat who both clans are heavily tied to, and although I can justify it with a conspiracy theory, it's still not a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll find out when we find out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T04:26:23-07:00","id":1394296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394289#post1394289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever the Wamphyri are is irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> the real reason why the original Tzimisce disciplines were what they were, since the topic came up. Your personal take on the Tzimisce is what's completely irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T04:36:13-07:00","id":1394297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394296#post1394296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gave <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> the real reason why the original Tzimisce disciplines were what they were, since the topic came up. Your personal take on the Tzimisce is what's completely irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Opinions on a forum are never irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose I sound like a broken record at this point. It's just strange to me how people don't seem to care why something was designed the way that it was. It's typical for any long-standing game line: Just keep repurposing, readjusting, and regurgitating elements of the game while completely losing the reason why something was put in the game in the first place. I honestly don't get why someone would insist on using the Tzimisce in the game, only to completely ditch their original identity and repurpose them as the &quot;Dracula Clan.&quot; That dude doesn't <i>need</i> a clan. It's obvious that Dracula's classic powers were split between the 10 original 1st Edition disciplines. You can do Dracula with just about any existing clan, from Ventrue to Gangrel to Tremere. </div> </div> </div>This is a weird argument to make because of MULTIPLE reasons. The short version being:<br /> <br /> 1. White Wolf and Paradox don't own the Necroscope vampires of Brian Lumley. I can assure you as he is very protective of that copyright. The Tzimisce should have their own identity, however inspired.<br /> 2. The Tzimisce can't be the same as those vampires because the alien-influenced creatures do not fit into the cosmology established for the 13 Clans. Tzimisce are human-derived even if they reject it.<br /> 3. The 13 Clans are made of ARCHETYPES that exist to allow you to play whatever type of vampire you want. Brujah for Lost Boys, Ventrue for classy rich vampires, Tremere for warlock vampires, Toreador for Anne Rice, and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Of course I know that Dracula was pegged as Tzimisce in 1992's <i>Children of the Inquisition.</i> But the dude didn't <i>define</i> the clan. He was explicitly presented as an independent rebel who went against typical Tzimisce conventions and behavior. And even <i>that</i> Dracula was only the second interpretation of the guy in the game line. The penitent Dracula who writes to Mina Harker in the introduction of the 1st Edition core book <i>barely even knows what shape-shifting is.</i> He's heard stories, but that's all. Not exactly the vampire superstar of 1999's <i>Children of the Night,</i> with his big dick swagger of 34 points in various disciplines, including Protean, Vicissitude, <i>and</i> Thaumaturgy.) </div> </div> </div>And yet Dracula is the vampire that is the definitive signature character of the Clan. The one whose existence will define and does define the Tzimisce even more so than Vykos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T05:01:56-07:00","id":1394298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394297#post1394297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opinions on a forum are never irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great! I like hot wings more than hamburgers.<br /> <br /> Opinions can be irrelevant <i>within a particular topic.</i> If the topic is &quot;Why were the original Tzimisce in-clan disciplines Animalism, Auspex, and Vicissitude,&quot; it's useless to speculate about the utility of Auspex to one poster's personal take on &quot;vampire surgeons,&quot; when we <i>know</i> the actual answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. White Wolf and Paradox don't own the Necroscope vampires of Brian Lumley. I can assure you as he is very protective of that copyright. The Tzimisce should have their own identity, however inspired. </div> </div> </div>Lumley is so protective of the copyright that he hasn't batted an eyelid in the 28 years that the obvious <i>Necroscope</i> vampires have existed in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. The Tzimisce can't be the same as those vampires because the alien-influenced creatures do not fit into the cosmology established for the 13 Clans. Tzimisce are human-derived even if they reject it. </div> </div> </div>They fit just fine into the game, otherwise everything Steven C. Brown wrote about them would not produce a playable clan. You just <i>reject</i> the original Vicissitude concept, Souleaters, and everything that goes with them, but that's a personal preference, not a statement of fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. The 13 Clans are made of ARCHETYPES that exist to allow you to play whatever type of vampire you want. Brujah for Lost Boys, Ventrue for classy rich vampires, Tremere for warlock vampires, Toreador for Anne Rice, and so on. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the Tzimisce for playing <i>Necroscope</i> vampires. Exactly the equivalent to having the Toreador for playing Anne Rice vampires. I think &quot;<i>Necroscope</i> vampire&quot; is a bit of a broader concept than &quot;Dracula,&quot; who happens to be <i>one dude.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yet Dracula is the vampire that is the definitive signature character of the Clan. The one whose existence will define and does define the Tzimisce even more so than Vykos. </div> </div> </div>Which just goes to show that Dracula should never have been a character within the World of Darkness. You put that dude into any clan and he automatically becomes the signature character of the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T05:06:23-07:00","id":1394299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394298#post1394298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opinions can be irrelevant <i>within a particular topic.</i> If the topic is &quot;Why were the original Tzimisce in-clan disciplines Animalism, Auspex, and Vicissitude,&quot; it's useless to speculate about the utility of Auspex to one poster's personal take on &quot;vampire surgeons,&quot; when we <i>know</i> the actual answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and we're discussing what Disciplines are beneficial for a concept or not as they can be adjusted in the new edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lumley is so protective of the copyright that he hasn't batted an eyelid in the 28 years that the obvious <i>Necroscope</i> vampires have existed in the game. </div> </div> </div>It's not legal action but simple taste. It's awful to wholly lift a concept and not pay an author. Thankfully, Vampire: The Dark Ages spent an expansive amount of time developing the Tzimisce beyond the concept of lifting another author's work and giving them a more movie vampire character. It moved them more to an interesting archetype that wasn't really covered well before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They fit just fine into the game, otherwise everything Steven C. Brown wrote about them would not produce a playable clan. You just <i>reject</i> the original Vicissitude concept, Souleaters, and everything that goes with them, but that's a personal preference, not a statement of fact. </div> </div> </div>But Souleaters are no longer canon and haven't been since Revised.<br /> <br /> For <i>decades.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, and the Tzimisce for playing <i>Necroscope</i> vampires. Exactly the equivalent to having the Toreador for playing Anne Rice vampires. I think &quot;<i>Necroscope</i> vampire&quot; is a bit of a broader concept than &quot;Dracula,&quot; who happens to be <i>one dude.</i> </div> </div> </div>And they're NOT Necroscope vampires because they have been moved away from that concept. I hope they should complete the transformation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which just goes to show that Dracula should never have been a character within the World of Darkness. You put that dude into any clan and he automatically becomes the signature character of the clan. </div> </div> </div>Except the Tzimsice are the best clan for replicating him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T05:10:15-07:00","id":1394300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzimisce should have their own identity</div> </div> </div> </div>You say this, but then you go on and on about removing what makes them have their own identity. You want to make them cookie cutter, which most Tzimisce fans wouldn't want at all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzimisce can't be the same as those vampires because the alien-influenced creatures do not fit into the cosmology established for the 13 Clans. Tzimisce are human-derived even if they reject it</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? What does this even mean? Maybe Tzimisce has some influences from &quot;Necroscope&quot; (never heard of it until now, looked it up and its some novel series. Cool), but that doesn't mean they are remotely the same as the vampires found in that series at all (apparently their called Wamphyri(?)-). The other point you bring out, I don't understand. Who denies that Vampires are human-derived? Isn't that a prerequisite to become a Vampire? Be human- then get turned? How is that different from the Tzimisce and what does Cosmology have to do with this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The 13 Clans are made of ARCHETYPES that exist to allow you to play whatever type of vampire you want. Brujah for Lost Boys, Ventrue for classy rich vampires, Tremere for warlock vampires, Toreador for Anne Rice, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say &quot;play whatever type of vampire you want,&quot; but after that you go on with boxed in roles just because of what you perceive what a clan should be. Is this why you want Tzimisce to be scraped down so badly to more fit their archetype? Do you feel their not &quot;Dracula&quot; enough? (Which they honestly shouldn't be. That would be cliche, that Tzimisce are good as they are.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dracula is the vampire that is the definitive signature character of the Clan. The one whose existence will define and does define the Tzimisce</div> </div> </div> </div>lolno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T05:13:21-07:00","id":1394302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394300#post1394300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say this, but then you go on and on about removing what makes them have their own identity. You want to make them cookie cutter, which most Tzimisce fans wouldn't want at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> confused me by saying this before. What THE HELL Is cookie cutter about the Tzimisce? They are the most overtly awesome vampires in the game, embodying all of the crazy Strahd and Castle shit that other clans seem afraid of embracing.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/8b/d4/e3/8bd4e347e23860b9e9d397d49c7a00e8.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:26px\">Tzimisce: Fuck yeah. We OWN being vampires.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Huh? What does this even mean? Maybe Tzimisce has some influences from &quot;Necroscope&quot; (never heard of it until now, looked it up and its some novel series. Cool), but that doesn't mean they are remotely the same as the vampires found in that series at all (apparently their called Wamphyri(?)-). The other point you bring out, I don't understand. Who denies that Vampires are human-derived? Isn't that a prerequisite to become a Vampire? Be human- then get turned? How is that different from the Tzimisce and what does Cosmology have to do with this? </div> </div> </div>Your confusion here is you're agreeing with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You say &quot;play whatever type of vampire you want,&quot; but after that you go on with boxed in roles just because of what you perceive what a clan should be. Is this why you want Tzimisce to be scraped down so badly to more fit their archetype? Do you feel their not &quot;Dracula&quot; enough? (Which they honestly shouldn't be. That would be cliche, that Tzimisce are good as they are.) </div> </div> </div>I don't know what you're disagreeing with me on, seriously. The Tzimisce are awesome because they are amazingly wild, varied, and capable of doing the Dracula/Castlevania/Hellsing thing that other Clans are not.<br /> <br /> I keep hammering the Dracula point home because other clans CANT DO THAT as well as the Tzimisce. You are attacking my argument from the perspective of how I feel about Ventrue.<br /> <br /> That they're generic and uninteresting and lack anything unique.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce ooze STYLE. They are like Lando Calrissian in that they can wear a cape and make it look good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> lolno. </div> </div> </div>Admit it, no Tzimisce is as cool as Vladimir Rustovich. All others are pretenders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T05:20:59-07:00","id":1394304,"title":"","content":"But yes, I think it is kind of hilarious that the argument has essentially gone to:<br /> <br /> Modern Tzimisce vs. Dark Age Tzimisce: Which is the best pony?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/c081e330-0c12-4801-bbdf-bc11caf948b3/dcyq6be-6b585d5d-0a9d-41fc-baaf-c39cbca3a8a7.png/v1/fill/w_600,h_536,strp/count_vlad_dracula_tepes___mlp_ponified_by_sugaryicecreammlp_dcyq6be-fullview.png?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1cm46YXBwOiIsImlzcyI6InVybjphcHA6Iiwib2JqIjpbW3siaGVpZ2h0IjoiPD01MzYiLCJwYXRoIjoiXC9mXC9jMDgxZTMzMC0wYzEyLTQ4MDEtYmJkZi1iYzExY2FmOTQ4YjNcL2RjeXE2YmUtNmI1ODVkNWQtMGE5ZC00MWZjLWJhYWYtYzM5Y2JjYTNhOGE3LnBuZyIsIndpZHRoIjoiPD02MDAifV1dLCJhdWQiOlsidXJuOnNlcnZpY2U6aW1hZ2Uub3BlcmF0aW9ucyJdfQ.-u1-YnbOOkgTo-a9kIqidSkwebvMMpRydBgKmcyLOGY\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I think we know which I feel.<br /> <br /> I also think it's kind of funny that some posters seem genuinely surprised I'm such a Dark Age Tzimisce fanboy. They are my 2nd favorite Clan overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T05:26:00-07:00","id":1394305,"title":"","content":"What makes the Tzimisce interesting is that they are centered around making clay of humans. They have Reverants, War-Ghouls, Schlatza, make furniture out of people, bare an inhuman morality, etc. They built a whole Cathedral out of flesh. That's what makes them interesting.. not Dracula themes. That would be cliche. Sure they may wear some interesting clothes like Dracula, but so does every other aristocratic style Vampire in any work of fiction. The &quot;style&quot; isn't unique and doesn't warrant nuking down the Tzimisce to that cartoon level. I also don't understand how you thought I was agreeing with you at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T05:30:08-07:00","id":1394306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394305#post1394305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes the Tzimisce interesting is that they are centered around making clay of humans. They have Reverants, War-Ghouls, Schlatza, make furniture out of people, bare an inhuman morality, etc. They built a whole Cathedral out of flesh. That's what makes them interesting.. not Dracula themes. That would be cliche. Sure they may wear some interesting clothes like Dracula, but so does every other aristocratic style Vampire in any work of fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes them interesting is they are the absolute lords and masters of their domains, which includes the people. Their clan culture, their unique style of Thaumaturgy, their history, their ancient blood feuds, their Revenant families, and their role in vampire society. Yeah, I don't have anything against Vicissitude but if you ask me, &quot;Which is more interesting? Hearing about Vicissitude or the history of the Basarab Revenant Family?&quot; then I'm going to choose the latter. I love memorizing the weird, kooky, and fascinating stories of the Tzimisce as well as their relationship to the best written portion of vampire history.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/books/1173146300l/251276._SX318_.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> But they can do what you like too.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with you liking what you like, why do you have a problem with what I like?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;style&quot; isn't unique and doesn't warrant nuking down the Tzimisce to that cartoon level. I also don't understand how you thought I was agreeing with you at all. </div> </div> </div>I know your argument isn't &quot;the only thing cool about the Tzimisce is one of their disciplines&quot; but I'm trying to get into the other things that make them awesome.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is real cool and versatile but there's so much MORE to the Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T05:33:36-07:00","id":1394307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394299#post1394299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not legal action but simple taste. It's awful to wholly lift a concept and not pay an author. Thankfully, Vampire: The Dark Ages spent an expansive amount of time developing the Tzimisce beyond the concept of lifting another author's work and giving them a more movie vampire character. It moved them more to an interesting archetype that wasn't really covered well before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the whole game is awful, because the vast majority of the setting and concepts of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> were lifted wholesale from Anne Rice, Bram Stoker, George R. R. Martin, and so on. Lumley isn't even in the Top 10 list of authors White Wolf should be paying for use of intellectual property, if that really is an issue. Mark Rein-Hagen was always fond of echoing T.S. Eliot: &quot;Good writers borrow, great writers steal.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Souleaters are no longer canon and haven't been since Revised.<br /> <br /> For <i>decades.</i> </div> </div> </div>So what? Unless you're saying that the pre-Revised game was <i>unplayable</i> because of the heavy <i>Necroscope</i> influence of the Tzimisce, this isn't an argument in support of your original claim. I repeat, <i>the game works just fine even if the Tzimisce are alien-influenced creatures.</i><br /> <br /> I don't really care about what's canon or not. Canon is a useless concept in roleplaying games, where every table will inevitably adjust things as they see fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except the Tzimsice are the best clan for replicating him. </div> </div> </div>If you completely remove the original identity of the Tzimisce and replace it with what you call &quot;a more movie vampire character,&quot; sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T05:34:51-07:00","id":1394308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394307#post1394307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you completely remove the original identity of the Tzimisce and replace it with what you call &quot;a more movie vampire character,&quot; sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you played Dark Ages?<br /> <br /> Just curious.<br /> <br /> The weird argument is like there's not literally DOZENS of supplements about the Dark Ages Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Transylvania Chronicles I-IV<br /> Transylvania by Night<br /> Liege Lord and Lackey<br /> Road of Kings<br /> The Players Guide to High Clans<br /> Spoils of War<br /> Right of Princes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T06:15:05-07:00","id":1394312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394308#post1394308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you played Dark Ages?<br /> <br /> Just curious.<br /> <br /> The weird argument is like there's not literally DOZENS of supplements about the Dark Ages Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's weird to me is that you think that the Tzimisce in the Dark Ages setting somehow invalidate my point. I love the original <i>Vampire: The Dark Ages</i> game line, and think the Tzimisce there are as cool as ever. I don't even mind the inclusion of &quot;Koldunic Sorcery,&quot; at least not in its early stages, when <i>kolduns</i> were meant to be an intensely rare and dying breed even in the Dark Medieval.<br /> <br /> What I don't like is the sheer amount of late-edition cross-pollination between the medieval and the modern setting. Every concept that was cool and unique in the <i>Dark Ages</i> books is dragged kicking and screaming into the modern world -- Cappadocians, Lamia, <i>kolduns,</i> Telyavs, Warrior Salubri, the list is endless. To me it smacks of Revised-era lack of creativity and the setting starting to eat its own tail instead of producing something actually new. <br /> <br /> Case in point: What was once a unique feature of a tiny minority of Tzimisce in the Dark Medieval is now so ubiquitous that apparently the Tzimisce should just straight up be another clan of magicians in the modern nights. <s>Thaumaturgy</s> Blood Sorcery for everyone! Well, I'm not a fan. The Tzimisce had a strong identity of their own from the start. Why not make up a new clan for the new concept? Oh, that's right, because a new clan would clash with the &quot;cosmology established for the 13 clans.&quot; Maybe the intensely restrictive &quot;canon&quot; that calcified into its final stages during the Revised era is the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T06:30:22-07:00","id":1394316,"title":"","content":"Ey, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I resent that. <br /> <br /> Dracula, even gonzo Castlevenia/Strahd/Dio inspired Dracula, can be done by literally any vampire. Anyone from any clan can be <i>fabulous. </i>I'd argue Tzmisce, lacking presence, would probably be worse at it. Sure, it's more normal for them, but they can't peak-weirdo like anyone from any other clan so well. <br /> <br /> Also Vicissitude is kinda really great for filling your castle with monsters. Much better than Dominate. Necromancy is cool, but Necromancy is only cooler when combined with Vicissitude. Tzmisce without vicissitude are like... How can I articulate this... Just another vampire group that doesn't strongly represent anything relevant in society to an equal or greater extent than any other clan. They're malkavians that prefer animals to staying hidden, they're Joe Exotic with less charisma and more intellegence... <br /> <br /> They can't really do anything a different clan couldn't do better. That's not <i>terrible. </i>but they're basically carried by clan culture which could be imitated by anyone else...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T06:41:47-07:00","id":1394321,"title":"","content":"Does anyone want to remove Vicissitude?<br /> <br /> Isn't the argument just to break up its powers among multiple sources?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T06:57:08-07:00","id":1394323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the argument just to break up its powers among multiple sources?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's YOUR argument and notion. Making Vicissitude &quot;to break up its powers among multiple sources&quot; isn't keeping it at all. It's removing/retgoning it (Protean splattered into Vicissitude? lmao)- just like the fate Obtenebration, Serpentis, and the various Necromancy paths suffered through in V5. Vicissitude is its OWN ability, doing what you suggest <i>IS</i> removing it and would be a disaster on an unimaginable scale for everyone who loves the Tzimisce. So shrugging it off like you DON'T want to remove it, but flip it toward &quot;amalgamation&quot; doesn't make sense to me- clearly you want it gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T06:58:47-07:00","id":1394324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394323#post1394323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's YOUR argument and notion. Making Vicissitude &quot;to break up its powers among multiple sources&quot; isn't keeping it at all. It's removing/retgoning it (Protean splattered into Vicissitude? lmao)- just like the fate Obtenebration, Serpentis, and the various Necromancy paths suffered through in V5. Vicissitude is its OWN ability, doing what you suggest <i>IS</i> removing it and would be a disaster on an unimaginable scale for everyone who loves the Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's retconned/removed except for having all the same powers available?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So shrugging it off like you DON'T want to remove it, but flip it toward &quot;amalgamation&quot; doesn't make sense to me- clearly you want it gone. </div> </div> </div>What?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <b>My View of Vicissitude</b><br /> <br /> I feel like Vicissitude has always been in need of a tweak gameplay-wise for balance issues. Vampires should be able to affect themselves with Vicissitude but flesh-crafting others should be a higher-level ability, especially if it's supposed to be permanent. I think the best way to handle it would be to combine the Path of Biothaumaturgical Experimentation and Vicissitude so that affecting the appearance of someone else requires a laboratory/torture chamber so that the various horrors and monsters that the Tzimisce are famous for can be created.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it's always been established that the more elaborate Tzimisce creations like vozhd require knowledge of Koldunism to create. Those who think they could create a human centipede with just Vicissitude are ignoring the text of the game. Mind you, I am biased as the Path of Biothaumaturgical Experimentation is something my characters have always loved and the most underrated path. It should absolutely be a Tzimisce-exclusive Path (or maybe Tzimisce/Tremere since Gargoyles exist) and its Path levels adapted to rituals for V5.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Biothaumaturgic_Experimentation\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bi...xperimentation</a><br /> <br /> I don't know if they're going to do it this way for the Tzimisce but I hope they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T07:05:15-07:00","id":1394328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394321#post1394321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone want to remove Vicissitude?<br /> <br /> Isn't the argument just to break up its powers among multiple sources?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because nothing says elegant game design like requiring 2 dots in Animalism, 3 in Protean, 2 amalgam powers and reciting a little prayer to get the same basic functionality you previously had by just writing Vicissitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 on your character sheet.<br /> <br /> Admittedly I just don't understand the aggressive consolidation of disciplines in V5. My eyes nearly bugged out of my head when I saw that the vaunted Oblivion discipline was not, in fact, a harmonious blend between old Necromancy and Obtenebration, but two different progressions awkwardly stapled together into standard powers and &quot;ceremonies,&quot; with strict prerequisites for the latter. So... what was gained, exactly? How is it cleaner to have this mess instead of Necromancy and Obtenebration as separate disciplines, each oozing with unique flavor?<br /> <br /> Are people just really tired of pronouncing Obtenebration at the table? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T07:15:03-07:00","id":1394334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394328#post1394328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because nothing says elegant game design like requiring 2 dots in Animalism, 3 in Protean, 2 amalgam powers and reciting a little prayer to get the same basic functionality you previously had by just writing Vicissitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 on your character sheet.<br /> <br /> Admittedly I just don't understand the aggressive consolidation of disciplines in V5. My eyes nearly bugged out of my head when I saw that the vaunted Oblivion discipline was not, in fact, a harmonious blend between old Necromancy and Obtenebration, but two different progressions awkwardly stapled together into standard powers and &quot;ceremonies,&quot; with strict prerequisites for the latter. So... what was gained, exactly? How is it cleaner to have this mess instead of Necromancy and Obtenebration as separate disciplines, each oozing with unique flavor?<br /> <br /> Are people just really tired of pronouncing Obtenebration at the table? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was never about consolidation but individualization. Every vampire could and should have a variety of powers and be encouraged to come up with their own.<br /> <br /> Say, my Malkavian guy can now have:<br /> <br /> * Eyes of Chaos<br /> ** Mesmerization<br /> *** Memory Alteration<br /> **** Induce Insanity<br /> ***** Mass Hallucinations","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T07:23:35-07:00","id":1394335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394316#post1394316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ey, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I resent that.<br /> <br /> Dracula, even gonzo Castlevenia/Strahd/Dio inspired Dracula, can be done by literally any vampire. Anyone from any clan can be <i>fabulous. </i>I'd argue Tzmisce, lacking presence, would probably be worse at it. Sure, it's more normal for them, but they can't peak-weirdo like anyone from any other clan so well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that it's not the CULTURE of the vampire Clan if you make Dracula into any vampire. He's just an individual vampire. You won't be dealing with a specific character who interacts with other characters like him or the history of the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> When I use Dracula as shorthand for the Tzimisce, he's not JUST Dracula but a variety of dark nobility figures who have been established in game.<br /> <br /> My favorite Tzimisce right now? What We Do in the Shadows.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.indiewire.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/What-We-Do-in-the-Shadows-Episode-7.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> When I think Tzimisce, I think:<br /> <br /> * What We Do in the Shadows<br /> * Hellsing<br /> * Castlevania<br /> * Classic movie Dracula<br /> * The Count von Count (away demon puppet!)<br /> * David Xanatos (odd choice but you see it, right)<br /> * Batman (Lord of his domain, brooding, insane old aristocrat, Bat motiffs)<br /> * Vampire Hunter D<br /> * Ramsay and Roose Bolton<br /> <br /> So I think of a variety of Lords, Ladies, and Aristocrats of the Night.<br /> <br /> It's not JUST Dracula.<br /> <br /> It's the creepy rituals, the occult monsters, the ancient decaying power, and the out of touch timelessness. The inhumanity and nobility mixed in one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394312#post1394312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's weird to me is that you think that the Tzimisce in the Dark Ages setting somehow invalidate my point. I love the original <i>Vampire: The Dark Ages</i> game line, and think the Tzimisce there are as cool as ever. I don't even mind the inclusion of &quot;Koldunic Sorcery,&quot; at least not in its early stages, when <i>kolduns</i> were meant to be an intensely rare and dying breed even in the Dark Medieval.<br /> <br /> <b>What I don't like is the sheer amount of late-edition cross-pollination between the medieval and the modern setting. Every concept that was cool and unique in the <i>Dark Ages</i> books is dragged kicking and screaming into the modern world -- Cappadocians, Lamia, <i>kolduns,</i> Telyavs, Warrior Salubri, the list is endless. To me it smacks of Revised-era lack of creativity and the setting starting to eat its own tail instead of producing something actually new.</b><br /> <br /> Case in point: What was once a unique feature of a tiny minority of Tzimisce in the Dark Medieval is now so ubiquitous that apparently the Tzimisce should just straight up be another clan of magicians in the modern nights. <s>Thaumaturgy</s> Blood Sorcery for everyone! Well, I'm not a fan. The Tzimisce had a strong identity of their own from the start. Why not make up a new clan for the new concept? Oh, that's right, because a new clan would clash with the &quot;cosmology established for the 13 clans.&quot; Maybe the intensely restrictive &quot;canon&quot; that calcified into its final stages during the Revised era is the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.<br /> <br /> Honestly, V5's entire metaplot is basically just The First Anarch Revolt/Inquisition 2.0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T07:41:16-07:00","id":1394337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394334#post1394334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought it was never about consolidation but individualization. Every vampire could and should have a variety of powers and be encouraged to come up with their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus fuck, No. Absolutely not. Insert a thousand ad hominems I can't get away with here because I'm just so infuriated with the idea. But then I get more infuriated because if i really discuss this, despite plans to keep it entirely civil, I'll be roped in for &quot;Edition warring&quot; or some other invented nonsense.<br /> <br /> 1: Disciplines are meant to be static. That's the lore. Ratings of 1-5 are planned out for you by God/Lilith/Caine/The Antes, and it's only when you can surpass the normal limits of the fifth level and enter the sixth level that you can do your own things.<br /> 2: Per dot, you achieve a lot less with V5 disciplines. So, whilst you might look at Auspex and &quot;Individualize&quot; yourself with Hightened senses or Sense the Unseen or precognition, you'd get <i>i</i>all of that with just one level of Auspex in prior editions. Old potence let you achieve a lot more just by being a simple strength enhancment than it does being the complex mess of unreasonably specific strength-inspired powers. <br /> 3: Learning, Choosing and Remembering the V5 powers is a lot more effort than it was in VTM. And I don't know about you, but vampires 'planning' their disciplines out and unlocking the same powers at different levels seems a little off. It's a lot more intuitive and easy to just have players go 1,2,3,4,5. Especially because in prior editions most powers built on top of what could be done with the prior power, whilst in V5 it's everywhere.<br /> 4: The Five power limit is extremely problematic in building characters. Also it has entirely fucked up sorcery.<br /> 5: Amalgamated disciplines deny payer opportunities thanks to the five power limit.<br /> 6: Amalgamated disciplines kill the mystery of disciplines.<br /> 7: encouraging <i>all </i>players to make up their own powers leads to more problems than benefits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vicissitude becoming Protean is just bad.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to balance Vicissitude, make it so that permanent body modification requires time to apply, so you can't just permanently disfigure someone with a tuck, you've gotta spend time weaving your change into their very being. If you've got enough opportunity to grant someone a permanent modification, you also had the opportunity to inflict final death on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-05-2020, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T07:47:06-07:00","id":1394341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394337#post1394337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus fuck, No. Absolutely not. Insert a thousand ad hominems I can't get away with here because I'm just so infuriated with the idea. But then I get more infuriated because if i really discuss this, despite plans to keep it entirely civil, I'll be roped in for &quot;Edition warring&quot; or some other invented nonsense.<br /> <br /> 1: Disciplines are meant to be static. That's the lore. Ratings of 1-5 are planned out for you by God/Lilith/Caine/The Antes, and it's only when you can surpass the normal limits of the fifth level and enter the sixth level that you can do your own things.<br /> 2: Per dot, you achieve a lot less with V5 disciplines. So, whilst you might look at Auspex and &quot;Individualize&quot; yourself with Hightened senses or Sense the Unseen or precognition, you'd get <i>i</i>all of that with just one level of Auspex in prior editions. Old potence let you achieve a lot more just by being a simple strength enhancment than it does being the complex mess of unreasonably specific strength-inspired powers.<br /> 3: Learning, Choosing and Remembering the V5 powers is a lot more effort than it was in VTM. And I don't know about you, but vampires 'planning' their disciplines out and unlocking the same powers at different levels seems a little off. It's a lot more intuitive and easy to just have players go 1,2,3,4,5. Especially because in prior editions most powers built on top of what could be done with the prior power, whilst in V5 it's everywhere.<br /> 4: The Five power limit is extremely problematic in building characters. Also it has entirely fucked up sorcery.<br /> 5: Amalgamated disciplines deny payer opportunities thanks to the five power limit.<br /> 6: Amalgamated disciplines kill the mystery of disciplines.<br /> 7: encouraging <i>all </i>players to make up their own powers leads to more problems than benefits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vicissitude becoming Protean is just bad.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to balance Vicissitude, make it so that permanent body modification requires time to apply, so you can't just permanently disfigure someone with a tuck, you've gotta spend time weaving your change into their very being. If you've got enough opportunity to grant someone a permanent modification, you also had the opportunity to inflict final death on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of this is not from V5, Combo Disciplines existed well before then.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages and V20.<br /> <br /> But yes, I know changes to rules are always controversial.<br /> <br /> +1 blood cookie though for resisting the urge to ad hominem, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4: The Five power limit is extremely problematic in building characters. Also it has entirely fucked up sorcery. </div> </div> </div>I think that's why all Paths are Rituals now.<br /> <br /> I 100% agree the 5 power limit is bullshit, though. I also think we need Elder Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2020, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05