e animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think the ability to warp and affect other vampires permanently should be available at Level 1, though?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To put it perfectly simple, <b>yes</b>. Also the first level of Vicissitude only allows the user of the discipline to reconfigure <i>themselves</i> only. Where are you coming up with other Vampires for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:05:34-07:00","id":1394349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394345#post1394345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think the ability to warp and affect other vampires permanently should be available at Level 1, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't permanent, you could always heal fleshcraft with blood, as aggravated wounds admittedly in v20, as long as you are the same generation or better than the fleshcrafter (it probably should be that Vampires always can, I think it was in DA, but not going box diving for those books today), which given the power of Dominate and Presence is pretty mild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:05:42-07:00","id":1394350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394347#post1394347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To put it perfectly simple, <b>yes</b>. Also the first level of Vicissitude only allows the user of the discipline to reconfigure <i>themselves</i> only. Where are you coming up with other Vampires for?</div> </div> </div> </div>So which is it? And why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:07:07-07:00","id":1394351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394335#post1394335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I think Tzimisce, I think:<br /> <br /> * What We Do in the Shadows - <b>Fish Malks</b>.<br /> * Hellsing <b>Lasombra</b><br /> * Castlevania - <b>Kiasyd</b>. (yeah I'm just being difficult, honestly I think everybody fits this guy) <br /> * Classic movie Dracula Which movie specifically? There's a lot of them. Most of them are <b>Toreador</b>. <br /> * The Count von Count (away demon puppet!) <b>Ravnos</b><br /> * David Xanatos (odd choice but you see it, right) Mage, but if I have to assign him to a vampire... <b>Tremere</b>. <br /> * Batman (Lord of his domain, brooding, insane old aristocrat, Bat motiffs) <b>Malkavian</b>, obviously. <br /> * Vampire Hunter D - Unfamiliar with the source material. <br /> * Ramsay and Roose Bolton - Roose could be a <b>Tzmisce</b>. Ramsay is <b>Baali </b>(and I say that not just because he's evil)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, V5's entire metaplot is basically just The First Anarch Revolt/Inquisition 2.0. </div> </div> </div>Maybe. I can see it going that way, but at the same time I believe the first Inquisition and Anarch revolt fitted it's context a lot better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:09:25-07:00","id":1394352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394337#post1394337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus fuck, No. Absolutely not. Insert a thousand ad hominems I can't get away with here because I'm just so infuriated with the idea. But then I get more infuriated because if i really discuss this, despite plans to keep it entirely civil, I'll be roped in for &quot;Edition warring&quot; or some other invented nonsense.<br /> <br /> 1: Disciplines are meant to be static. That's the lore. Ratings of 1-5 are planned out for you by God/Lilith/Caine/The Antes, and it's only when you can surpass the normal limits of the fifth level and enter the sixth level that you can do your own things.<br /> 2: Per dot, you achieve a lot less with V5 disciplines. So, whilst you might look at Auspex and &quot;Individualize&quot; yourself with Hightened senses or Sense the Unseen or precognition, you'd get <i>i</i>all of that with just one level of Auspex in prior editions. Old potence let you achieve a lot more just by being a simple strength enhancment than it does being the complex mess of unreasonably specific strength-inspired powers.<br /> 3: Learning, Choosing and Remembering the V5 powers is a lot more effort than it was in VTM. And I don't know about you, but vampires 'planning' their disciplines out and unlocking the same powers at different levels seems a little off. It's a lot more intuitive and easy to just have players go 1,2,3,4,5. Especially because in prior editions most powers built on top of what could be done with the prior power, whilst in V5 it's everywhere.<br /> 4: The Five power limit is extremely problematic in building characters. Also it has entirely fucked up sorcery.<br /> 5: Amalgamated disciplines deny payer opportunities thanks to the five power limit.<br /> 6: Amalgamated disciplines kill the mystery of disciplines.<br /> 7: encouraging <i>all </i>players to make up their own powers leads to more problems than benefits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vicissitude becoming Protean is just bad.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to balance Vicissitude, make it so that permanent body modification requires time to apply, so you can't just permanently disfigure someone with a tuck, you've gotta spend time weaving your change into their very being. If you've got enough opportunity to grant someone a permanent modification, you also had the opportunity to inflict final death on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey look. It's facts disguised as opinions that are wrong.<br /> <br /> 1. Blood Sorcery and in fact the beloved Viss are both proof that they aren't 'static', combo disciplines are proof that they aren't static. Inceptors are proof that they aren't static. Disciplines weren't 'planned out' by anyone. Even in lore they were just Caine unlocking the power contained within the blood.<br /> 2. I'll give you that for certain levels they got nerfed. But let's take auspex, which now has Clairvoyance as a level 5 power. Or Share the Senses which is a level 3 power. Or Premonition. Or potence. Passively added to strength, spend a blood to turn it into auto successes. Now has a power that does that (Prowess) but also let's you: Do agg to humans, drink from humans in seconds, have imprint as a level 3 power, have earth shock as a level 5 power, can deal agg as a level 5 power. So you can't really make the argument that they do LESS and then bitch about a discipline objectively achieving more.<br /> 3. Learning powers takes more effort. If you dip into in clans only. Sure. Except base V20, I'd reasonably need to learn the power of 17 Disciplines, not including specific necromancy or thaumaturgy paths, or bloodline disciplines. V5, you need to learn 10 disciplines with different powers.<br /> 4. It's an opinion finally. I'd disagree that it's problematic in building characters or that it's fucked up sorcery. It's only problematic if you want to have ALL the powers. Because we go back to your first argument. It's fine when there's one power per dot but not when there's multiple options? Elders simply need to pick up a wider variety of powers rather than more. Sorcery was also problematic because it doesn't need instant magical powers, it replicates other disciplines effects overtime so at the least the time cost is minimal.<br /> 5. That is much the point is that they are opportunity costs, which is why amalgams are much more powerful. But fine, an actual opinion.<br /> 6. If anything, it does the opposite. Players know the gist of what dominate does. So why the fuck is one person freaking out after the malkavian talked to them? Players know what protean does, so how on earth is the Tzimisce just melting another person's flesh with a touch? Amalgams let you break the rules and make people ask WHY something is happening. That doesn't 'kill mysteries' it does the exact opposite.<br /> 7. Hey look, an opinion that's correct but not supported by the book.<br /> <br /> As for viss becoming protean. I get it. Change is scary. It can't be it's own discipline by virtue of the fact that there's no way it could support having multiple power options. In addition to the other issues it has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:12:20-07:00","id":1394355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394345#post1394345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think the ability to warp and affect other vampires permanently should be available at Level 1, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never allowed it to work Permanently on Vampires. It's just another in a Looong list of things that needed to be house ruled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:14:22-07:00","id":1394356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394355#post1394355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never allowed it to work Permanently on Vampires. It's just another in a Looong list of things that needed to be house ruled.</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't, if the vampire didn't want it to, you healed it as aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:14:24-07:00","id":1394357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394341#post1394341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of this is not from V5, Combo Disciplines existed well before then.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, when I meant 'amalgamations' I meant Quietus/Thaumaturgy and Necromancy/Obtenebration mergers. <br /> <br /> <br /> Combination disciplines were entirely different in prior editions. Combo disciplines were something you got <i>after </i>you had the prequisite levels of a discipline, and they would not interfere with your overall rating. Now a combination discipline is a power that takes one of your 5 dots, which is a mess in more ways than one. <br /> <br /> Everything I listed is a problem V5 introduced. I'm entirely not against alternate powers, I loved LotC's alternative assamite powers (it's not a flawless execution, but it's a great idea) but in that case you could go back and get the powers you missed out on without it counting against your limits. (I also feel that it makes <i>sense </i>for specialised powers like Quietus, Protean and Valaren but really isn't a good idea for common disciplines like Presence/Potence/Dominate...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:15:12-07:00","id":1394358,"title":"","content":"Arguably, I'd say Protean is becoming Viss since it's going from Static Powers to a bunch of different ones.<br /> <br /> I assume that Vicissitude will also be an alternate name for it.<br /> <br /> Unless we have Tzimisce Blood Sorcery named Vicissitude rather than Protean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:16:28-07:00","id":1394359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394356#post1394356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It didn't, if the vampire didn't want it to, you healed it as aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok I should word it that all changes reverted the next night like cutting your hair or getting a tattoo. it doesn't stick and you revert back normally, no need to heal like aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:17:25-07:00","id":1394360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394359#post1394359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok I should word it that all changes reverted the next night like cutting your hair or getting a tattoo. it doesn't stick and you revert back normally, no need to heal like aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which kinda screws over characters who wanted the change to stick, but to each their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:18:34-07:00","id":1394361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394358#post1394358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguably, I'd say Protean is becoming Viss since it's going from Static Powers to a bunch of different ones.<br /> <br /> I assume that Vicissitude will also be an alternate name for it.<br /> <br /> Unless we have Tzimisce Blood Sorcery named Vicissitude rather than Protean.</div> </div> </div> </div>The precedent is for it to be amalgams that straight jacket you Into a preset build to actually have thr.m.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:20:42-07:00","id":1394362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394360#post1394360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which kinda screws over characters who wanted the change to stick, but to each their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you actually have Vicissitude you can change yourself as often as you like. If you want a more stable canvas that's what humans are for. Of course your more by the rules than I am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:24:05-07:00","id":1394363,"title":"","content":"You know? At this point they should amalgam all the disciplines into one mega discipline that would be Thin-Blood alchemy 2.0. Then by that point all the fun stuff can be taken out and the game can steer more to tabletop Sims 3 than VTM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:35:22-07:00","id":1394364,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Necroticbinder;n1394352]<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Blood Sorcery and in fact the beloved Viss are both proof that they aren't 'static', combo disciplines are proof that they aren't static. I<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">nceptors are proof that they aren't static</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you made a good point here. Let's adress it. <br /> <br /> Magic follows universal rules and princibles. <br /> When you are incepting, you are uncovering new magic, and working in accordance to it's rules. <br /> When you are using the same disciplines others use, you are working with the same rules as they do. <br /> If someone were to learn the discipline you incepted, they would be using the same rules as you. <br /> Combo disciplines are the result of &quot;lawyering&quot; with rules. You aren't breaking any rules, you're just abusing them for the results you want. <br /> <br /> Vampires, Werewolves, Changelings, Hedgewizards, wraiths and spirits all work according to rules. Mages still have rules, but they're a lot more lax, so they think of their magic as &quot;dynamic&quot; and everyone else's magic as &quot;pattern magic&quot;. But when a mage tries to break rules they backlash hard. <br /> <br /> So, basically, those guys you mentioned aren't making up whatever the hell they want, it's a lot closer to just finding new sets of rules that other people haven't discovered yet. They're still working within a &quot;static&quot; framework. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get it. Change is scary. </div> </div> </div>Are you baiting me? How is it that I can write long lists of reasons why it'd be bad for Vicissitude and Tzmisce players and you can dismiss all these concerns as a foolish fear of change. I ask again; <i>are you baiting me? </i> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It can't be it's own discipline by virtue of the fact that there's no way it could support having multiple power options. In addition to the other issues it has. </div> </div> </div>You really think Vicissitude couldn't support multiple power options? I don't really know what to say to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:38:02-07:00","id":1394366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394296#post1394296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gave <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> the real reason why the original Tzimisce disciplines were what they were, since the topic came up. Your personal take on the Tzimisce is what's completely irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and I appreciate the info, not being familiar with Necroscope. <br /> <br /> I agree it\u2019s useful to know why things were developed the way they were. It doesn\u2019t mean we have to slavishly adhere to tradition, but knowing why things are the way they are helps to make an informed decision about what to keep and what to change.<br /> <br /> What gets me is how many people (this part is not not aimed at you) can\u2019t handle things being changed in a new edition, like adjusting things is some kind of sin, even though the version they\u2019re attached to was itself most often an adjustment of something previous. This is how these things go, especially in WoD, which is a conservative\u2019s nightmare (in more ways than one).<br /> <br /> And in any case, there are several things that are pretty well certain: 1) This edition will not have unique disciplines. 2) The Tzimisce have already been confirmed to have Protean as of Chicago by Night. 3) Clan writeups are expected to be sect-agnostic, to emphasize that lineage and loyalty are not equivalent. 4) Following that, bloodlines will not be getting full clan writeups but are to be treated as the parent clan and represented with Flaws and Loresheets. 5) Blood Sorcery is now an umbrella term for a bunch of stuff that had different names in previous editions, thus not monopolized by a single clan. 6) This edition will not be presenting paths of enlightenment as a replacement for the Humanity system, though they can be represented by slightly tweaking Convictions. <br /> <br /> All of this gives us a pretty good idea of what to expect. For what it\u2019s worth, I think these design principles make a lot of sense, and I\u2019m eagerly awaiting the Tzimisces writeup. Still think they should put the S back...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T09:02:10-07:00","id":1394367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394337#post1394337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus fuck, No. Absolutely not. Insert a thousand ad hominems I can't get away with here because I'm just so infuriated with the idea. But then I get more infuriated because if i really discuss this, despite plans to keep it entirely civil, I'll be roped in for &quot;Edition warring&quot; or some other invented nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou do something here <i>other than </i>edition warring? I haven\u2019t seen it. Do you have a link?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1: Disciplines are meant to be static. That's the lore. Ratings of 1-5 are planned out for you by God/Lilith/Caine/The Antes, and it's only when you can surpass the normal limits of the fifth level and enter the sixth level that you can do your own things.<br /> 2: Per dot, you achieve a lot less with V5 disciplines. So, whilst you might look at Auspex and &quot;Individualize&quot; yourself with Hightened senses or Sense the Unseen or precognition, you'd get <i>i</i>all of that with just one level of Auspex in prior editions. Old potence let you achieve a lot more just by being a simple strength enhancment than it does being the complex mess of unreasonably specific strength-inspired powers.<br /> 3: Learning, Choosing and Remembering the V5 powers is a lot more effort than it was in VTM. And I don't know about you, but vampires 'planning' their disciplines out and unlocking the same powers at different levels seems a little off. It's a lot more intuitive and easy to just have players go 1,2,3,4,5. Especially because in prior editions most powers built on top of what could be done with the prior power, whilst in V5 it's everywhere.<br /> 4: The Five power limit is extremely problematic in building characters. Also it has entirely fucked up sorcery.<br /> 5: Amalgamated disciplines deny payer opportunities thanks to the five power limit.<br /> 6: Amalgamated disciplines kill the mystery of disciplines.<br /> 7: encouraging <i>all </i>players to make up their own powers leads to more problems than benefits. </div> </div> </div>1: Bullshit rationalization for how they happened to have already designed the system. There\u2019s zero reason to design from this perspective going forward.<br /> 2: Not true from what I can see. First dot was traditionally Heightened Senses. Sense the Unseen is a different alternative not traditionally included in Heightened Senses. The disciplines are actually very well designed by people quite familiar with previous editions\u2019 strengths and weaknesses.<br /> 3: True, but worth it for more choices and less predictability.<br /> 4: Disagree, as players now have more choices and are less cookie-cutter. Sorcery started fucked-up and is now less so.<br /> 5: Don\u2019t see how this could possibly be the case. Only elders ever got to the 6th dot in previous editions, and then they had to pick powers just like V5 has you do. They just had the option of picking extremely unbalanced god powers, of which there were often several per dot. V5 just compresses this range and offers choices from the beginning. So disciplines basically work as they did for elders from the beginning.<br /> 6: The opposite is true, as you don\u2019t know what someone with a particular discipline will be capable of.<br /> 7: Who is doing that? Most will pick from a list, but the list is open-ended. Those who know what they\u2019re doing can add to it.<br /> <br /> From my perspective, going from predictable and familiar to much more varied and personalized is a good thing. You can\u2019t simultaneously bemoan that things are less familiar <i>and </i>less mysterious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vicissitude becoming Protean is just bad. </div> </div> </div>Unique snowflake disciplines are just bad. But I don\u2019t think it\u2019s as simple as Vicissitude being folded into Protean. Tzimisce will have Protean, we know this, but fleshcrafting will almost certainly be an amalgam, as Dementation is now. It\u2019s unlikely that the Gangrel or Ministey will have easy access to it, as Ventrue and Lasombra lack easy access to Dementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 06-05-2020, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T09:33:38-07:00","id":1394374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394366#post1394366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, and I appreciate the info, not being familiar with Necroscope. <br /> <br /> I agree it\u2019s useful to know why things were developed the way they were. It doesn\u2019t mean we have to slavishly adhere to tradition, but knowing why things are the way they are helps to make an informed decision about what to keep and what to change.<br /> <br /> What gets me is how many people (this part is not not aimed at you) can\u2019t handle things being changed in a new edition, like adjusting things is some kind of sin, even though the version they\u2019re attached to was itself most often an adjustment of something previous. This is how these things go, especially in WoD, which is a conservative\u2019s nightmare (in more ways than one).<br /> <br /> And in any case, there are several things that are pretty well certain: 1) This edition will not have unique disciplines. 2) The Tzimisce have already been confirmed to have Protean as of Chicago by Night. 3) Clan writeups are expected to be sect-agnostic, to emphasize that lineage and loyalty are not equivalent. 4) Following that, bloodlines will not be getting full clan writeups but are to be treated as the parent clan and represented with Flaws and Loresheets. 5) Blood Sorcery is now an umbrella term for a bunch of stuff that had different names in previous editions, thus not monopolized by a single clan. 6) This edition will not be presenting paths of enlightenment as a replacement for the Humanity system, though they can be represented by slightly tweaking Convictions. <br /> <br /> All of this gives us a pretty good idea of what to expect. For what it\u2019s worth, I think these design principles make a lot of sense, and I\u2019m eagerly awaiting the Tzimisces writeup. Still think they should put the S back...</div> </div> </div> </div>6) having tried it, no they really can't. You don't get the same feeling of walking the razor edge that decent Paths gave, at all, and most paths have zero reason to interact with human touchstones (but then I have a big problem with touchstones anyway, don't out source self control, self belief and self discipline, to another person, especially one you then have to keep static to embody what ever it is) it would be a completely different system, both in RP and rules terms, which if people want it, fine, just don't tell me the Paths 'can be done by tweaked convictions' that is manifestly incorrect.<br /> <br /> Oh and on Amalgam powers, they dictate what disciplines you need at character creation to do something that used to be 'take x dots in y discipline and your good', now that also dictates other background choices, so you end up with same background, same Predator type etc, just to start with the iconic power, that's less variety, not more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":".  Words. 06-05-2020, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T09:37:02-07:00","id":1394375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394367#post1394367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [1: Bullshit rationalization for how they happened to have already designed the system. There\u2019s zero reason to design from this perspective going forward.<br /> <b>This is how it was Written. I'm not rationalizing on behalf of the books; I might rationalize some elaborations, but the metaphysics of disciplines are largely written down. For instance many have speculated Dominate's Generation restriction was Caine's doing</b><br /> 2: Not true from what I can see. First dot was traditionally Heightened Senses. Sense the Unseen is a different alternative not traditionally included in Heightened Senses. The disciplines are actually very well designed by people quite familiar with previous editions\u2019 strengths and weaknesses.<br /> <b>I'll hold off on the zingers, but you are wrong here. Sense the Unseen was something you had just by having any levels in Auspex at all, IE you get it with Auspex 1. Premonition was also loaded into the Auspex discipline. If you're going to &quot;correct&quot; me, at least try to be correct. </b><br /> 3: True, but worth it for more choices and less predictability.<br /> <b>That's your opinion, but I don't think it's the correct one. Although we might crave the idea of more options, our psychology tends to go the other way and we are more comfortable with less choice. I can link you studies if you really want to follow up on this. </b><br /> 4: Disagree, as players now have more choices and are less cookie-cutter. Sorcery started fucked-up and is now less so.<br /> <b>Sorcery is now indistinguishable from normal disciplines and thus has no reason to exist. Again, the princples of sorcery were all written down (There's literally a trilogy on it) so this retcon is pretty absurd. </b><br /> 5: Don\u2019t see how this could possibly be the case. Only elders ever got to the 6th dot in previous editions, and then they had to pick powers just like V5 has you do. They just had the option of picking extremely unbalanced god powers, of which there were often several per dot. V5 just compresses this range and offers choices from the beginning. So disciplines basically work as they did for elders from the beginning.<br /> <b>But we're not playing elders, and six+ dots don't exist anymore. What kind of Gymnastics do you think you are doing here? Actually, the point of Elders doing whatever they wanted was to make the younger vampires jealous and hungry. If you just replace the 1-5 static linearity with the dynamic transcendant 6-10 &quot;pick what powers you want&quot; then what is there to envy? </b><br /> 6: The opposite is true, as you don\u2019t know what someone with a particular discipline will be capable of.<br /> <b>Does<i> Vampire: The Masquerade</i> star xanxia cultivators with hidden cards to play or is it about undead bloodlines with hereditary powers? </b><br /> 7: Who is doing that? Most will pick from a list, but the list is open-ended. Those who know what they\u2019re doing can add to it.<br /> <b>Did you know the average person thinks they're &quot;Above average&quot;? Who actually knows what they're doing? You've shown a grevious lack of understanding regarding Auspex and blood magic; Do you qualify? In your view I'm entirely wrong with everything, do I qualify? If you encourage people who 'know what they're doing' to step up... You're just going to witness the power of the Dunning krueger effect. Then you're going to have to upset people by shutting down their absurd ideas that they felt <i>encouraged </i>to share</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unique snowflake disciplines are just bad. </div> </div> </div><i>But unique snowflake powers within normal disciplines are just plain fantastic. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-05-2020, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T09:38:19-07:00","id":1394376,"title":"","content":"There are aspects of V5 that I like and that I don\u2019t like. I like the Lasombra moving into the Camarilla. I also like how they have given multiple Discipline powers per level, that may be my favorite rule change. The customizability it adds to characters is great. I think I would allow characters to use experience to buy more than one power per level though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T10:14:08-07:00","id":1394385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you just replace the 1-5 static linearity with the dynamic transcendant 6-10 &quot;pick what powers you want&quot; then what is there to envy?</div> </div> </div> </div>EXACTLY! Butchering ALL the disciplines with only a cap of 5 and making you choose a finite amount of powers is one of the biggest disasters for V5. It DOESN'T make any sense from an IC and OOC perspective. Now the players have no drive to try and commit diablerie, because what would be the point?<br /> <br /> ICly, why would the practitioner who is getting more and more experienced in the particular discipline how be limited to ONE technique per advancement? Why? As you progress you should get AWARDED for every pushing through night by night with a cache of powers for each dot you progress through. OOC the 5 cap and only one power technique is <b>ridiculous</b>. What if you want a totally different power but now all your dots are used up? You can't because &quot;its already progressed through&quot; instead of you getting the appropriate power(s) per dot all at once. It's one of the most baffling thing to me when I first learned of V5 when I started getting into cWoD in general. <br /> <br /> Also your definitely right <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a>- possible Elder games are now impossible because now even neonates are basically on the same tier as of now. Y'know its funny how Vicissitude is clobbered as a &quot;snowflake&quot; discipline when that couldn't be further from the truth. It's INTERESTING, bar being one of the best RP disciplines as of V20 and everything &quot;unique&quot; is not &quot;snowflake&quot; because it maybe rare or relegated to a few specific splats. If you REALLY want &quot;snowflake&quot; Thin-Blood alchemy is definitely what you'd actually mean (a discipline in all reality is just something to justify Thin-Bloods being interesting and an attempt to make them viable because as per meta high gens are becoming more and more common).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T10:28:48-07:00","id":1394387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394366#post1394366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in any case, there are several things that are pretty well certain: 1) This edition will not have unique disciplines. 2) The Tzimisce have already been confirmed to have Protean as of Chicago by Night. 3) Clan writeups are expected to be sect-agnostic, to emphasize that lineage and loyalty are not equivalent. 4) Following that, bloodlines will not be getting full clan writeups but are to be treated as the parent clan and represented with Flaws and Loresheets. 5) Blood Sorcery is now an umbrella term for a bunch of stuff that had different names in previous editions, thus not monopolized by a single clan. 6) This edition will not be presenting paths of enlightenment as a replacement for the Humanity system, though they can be represented by slightly tweaking Convictions.<br /> <br /> All of this gives us a pretty good idea of what to expect. For what it\u2019s worth, I think these design principles make a lot of sense, and I\u2019m eagerly awaiting the Tzimisces writeup. Still think they should put the S back...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, but I don't like a single one of the design principles outlined above. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's partly why I don't like participating in V5 threads -- I tend to come across as very negative about the whole endeavor, but that doesn't really reflect what I think about the new edition as a whole. I'm <i>more than happy</i> to see a new version of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> back on the market, and even though it's clearly not the edition for me, I don't begrudge anyone for enjoying the hell out of it. That would be very silly of me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T10:28:52-07:00","id":1394388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394302#post1394302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know what you're disagreeing with me on, seriously. The Tzimisce are awesome because they are amazingly wild, varied, and capable of doing the Dracula/Castlevania/Hellsing thing that other Clans are not.<br /> <br /> I keep hammering the Dracula point home because other clans CANT DO THAT as well as the Tzimisce. You are attacking my argument from the perspective of how I feel about Ventrue.<br /> <br /> That they're generic and uninteresting and lack anything unique.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce ooze STYLE. They are like Lando Calrissian in that they can wear a cape and make it look good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why you're so opposed to Gangrel or Ventrue having those qualities but, taking Ventrue and Gangrel out the picture for a minute, do you really expect V5 to deliver on that fantasy of yours?<br /> <br /> because, in previous editions, there was one clan in the Camarilla (and I stress &quot;in the camarilla&quot;) that 100% fit that archtype,<br /> and guess who it was?<br /> guess again<br /> well, it was the Lasombra antitribu<br /> <br /> creepy powerful vampire lords in their castles? that's them<br /> almighty alucard types that devour their whole city and anyone trying to take over? that was them (within reasonable limits imposed by the camarilla, because the camarilla sucked like that)<br /> <br /> and now, it's been two years (?) since v5 came out,<br /> and where are those creepy lasombra lords in their castles?...*cricket sounds*<br /> all we get is the new boys lasombra who cower before their ancients, and hammer it in your head that they're masters of the world's religions...then hammer it down some more, and then again some more as if they're not trying to convince you but themselves<br /> <br /> while I do share your passion for the feudal tzimisce, what tells you they won't shaft them the same way they did the Lasombra Antis?<br /> do you have some insider info to reveal?<br /> maybe some backer exclusive behind the scenes unreleased secret info?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-05-2020, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiad