_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T18:57:23-07:00","id":1394472,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> you arr right. Auspex in prior editions gave premonition AND sixth sense for free at level 1. The game even give a ex: sense a firearm aiming the back of your neck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T20:30:36-07:00","id":1394491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394367#post1394367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYou do something here <i>other than </i>edition warring? I haven\u2019t seen it. Do you have a link?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I'll be the judge of that, thank you.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T05:16:04-07:00","id":1394544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394465#post1394465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am hoping that they keep a lot of Dark Ages Tzimisce and update them for Modern Nights</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why I was perplexed earlier in the thread when you set the original 2nd Edition Tzimisce and <i>Dark Ages</i> Tzimisce in opposition with one another is that I don't see the <i>Dark Ages</i> Tzimisce as a change of direction at all. When I write &quot;<i>Necroscope</i> vampire,&quot; to my mind that <i>includes all of the trappings and visuals of feudal lords that you are so fond of.</i> Even I don't want to keep hammering home the <i>Necroscope</i> point any more than I already have, because I too think that the Tzimisce should not be <i>direct</i> ripoffs of the Wamphyri, just like the Toreador are not <i>direct</i> ripoffs of <i>The Vampire Chronicles</i> vampires. But <i>Necroscope</i> characters like Faethor Ferenczy and Thibor Ferenczy <i>are</i> proud, regal feudal lords in the exact mold of Strahd von Zarovich, <i>Castlevania's</i> Dracula, and other examples of Tzimisce paragons from various media that you gave earlier in the thread. In the <i>Necroscope</i> series, the vampires in question just happen to be medieval humans who were infected with a parasitic lifeform whose origins are wilder than they ever would have conceived. But that's just another <i>origin story</i> for vampirekind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, I wouldn't be surprised if that is what they do because the treatment of body modification by the public has changed greatly. It's not a discipline one should look at being any worse than another Vampire Discipline. </div> </div> </div>Here is where we have to part ways, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I don't think classic Vicissitude says <i>anything at all</i> about the authors' views on body modification. From my perspective, that's like saying that the alien in John Carpenter's <i>The Thing</i> is the misunderstood hero of the story -- it just wants to liberate the stodgy researchers from the rigid confines of the human form! You <i>could</i> make the argument, I guess, but you would have to change the plot, tone, characterizations, and even the entire genre of the movie to make it work. Which, in a roundabout way, brings us back to my original question. If a thing (pun intended) was never intended nor designed to support certain kinds of concepts, why take the old thing, rewrite it completely, and insist that the end result is still a continuation of the old idea? It would be so much easier to scrap Vicissitude entirely, including the name, and design a new discipline from scratch that would better support the things you want to see support for, without the <i>considerable</i> negative connotations that this particular discipline has. At its core, Vicissitude has always been about <i>body horror.</i> This is <i>not</i> a good starting point for positive representations of body modification culture.<br /> <br /> I have always had the impression that you are very fond of the personal horror angle of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade.</i> Think of how you would react if there was a push to remove personal horror from the game in favor of more positive representations of vampires. Superheroes with Fangs, some might even call it. I'm sure you can see the analogy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T08:44:02-07:00","id":1394568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394544#post1394544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always had the impression that you are very fond of the personal horror angle of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade.</i> Think of how you would react if there was a push to remove personal horror from the game in favor of more positive representations of vampires. Superheroes with Fangs, some might even call it. I'm sure you can see the analogy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They already did this. It was called V20. Har har har har.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T09:13:18-07:00","id":1394572,"title":"","content":"With the cosmic alien horror de-canonized and the 'Vicissitude as Disease' thing only popping up in Gehenna scenarios (Which aren't canon) Vicissitude is a discipline famous for it's abuse but isn't inherently evil. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">There was some nonsense In DAV20 about Modifications always being painful and terrible for you but DAV20 had some funny ideas about a lot of things. </span><br /> <br /> Some people look at body modification as body horror. A guy covered head to toe in tattoos, with subdermal implants and ten-thousand piercings, is a sight of horror for more conservative people. &quot;Liberal&quot; people look at traditional african scarification as a horrific, barbaric abuse that must be curb-stomped out of humanity. Modern sex re-assignment surgery is, sadly, little more than genital mutilation in order to help some very desperate people, and those very unfortunate people are not looked at very kindly by society. Even when plastic surgery gives us glorious golden faces and bodies to kill for, we as a society look down on the people who use it as cheats.<br /> <br /> Why then, does Vicissitude need a nice rebranding?<br /> <br /> It doesn't. Nothing so much as fucked me off in V5 as a thinblood alchemy <i>level 1 </i>ritual that trivialised a complete perfect sex change. You think that it's easy? That you can just hocus-pocus you way into having the body you would've had were it one chromosome different? All you need to do is get yourself introduced to your local thinblooded fairy... <i>Fuck off</i>.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is perfect for what it is, what it does, and what it represents. It might need a mechanical re-balance, but it's role in the story has too much meaning to it for someone to wash it away for a shallow, sanitized shell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T09:44:08-07:00","id":1394576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394572#post1394572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't. Nothing so much as fucked me off in V5 as a thinblood alchemy <i>level 1 </i>ritual that trivialised a complete perfect sex change. You think that it's easy? That you can just hocus-pocus you way into having the body you would've had were it one chromosome different? All you need to do is get yourself introduced to your local thinblooded fairy... <i>Fuck off</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compared to what? A fuckwit spending points on intelligence to play the smart kid for once? Or the guy never getting picked for the team (or any team) to have Potence, Celerity or somesuch and feel like a star for once? You fuck off!<br /> It's perfectly legit to have the wish or ambition to play a character that is unsure about their gender (and all related and maybe even unrelated issues) and have them have a power to explore that side of existence in this game. This kind of wannabe gatekeeping makes me SICK!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T09:58:50-07:00","id":1394579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pangur B\u00e1n</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394576#post1394576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Compared to what? A fuckwit spending points on intelligence to play the smart kid for once? Or the guy never getting picked for the team (or any team) to have Potence, Celerity or somesuch and feel like a star for once? You fuck off!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he has a point. A level <i>1</i> ritual by a new power system defined by its creation by weak vampires with no tradition doing something as complicated as a full sex change is strange, to say the least. This seems like an extremely powerful thing to do but the barrier of entry seems low. Why can't this ritual be used for more than just sex changes? Why not permanent Mask of 1000 Faces? Why not creation into war ghouls? Why not Ordo Dracul-style improvements to the vampiric form? Why not a form that is more muscular, or more attractive, or more this or more that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's perfectly legit to have the wish or ambition to play a character that is unsure about their gender (and all related and maybe even unrelated issues) and have them have a power to explore that side of existence in this game. This kind of wannabe gatekeeping makes me SICK! </div> </div> </div>Nowhere did he make an opposition to that. Your outrage is not justified.<br /> <br /> Speaking as a trans person myself, the best handling of the issue of gender identity has been the Cover system as found in Demon: the Descent. The nature of the Cover system allows players to explore bits of their own gender identity as they find themselves making do, and having a preference for, certain kinds of gendered appearances they want to have. Cis players can find themselves approaching a type of dysphoria as they get thrust into a Cover which isn't their identified gender because that's all that was available at the time, and I personally think it's an interesting exploration at the concept.<br /> <br /> At best, the profane hieros gamos is a noticeably distinct mechanic for the trans audience with all the hiccups that entails, and at worst, a rather patronising portrayal of the massively medically complicated nature of gender reassignment in medicine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T10:11:32-07:00","id":1394581,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26181_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26181\" data-vbnamecard=\"26181\">MalkSam</a> First of all, let me start by saying: You think your experience (and I will not speak about my own in this forum) allows you to tell me my outrage is not justified? Maybe not for you and I congratulate you for it, but for me it is. That's why it is my outrage.<br /> He did make a point about the ritual (as an aside, pointing out that it is a level 3 ritual in my book) being way too easy. Well, compared to what?! The level 1 power of Potence in previous versions of the game for example gave an automatic success for any kind of feat of strength test. Any kind. You know how hard that is to achieve? It's impossible by human standards. Would you argue that as being a &quot;patronising portrayal&quot; of something bodybuilders spend years to achieve and just as much never reach?<br /> <br /> The game is not intended to recreate the medical complications of gender reassignment. For a whole lot of reasons it shouldn't have to.<br /> Thanks for the recommendation of Demon: the Descent. I shall have a look at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T10:26:02-07:00","id":1394582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pangur B\u00e1n</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394581#post1394581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26181_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26181\" data-vbnamecard=\"26181\">MalkSam</a> First of all, let me start by saying: You think your experience (and I will not speak about my own in this forum) allows you to tell me my outrage is not justified? Maybe not for you and I congratulate you for it, but for me it is. That's why it is my outrage.<br /> He did make a point about the ritual (as an aside, pointing out that it is a level 3 ritual in my book) being way too easy. Well, compared to what?! The level 1 power of Potence in previous versions of the game for example gave an automatic success for any kind of feat of strength test. Any kind. You know how hard that is to achieve? It's impossible by human standards. Would you argue that as being a &quot;patronising portrayal&quot; of something bodybuilders spend years to achieve and just as much never reach?<br /> <br /> The game is not intended to recreate the medical complications of gender reassignment. For a whole lot of reasons it shouldn't have to.<br /> Thanks for the recommendation of Demon: the Descent. I shall have a look at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am saying your outrage is not justified because of what you are implying MyWifeIsScary's point was. His point was that Vicissitude's thunder is being stolen by Thin Blood Alchemy essentially doing what it does, but better, and with a far lesser barrier to entry. He was <i>not </i>saying that he has some sort of distaste, or that there is no room for, players who want to have gender-diverse or questioning PCs. You are painting him as intolerant by misconstruing him (at least, if I am reading your post right).<br /> <br /> Profane Hieros Gamos is under the spotlight here because it is specifically designed to deal with the concept of gender identity. The issue is that the amount of very specific and numerous things you'd need to change for an entirely perfect gender reassignment are very, <i>very </i>numerous, but a level 1 ritual trivialises it and in doing so, raises questions as to what Thin Blood Alchemy is capable of and why this powerful body transmogrification is suddenly so easily accessed. Becoming stronger is quite simple, atomically. You just have more protein in your muscles, thus more muscle fibres. It is a different ball game than gender reassignment.<br /> <br /> And I agree that the game should not recreate the medical complications of gender reassignment, but there was also a much better way of doing this than what the game presents. I personally have quite a distaste for this ritual. I don't find it empowers my identity, I find it erases it. I, and many of my trans acquaintances, find ourselves creating our outward identities in the face of our clashing birth genders. We look past our biology for ways to express our gender identities, and many of us eschew the idea of surgeries out of the idea that we don't need modifications to our outward genitalia to express, and feel, like who we are. Profane Hieros Gamos throws all of that under the bus in a level 1 thin-blood finger snap, and I find it more making light of my situation rather than empathising with it.<br /> <br /> I don't claim to speak for all trans people, however. I'm sure there are people who appreciate the inclusion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T10:38:53-07:00","id":1394583,"title":"","content":"if it's limited to sex change, lvl 1 is enough (at higher levels, there's more powerful rituals to get, especially for how trivial sex change is in the supernatural world),<br /> lvl 1 is enough to make body mods like piercings and tattoos permanent and enough to revitalize sexual organs or taste glands etc<br /> <br /> VtM (as well as MtA and sorcerers) is usually more lax about flesh crafting, and blood magic has always been powerful even at low levels (which made demonic investments kinda pointless outside of dark thaumaturgy)<br /> <br /> VtR is where it gets harder<br /> <br /> tbh, I'm not a fan of how thaumaturgy makes everything easy in VtM, but that's always been a thing, V5 didn't invent that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-06-2020, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T10:56:00-07:00","id":1394587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394583#post1394583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if it's limited to sex change, lvl 1 is enough (at higher levels, there's more powerful rituals to get, especially for how trivial sex change is in the supernatural world),<br /> lvl 1 is enough to make body mods like piercings and tattoos permanent and enough to revitalize sexual organs or taste glands etc</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I mentioned the numerous changes that a perfect sex change would require. Just off the top of my head, you are not only completing replacing an entire set of genitalia with a different, functioning one, you're also changing skin texture, fat redistribution, muscle mass, bone placement, hair density, size and placement of the vocal tract, and a new system of hormone regulation, and I am absolutely no expert in anatomy nor sexual dimorphism.<br /> <br /> It is a myriad of minute but significant changes and it can't be reasonably compared to things like tattoos and piercings. Those are mechanically so simple in comparison.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T11:23:56-07:00","id":1394591,"title":"","content":"Just in case it has slipped through the cracks. Profane Hieros Gamos is only usable by the alchemist concocting the tincture. One could also argue that the process is involved enough not to be a simple finger snap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T11:27:18-07:00","id":1394592,"title":"","content":"Thin-Blood alchemy is the most stupid thing they came up with in V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T11:29:06-07:00","id":1394593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394591#post1394591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just in case it has slipped through the cracks. Profane Hieros Gamos is only usable by the alchemist concocting the tincture. One could also argue that the process is involved enough not to be a simple finger snap.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it is explicitly usable by others with the aid of the alchemist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T11:30:46-07:00","id":1394594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394587#post1394587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why I mentioned the numerous changes that a perfect sex change would require. Just off the top of my head, you are not only completing replacing an entire set of genitalia with a different, functioning one, you're also changing skin texture, fat redistribution, muscle mass, bone placement, hair density, size and placement of the vocal tract, and a new system of hormone regulation, and I am absolutely no expert in anatomy nor sexual dimorphism.<br /> <br /> It is a myriad of minute but significant changes and it can't be reasonably compared to things like tattoos and piercings. Those are mechanically so simple in comparison.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get your point, but that's not exactly my argument,<br /> I'm not really arguing the complexity of the...surgery, but rather the insignificance that is sex change in a world where dominate 2 is a trivial power<br /> <br /> if it were general flesh crafting, the sort of thing that would allow you to do anything from changing your whole body to creating war ghouls etc, I'd make it a lvl4+ ritual maybe,<br /> <br /> but if it's only sex change (and only sex change), lvl2 at worse, but lvl 1 is more than enough imo<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> the permanent tattoo and revitalizing dead organs I mentioned are just examples of lvl 1 rituals that allowed to bypass limitations imposed by the vampiric curse,<br /> and those are far more useful than sex change","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-06-2020, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T11:42:49-07:00","id":1394596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394572#post1394572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't. Nothing so much as fucked me off in V5 as a thinblood alchemy <i>level 1 </i>ritual that trivialised a complete perfect sex change. You think that it's easy? That you can just hocus-pocus you way into having the body you would've had were it one chromosome different? All you need to do is get yourself introduced to your local thinblooded fairy... <i>Fuck off</i>.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is perfect for what it is, what it does, and what it represents. It might need a mechanical re-balance, but it's role in the story has too much meaning to it for someone to wash it away for a shallow, sanitized shell.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You're doing it again. If you can't discuss V5 without being offended by it then you shouldn't participate in V5 discussions. This is the final warning.<br /> <br /> Everyone else?<br /> <br /> Discussing whether a real life life-changing transition is also offensive or not by the level of a game mechanic required to represent it is something I am confidant has no relevance to real life trans issues.<br /> <br /> As such, please move on.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394592#post1394592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thin-Blood alchemy is the most stupid thing they came up with in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">These kind of comments are also not helpful. Feel free to think Thin-Blood alchemy is stupid. But if you're going to say it, explain why and what you'd do to replace it.<br /> <br /> This is a forum about discussing how to help fellow gamers with their games after all.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-06-2020, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T11:56:08-07:00","id":1394599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394587#post1394587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why I mentioned the numerous changes that a perfect sex change would require. Just off the top of my head, you are not only completing replacing an entire set of genitalia with a different, functioning one, you're also changing skin texture, fat redistribution, muscle mass, bone placement, hair density, size and placement of the vocal tract, and a new system of hormone regulation, and I am absolutely no expert in anatomy nor sexual dimorphism.<br /> <br /> It is a myriad of minute but significant changes and it can't be reasonably compared to things like tattoos and piercings. Those are mechanically so simple in comparison.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The ritual sounds like some that plays into thin-bloods being both weak and strong. Physically, it's an impressive feat than simplifies a complex change, but for cis kindred, it has little practical use. And if you think that's a big deal, what does that make turning into an animal?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T12:04:57-07:00","id":1394601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394599#post1394599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ritual sounds like some that plays into thin-bloods being both weak and strong. Physically, it's an impressive feat than simplifies a complex change, but for cis kindred, it has little practical use. And if you think that's a big deal, what does that make turning into an animal?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">See above. Please drop this conversation topic.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T12:22:52-07:00","id":1394604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394593#post1394593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it is explicitly usable by others with the aid of the alchemist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am looking at the text and do not see that. Where?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T12:31:42-07:00","id":1394605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">explain why</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it plainly doesn't make any sense at all. Thin-Bloods are supposed to be the weakest in VTM just from the meta alone. Not only that with what is established about them, they aren't even Vampires anymore- IIRC some even can have <i>children</i> outright. Thin-Bloods because of the whole Caine generation thing is meant to be a stop-gap, how are they getting these disciplines out from nowhere? Wut? It doesn't make sense to me. Not only that Thin-Bloods are the most disoriented group within Vampire society, they barely understand anything of what is going on. Who even has started Thin-Blood alchemy and who is the one making all these rituals to disseminate amongst the other Thin-Bloods? And how could it fly under the radar of the various Princes who wouldn't want Thin-Blood upstarts to gain and become efficient in these disciplines? Even then the blood is so thin within Thin-Bloods, how are they mustering up any innate power to establish these disciplines in the first place? It's hilarious!<br /> <br /> Thin-Blood alchemy was simply made to flex-tape the fiat laid down from the Caine-Generation meta, a way for Thin-Bloods to be viable PCs and NPCs despite previously they were essentially the call signs of &quot;Gehenna&quot;. Maybe this is the reason why their trying to adapt out Elders as possible avenues to play as with all the nerfs and retcons about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T12:41:15-07:00","id":1394607,"title":"","content":"I don't like the idea of Thin Blood Alchemy either. It seems so random. If the thin bloods are going to have a special Discipline, it should be a power which reduces or negates vampiric weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T12:45:52-07:00","id":1394608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394607#post1394607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the idea of Thin Blood Alchemy either. It seems so random. If the thin bloods are going to have a special Discipline, it should be a power which reduces or negates vampiric weaknesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, they can be what was described in the rules of V20 and BJD concerning the 14th,15th, and 16th generations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T12:55:01-07:00","id":1394609,"title":"","content":"I think this thread is drifting more and more away from the Lasombra... maybe it should be closed, so we can create others like &quot;Thin-Blooded Alchemy: yeah or nay?&quot; and &quot;Speculations about the future of the Tzimisce in V5&quot; and &quot;Comments on the cultural roots of the Tzimisce as depicted in DAV and V20, with specific references to Brian Lumley's Necroscope series&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T13:23:29-07:00","id":1394615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394604#post1394604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am looking at the text and do not see that. Where?</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>Profane Hieros Gamos</i> formula was completely rewritten in errata. The original version was a level-one ritual, maybe only usable by the alchemist (it's unclear), which changes gender but nothing else. The new version is a level-three ritual, explicitly usable on others, which turns someone into their ideal vision of themself, whatever that may be. So yes it can change gender presentation, but also everything from hair length to muscle tone; the fluff around it is that it's changing the pattern the vampiric body resets to each sunset, replacing it with the vampire's own ideal. (But if anything goes less than perfectly, the subject can end up looking like a Nosferatu for good. Alchemy is weird and experimental and unreliable.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T13:46:54-07:00","id":1394621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394609#post1394609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this thread is drifting more and more away from the Lasombra... maybe it should be closed, so we can create others like &amp;quot;Thin-Blooded Alchemy: yeah or nay?&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Speculations about the future of the Tzimisce in V5&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Comments on the cultural roots of the Tzimisce as depicted in DAV and V20, with specific references to Brian Lumley's Necroscope series&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again this?? Threads should be closed only in exceptional situations, like the creator using the n word. Don't ask to close foruns only because we are discussing things you don't agree. Its perfectly normal a chat evolve to others topics. We are not robots discussing math.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T13:52:47-07:00","id":1394622,"title":"","content":"it's fine, imo the most entertaining thread in a while,<br /> <br /> if you feel the thread needs be closed, just make a report, and the mods will decide,<br /> it kinda ruins the mood when you suggest the thread needs to be closed in public,<br /> makes people feel targeted<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T13:54:14-07:00","id":1394623,"title":"","content":"I lost my post.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> s<br /> Playing with stories like VTM has a very real impact on how we view the world. I don't think it's fair at all to say that whether a transition is easy or not within a story would have no impact on the issues in real life. VTM has an absolutely huge trans following; I've seldom played a game without a trans player at my table, and they enjoy the escapism or catharsis of either playing the opposite sex or by playing a transitioned character who can strike back.<br /> <br /> In my experience, Trans players have almost exclusively played CIS characters of their desired sex. I see little reason to undermine players who want to challenge themselves with Trans characters by offering them an easy,trivialising, patronizing ritual (That's way too powerful for it's level; looking at other transformative powers this'd be easily at leasta level 5 ritual if you want kid production capabilities) and, I don't know, I can't imagine my Trans players choosing to play &quot;Well, I was born a man, but I met this thinblood and I'm now a woman and it needn't be mentioned again&quot;<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">&quot;It's an unreasonably attractive cis girl or bust&quot; - paraphrasing of someone I've played far too much with. </span><br /> <br /> Vicissitude is the ultimate deviant discipline. It horrifies the establishment, and it empowers people to be who they want. It's the most wonderful beautiful allegory for both people struggling to fit in and people who want to stand out. It's the <i>bestest</i> most <i>wonderfulest</i> most creative Dr.Gothic-Punk Discipline ever. It cannot be watered down, sanitized, undermined, normalized or otherwise subversed in todays age. It represents too much. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I'll start imprisoning those who say it should be Protean whenever I get round to building appropriate accommodation) </span><br /> <br /> If it were up to me, I'd give Vicissitude &quot;Procedures&quot; (Mechanically similar to Rituals) that let them do all sorts of very specific things with the body, and I'd write several in regarding sex changes. That'd work far better than sorcery both in thematic and practical terms.<br /> <br /> Taking away Vicissitude and turning it into Protean is about more than just the clan's identity. It's an attack on a sacred cow. Perhaps the gender changing ritual was well meaning, but it completely undermines <i>the </i>discipline of those who want to change their body. (I also feel it's too &quot;nice&quot; for the &quot;World of Darkness&quot;) Maybe you've just gotta have a certain mindset to appreciate and understand Vicissitude, it sure as hell has it's in-universe detractors, and in-universe propaganda seems to influence out-of-universe opinions.<br /> <br /> Summary:<br /> -Vicissitude is art.<br /> -Art influences our lives<br /> -Vicissitude is the best.<br /> -Vicissitude is the best thing for characters who don't conform.<br /> -Real life people who don't conform are either going to play characters that do conform or they're going to go all-in on nonconformity; I don't believe any magical conformity ritual will be of any need, it just sounds &quot;supportive&quot; to have it in the game.<br /> -[Eldest] was an absolute madlad to steal this stuff from the gardens.<br /> -Vicissitude should get it's own rituals to represent practitioners experimenting and mastering the quasi-science of vicissitude.<br /> -Making Vicissitude a branch of Protean would be the complete wrong direction for all the reasons.<br /> -Protean is a low clan discipline for people who wear wolf and moon shirts and sleep outside, Vicissitude is a Chad High clan discipline for transcendent land-owning doctor-wizards with good manners.<br /> -Making Vicissitude Koldunism would be... Less bad, but still bad.<br /> -This is still relevant to lasombra, because Obtenebration has a lot of parallels with Vicissitude.<br /> -You can base an untold number of character concepts on just Vicissitude. No other discipline lets you really do that. It would be an absolute shame to hand off features of Vicissitude to something else.<br /> <br /> I'm having a hard time expressing my thoughts and feelings on this one. Sorry. There's some stuff I just can't attempt to articulate without seeming like a madman. We are imperfect people. In order to be evocative, you have to be hard. You lose that if you just want to come up with a nice solution to everything you find &quot;problematic&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Edit: I was writing this before your second stop post came through, but I really don't want to delete it post. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-06-2020, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T14:07:16-07:00","id":1394624,"title":"","content":"TLDR: Merging Vicissitude out of nowhere with Protrean will be an unmitigated disaster. It was bad enough Obtenebration and full on Necromancy bit the dust for whatever they were thinking of in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 06-06-2020, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T14:31:14-07:00","id":1394628,"title":"","content":"Hey, since we're on the topic, we can revisit my old idea of Vicissitude as Paths:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/187154-vicissitude-as-paths\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/187154-vicissitude-as-paths\"> Vicissitude as Paths - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/187154-vicissitude-as-paths\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/187154-vicissitude-as-paths </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> There was a thread a while back about making a Kuldunic Sorcery path that related to manipulating a blood bond, since the Tzimisce are known for that. That idea appealed to me, though part of me also thought that it could be neat to make the ability to increase the efficacy of the blood bond a part of </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Or alternatively, Vicissitude being different for different Revenant families:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/841919-vicissitude-by-revenant-family\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/841919-vicissitude-by-revenant-family\"> Vicissitude by Revenant Family - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/841919-vicissitude-by-revenant-family\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/841919-vicissitude-by-revenant-family </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So, we have talked about Vicissitude house rules before, and I have some more. These are a bit strange because they are based on an alternative setting that my gaming group is working on where Revenant families have a much bigger role in the setting, especially within the Tzimisce Clan. So the nature of a Tzimisce's Vicissitude is going to vary based on the Revenant family that it was born into. Here are some examples for those families which have Vicissitude, I may tweak them further based on my own examination and any input I get from the forums. Zantosa 1. Beyond Pain. The Zantosa push their bodies </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T14:40:59-07:00","id":1394629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394621#post1394621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again this?? Threads should be closed only in exceptional situations, like the creator using the n word. Don't ask to close foruns only because we are discussing things you don't agree. Its perfectly normal a chat evolve to others topics. We are not robots discussing math.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I don't understand what you think is so problematic about wanting a thread (not a forum, a single thread) to stay on topic. It's not a matter of agreement (in fact, I agree with lots of things people here have said), it's a matter of clarity. And I don't know what you mean with &quot;Again this&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 06-06-2020, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T14:48:11-07:00","id":1394633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394622#post1394622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's fine, imo the most entertaining thread in a while,<br /> if you feel the thread needs be closed, just make a report, and the mods will decide,<br /> it kinda ruins the mood when you suggest the thread needs to be closed in public,<br /> makes people feel targeted</div> </div> </div> </div>If people feels fine, it's fine.<br /> I'm sorry about raining on your parade; it kinda ruins the mood for me when I open my subscriptions, hoping to read about the Lasombra, and find ten entries about the Tzimisce, Lumley, Vicissitude, the f* word, and posters calling other posters 'idiot' and saying this or this is 'idiotic'.<br /> <br /> But your mileage may vary, of course.<br /> I could say: &quot;You could have commented on my behaviour on private, or reported me; commenting it on public makes me feel targeted, for instance&quot;, but I haven't. It's only a hypothesis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T15:04:03-07:00","id":1394637,"title":"","content":"Thread drift is inevitable after five pages. Though if anyone wants to open a new topic, please do. I'm not shutting down the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-06-2020, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T15:05:25-07:00","id":1394638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394607#post1394607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the idea of Thin Blood Alchemy either. It seems so random. If the thin bloods are going to have a special Discipline, it should be a power which reduces or negates vampiric weaknesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, I feel like the V5 Thin Bloods are weaker than the Revised version. The Thin Bloods previously had 3 dots in Disciplines didn't they? Now they can have none.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T15:09:01-07:00","id":1394639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394638#post1394638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, I feel like the V5 Thin Bloods are weaker than the Revised version. The Thin Bloods previously had 3 dots in Disciplines didn't they? Now they can have none.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely. They get a dot based off of the last blood they drank and depending on the strength of resonance they can get two. Also, there is the trait that allows them to take a discipline as an out of cost discipline. Also, alchemy does allow for discipline replication up to fourth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T15:43:48-07:00","id":1394642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394638#post1394638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, I feel like the V5 Thin Bloods are weaker than the Revised version. The Thin Bloods previously had 3 dots in Disciplines didn't they? Now they can have none.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compare that to ghoul families, they were slightly more powerful, for more weaknesses","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T15:56:17-07:00","id":1394647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394642#post1394642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Compare that to ghoul families, they were slightly more powerful, for more weaknesses</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, basically Thin Bloods were something that I felt were about Revenant power which is to say, &quot;Ghouls +&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T16:34:49-07:00","id":1394656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394638#post1394638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I feel like the V5 Thin Bloods are weaker than the Revised version. The Thin Bloods previously had 3 dots in Disciplines didn't they? Now they can have none.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the Thin-Bloods feel like a completely different entity than they were in Revised/V20.<br /> <br /> In the previous editions they were weaker, but still functioned like other vampires for the most part. They took damage the same way (though sunlight was only lethal to 15/16th Gen it still burned them with no option to mitigate it completely) and had normal vampire disciplines for the most part (inceptors were rare) that they learned up to the 4th, 3rd or 2nd dot depending on their generation. Biological activity was a rare side-effect in 15-16th gens of having spent large amounts of blood and not a regular occurrence.<br /> <br /> Now they take damage like mortals, can walk around in sunlight and be biologically indistinguishable from a human, pick up random disciplines from feeding while not (usually) being able to actually permanently learn any, but can mix their blood up with things like nylon or what have you to create what amount to magic potions.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t even want to think about how V5 intends to implement Dhampirs given these changes (and on the few occasions I get to play instead of run, Dhampirs are my jam). Hunger dice don\u2019t fit the previous lore where expending their supernatural mojo left them exhausted rather than hungry.<br /> <br /> For similar reasons picking up disciplines from feeding doesn\u2019t fit Dhampirs since they can\u2019t actually feed on humans at all, their supernatural energy is restored with time and rest. And a lot of fun with a Dhampir was specifically in having a very limited, but also specific set of tools to use to help you survive in the world with vampires.<br /> <br /> The problem I foresee is that with how they\u2019ve set up V5, the thin-bloods ate quite a bit of the Dhampirs conceptual space while also incorporating things that make them utterly un-Dhampir-like (in the sense of how they worked in Revised/V20) so you can\u2019t really use a thin-blood to play a Dhampir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T16:36:59-07:00","id":1394657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394656#post1394656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I foresee is that with how they\u2019ve set up V5, the thin-bloods ate quite a bit of the Dhampirs conceptual space while also incorporating things that make them utterly un-Dhampir-like (in the sense of how they worked in Revised/V20) so you can\u2019t really use a thin-blood to play a Dhampir.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I wouldn't be surprised if Dhampyr are Thin Bloods now. It would work pretty well if those &quot;born&quot; vampires use the same skills.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T18:44:18-07:00","id":1394690,"title":"","content":"<u>Lasombra in V5</u><br /> <br /> <b>What I liked</b><br /> <br /> 1. <b>Betrayal-Five</b>: I liked the idea of the Lasombra betraying the Sabbat because I've always had it told to me the Lasombra are treacherous, they're untrustworthy, they only care about themselves, and they are Social Darwinists to the extreme. We rarely got to see it, though because they were so neck deep in the Sabbat and hunted down anyone who joined the Camarilla. It worked for me because it was a genuine surprise they would turn on their fellows like Littlefinger did Ned Stark. They TOLD US they were untrustworthy after all.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>More Lasombra in the Camarilla</b>: I've always liked the Lasombra and feel like their strengths and clan culture play well to the Camarilla. They're riddled with intrigue, infighting, politics, and subtlety. That kind of thing exists in the Sabbat but it's not really an environment that brings out their absolute best since the Sabbat are more like Klingons than Romulans. Monomancy means that you never really get Toreador games of gossip and frame-ups.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The Antediluvian being alive is out of the bag</b>: This happened in BJD but this is now much more overtly so. It's been a secret for 600 years and it's nice to see it finally revealed to the rest of the Lasombra clan even if it's by word of mouth rather than the alternative.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>The idea of a &quot;Lasombra Silent Majority&quot;</b>: I like the idea that Sierra represented. There's apparently a bunch of Sabbat who would love to gather power among mortals and mundane resources but are forced to avoid it because of the responsibilities to their pack. It shows that the Camarilla would have an appeal to some of them so they could just build their own kingdoms of resources.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>The Cult of Shalim</b>: I believe Shalim is the Lasombra Antediluvian rather than an ancient eldritch horror because I like the idea that it's transcended things and wants to unmake creation but either way, it's nice to have a kind of Nephandi-esque group.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Marcus Vitel is responsible for the Lasombra Defection</b>: I love a lot of the classic NPCs and it's great when they get mentioned or incorporated into the existing plotlines. Marcus Vitel having retaken Washington D.C. from the Sabbat with the Anarchs, only to work to get his Clan to convert to the Camarilla (despite the fact the Camarilla almost killed him) strikes me as the kind of genius chessmaster moves you expect from a Methuselah. I also appreciate the inclusion of Talley.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>The Sacrifice is kickass</b>: Possibly the best Chronicle ever made for a vampire supplement. Making the Lasombra join the Camarilla based on PC decision may be a bit fanservice but it's fanservice I can get behind.<br /> <br /> <b>What I didn't like</b><br /> <br /> 1. <b>Not much Sabbat information</b>: We get some allusions to what the Sabbat are up to in the Gehenna War and that some are doing their usual thing when the Lasombra defect but I felt they could have inserted a little info about the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Obternation</b>: Frankly, I think some of the combinations of Disciplines don't make much sense. Quietus is mixed with Blood Sorcery? Necromancy is mixed with Obternation? I feel like the combination is a good idea in general but I feel like the choices are counter-intuitive. Obternation and Quietus should have been mixed with Obfuscate. Necromancy should have mixed with Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The Lasombra Bane</b>: Is ridiculous as there's no reason that Lasombra should have a problem with technology. This is nothing that was hinted at in previous editions and makes their Bane even worse than the Nosferatus (which was dialed back to &quot;really fucking ugly&quot; not &quot;monstrous nightmare creature&quot;). It also means they have to have ghouls when I think the Lasombra have never been a ghoul-heavy clan, that's been the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>No Lucita</b>: Nuff said. Even more so if she's actually dead-dead.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Lasombra craftiness is told not shown</b>: The Lasombra are going to agree to be Blood Bound to the Princes because they know about the Vinculum and the Camarilla doesn't. Also, they know that they have to kill a bunch of Sabbat on their way out so, &quot;Deliver a dead Sabbat Elder for your defection&quot; is fine. However, that's mostly left to inference. We should have had it spelled out the Keepers were playing the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-06-2020, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T23:41:11-07:00","id":1394731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394690#post1394690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Lasombra in V5</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What I didn't like</b><br /> <br /> <br /> 2. <b>Obternation</b>: Frankly, I think some of the combinations of Disciplines don't make much sense. Quietus is mixed with Blood Sorcery? Necromancy is mixed with Obternation? I feel like the combination is a good idea in general but I feel like the choices are counter-intuitive. Obternation and Quietus should have been mixed with Obfuscate. Necromancy should have mixed with Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You run into the 5 power limit, you merger Obfuscate with Quietus and Banu are having to choose between their clan iconic Quietus powees, and being able to effectively hide to get close enough to use them, plus given the merger of 2 clan disciplines what do you give them instead? For all it breaks the cosmic Horror of Obtenerbration, at least merging it with Necromancy is not likely to give massive issues of choice paralysis, Protean, Serpentis and Viscittitude all being merged may just give you similar choice paralysis, depending on how exactly it is done","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 06-07-2020, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T03:43:19-07:00","id":1394744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394657#post1394657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I wouldn't be surprised if Dhampyr are Thin Bloods now. It would work pretty well if those &amp;quot;born&amp;quot; vampires use the same skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which destroys the entire point of Dhampirs NOT needing or even being able to feed from humans; That they aren\u2019t monsters simply for being born.<br /> <br /> It also runs against all the real world lore on half-vampires where they gain some of the vampire\u2019s strengths (which make them better at hunting vampires) and none of the weaknesses and most importantly do NOT feed on their fellow mortals.<br /> <br /> Decisions like that... just completely retconing not just the mechanics, but the entire foundation of the concept (you could roll up a Blade or Alucard or even a Buffy-ish style Dhampir previously)... if that\u2019s where they go with it, do themselves no favors.<br /> <br /> It would be just one more log on the pile of things that ensure I\u2019ll be sticking with V20 because V5 was definitely not written for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T08:29:40-07:00","id":1394777,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of having playable LaSombra on the camarilla becuase they are one of my fav clans but the execution is horrible...<br /> <br /> <b>- The Clan Bane is a death sentence</b>: maybe even worse than the nosferatu one due to how easy is to spot them thanks to lack of reflection on the era of the cristal castles not to mention that they being technological disabled makes them likely to go the endangered species list.<br /> <br /> <b>- They are politically fucked: </b>they have it worse than thin bloods becuase thin bloods can just mind their bussiness or join the anarchs if discovered , LaSombra however not only start as nobodies in the Camarilla , they are view as manipulative bastards and traitors so nobody wants to be their ally or trust them wich makes the majority of them unable to do their thing and participate in deep politics.<br /> <br /> <b>-Their heads have a price:</b> All the reamining sabbat has a personal reason to steal their blood and soul and they didnt need one to being with ,worse is the sheriff and princes wouldnt be doing anything to stop that becuase why risk their unlife when they can watch them kill each other.<br /> <br /> <b>- Hecata do the same withtout those disadvantages:</b>Why would anyone play a LaSombra when the Hecata got the same spread and are actually player friendly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T09:15:24-07:00","id":1394786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394638#post1394638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, I feel like the V5 Thin Bloods are weaker than the Revised version. The Thin Bloods previously had 3 dots in Disciplines didn't they? Now they can have none.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing to remind, BJD made spefically a Point that Thinblood is not automatically Caitiff or High Generation. Both can happen though rarely on low Generations too but yeah with Generation 14 + it is plainly clear they got weaker. If they are in V5 even weaker then before I can not say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394656#post1394656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the Thin-Bloods feel like a completely different entity than they were in Revised/V20.<br /> <br /> In the previous editions they were weaker, but still functioned like other vampires for the most part. They took damage the same way (though sunlight was only lethal to 15/16th Gen it still burned them with no option to mitigate it completely) and had normal vampire disciplines for the most part (inceptors were rare) that they learned up to the 4th, 3rd or 2nd dot depending on their generation. Biological activity was a rare side-effect in 15-16th gens of having spent large amounts of blood and not a regular occurrence.<br /> <br /> Now they take damage like mortals, can walk around in sunlight and be biologically indistinguishable from a human, pick up random disciplines from feeding while not (usually) being able to actually permanently learn any, but can mix their blood up with things like nylon or what have you to create what amount to magic potions.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t even want to think about how V5 intends to implement Dhampirs given these changes (and on the few occasions I get to play instead of run, Dhampirs are my jam). Hunger dice don\u2019t fit the previous lore where expending their supernatural mojo left them exhausted rather than hungry.<br /> <br /> For similar reasons picking up disciplines from feeding doesn\u2019t fit Dhampirs since they can\u2019t actually feed on humans at all, their supernatural energy is restored with time and rest. And a lot of fun with a Dhampir was specifically in having a very limited, but also specific set of tools to use to help you survive in the world with vampires.<br /> <br /> The problem I foresee is that with how they\u2019ve set up V5, the thin-bloods ate quite a bit of the Dhampirs conceptual space while also incorporating things that make them utterly un-Dhampir-like (in the sense of how they worked in Revised/V20) so you can\u2019t really use a thin-blood to play a Dhampir.</div> </div> </div> </div>While TotTB said Dhampir is technically a Revenant there are different rules in BJD diary where it is said, that Dhampirs can feed and so create more vitae from plain blood instead of Revenants that beside drinking from a Vampire there is only the option to wait.<br /> But being able to create blood from Vitae is after comparesing the only real advantege in comparison to Revenants. While Dahmpirs pay at Creation same for Disciples as normal vampires they get less freebies then Revenants and need to pay the same amount of XP as Ghouls for learning disciples but can not even go beyond one Dot even if they would drink Vitae from a low generation vampire. So as much as I love Dhampirs from my opinion they overdid with saying &quot;Dhampirs are just Vampires with ultrathinblood.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T09:47:06-07:00","id":1394791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394744#post1394744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which destroys the entire point of Dhampirs NOT needing or even being able to feed from humans; That they aren\u2019t monsters simply for being born.<br /> <br /> It also runs against all the real world lore on half-vampires where they gain some of the vampire\u2019s strengths (which make them better at hunting vampires) and none of the weaknesses and most importantly do NOT feed on their fellow mortals.<br /> <br /> <b>Decisions like that... just completely retconing not just the mechanics, but the entire foundation of the concept (you could roll up a Blade or Alucard or even a Buffy-ish style Dhampir previously)... if that\u2019s where they go with it, do themselves no favors.</b><br /> <br /> It would be just one more log on the pile of things that ensure I\u2019ll be sticking with V20 because V5 was definitely not written for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, before you continue, I should note that dhampirs would be among the only Kindred who could sustain themselves reliably and without difficulty on animal blood. Not only would animal blood not be like drinking a rancid pool, it would be perfectly normal for a human to eat animals.<br /> <br /> Part of what makes Thin Bloods capable of living among humans whereas most vampires can't.<br /> <br /> V5 made the call lower generations can't drink animal blood at all, which I think was an interesting retcon. Even high generation are like, &quot;Animal blood. BLEAH!&quot; While Thin Bloods go, &quot;Yummy!&quot;<br /> <br /> As for dhampyr:<br /> <br /> Blade, D (Vampire Hunter D), and Alucard have all CRAVED blood. They just have ways around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:05:22-07:00","id":1394794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394777#post1394777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of having playable LaSombra on the camarilla becuase they are one of my fav clans but the execution is horrible...<br /> <br /> <b>- The Clan Bane is a death sentence</b>: maybe even worse than the nosferatu one due to how easy is to spot them thanks to lack of reflection on the era of the cristal castles not to mention that they being technological disabled makes them likely to go the endangered species list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, the Clan Bane is terrible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>- They are politically fucked: </b>they have it worse than thin bloods becuase thin bloods can just mind their business or join the anarchs if discovered , LaSombra however not only start as nobodies in the Camarilla , they are view as manipulative bastards and traitors so nobody wants to be their ally or trust them wich makes the majority of them unable to do their thing and participate in deep politics. </div> </div> </div>I believe the Lasombra will be running the Camarilla in ten years. They're at their strongest politically at the very beginning because the Ventrue are at a position where they have lost their traditional allies in the Tremere and are the Clan who invited the Keepers to join in the first place. The Banu Haqim also are in need of new allies in the Camarilla and have no problem with the Lasombra so they already have a wonderful new ally of convenience. Throwing out the Brujah and Gangrel mean that two clans who would have hated them are also gone. Yes, the Lasombra will be a pillar of the Establishment as soon as they join.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>-Their heads have a price:</b> All the reamining sabbat has a personal reason to steal their blood and soul and they didnt need one to being with ,worse is the sheriff and princes wouldnt be doing anything to stop that becuase why risk their unlife when they can watch them kill each other. </div> </div> </div>Uh, no, this is what it was like BEFORE they defected en masse. The books HATED Lasombra Antitribu and said that the entire Sabbat was going to hunt down and exterminate any member of the Keepers who defected or wasn't a member of their group. Part of the reason why the Lasombra defection happened was because they were such a popular Camarilla clan in LARPS and games to begin with. Now the Sabbat can't go after them because the Lasombra defectors are an army.<br /> <br /> In LA BY NIGHT, the Lasombra notably ARE the Sheriffs and Scourges because the Lasombra are willing to do the murderous shit work the Brujah and Gangrel used to do. The Lasombra are full of hardened soldiers who don't mind killing their fellow Kindred.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>- Hecata do the same withtout those disadvantages:</b>Why would anyone play a LaSombra when the Hecata got the same spread and are actually player friendly? </div> </div> </div>Because the Hecata will never wield an ounce of the power the Lasombra will in the Camarilla. I predict in a few years they'll be the replacement for the Tremere in second most powerful Camarilla clan. The Hecata aren't a member clan and are uninterested in vampire power and prestige.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-07-2020, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:08:38-07:00","id":1394796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394791#post1394791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, before you continue, I should note that dhampirs would be among the only Kindred who could sustain themselves reliably and without difficulty on animal blood. Not only would animal blood not be like drinking a rancid pool, it would be perfectly normal for a human to eat animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus, have you been possessed by the ghost of Aya Tari?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:09:34-07:00","id":1394797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/mai