f=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:10:57-07:00","id":1394798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394797#post1394797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I used to play vegetarian vampires.</span><br /> <br /> I'M SO ASHAMED!</div> </div> </div> </div>kill it with fire","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:14:55-07:00","id":1394800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394798#post1394798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> kill it with fire</div> </div> </div> </div>On a more serious note, one of the subtler changes of V5 is that they codified that generation changes the kind of blood you can successfully drink. I used to play an 8th generation animal blood drinking Ventrue (which was against the rules but I was 14-16 when I played him). Now, only 11th, 12th, and 13th generation vampires can drink animal blood. Also, Thin Bloods who are capable of living on the blood of animals without difficulty. I think that's one of the biggest advantages of both the Gangrel, Nosferatu, and Thin Bloods in general. Those three clans can feed off sources of blood that other Kindred would find unpalatable.<br /> <br /> Thin Bloods can be &quot;Friendly Neighborhood Vampires&quot; because they don't frenzy except under exceptional circumstances, can live off animal blood, or amounts of blood that won't kill regular humans.<br /> <br /> Normal vampires? They're an ever-continuing threat to humans around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:32:09-07:00","id":1394804,"title":"","content":"I really don't like that codifying. I've always considered &quot;methuselah's thirst&quot; and stuff like that to be rumours and 'let's kill elders'/don't diablerize propaganda. It was something to terrify younger vampires and cases would pop up from time to time as evidence of it's existence (They would be exceptions, not the norm, but neonates wouldn't know that) <br /> <br /> I never read the &quot;Dhampir&quot; book or whatever, so I just made the assumption they were revenants with different origins. (and they would have revenant children if you paired them up with other revenants; One needs only imagine how you can start your own revenant family this way) <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're at their strongest politically at the very beginning because the Ventrue are at a position where they have lost their traditional allies in the Tremere and are the Clan who invited the Keepers to join in the first place. The Banu Haqim also are in need of new allies in the Camarilla and have no problem with the Lasombra so they already have a wonderful new ally of convenience. Throwing out the Brujah and Gangrel mean that two clans who would have hated them are also gone. Yes, the Lasombra will be a pillar of the Establishment as soon as they join. </div> </div> </div>1- The Tremere are still there. The Ventrue grew to see them as bothersome rivals more than &quot;friends&quot;. I believe House Carna is a Facade, so I don't think this is a very valid point. The Ventrue would be stronger with a seemingly weakened Tremere. <br /> 1B- Toreador are better allies for ventrue, and there are a lot more of them. <br /> 2- I'm not sure why the Ventrue would invite them in En-mass. It could be prestration related, but the only other reason I see the Ventrue inviting the Lasombra in would be a &quot;Not the best ally but would be a worse enemy&quot; kinda thing. <br /> 3- What hatred do Brujah and Gangrel have towards lasombra? Or at least, why would the throwout of the Brujah and Gangrel benefit the Lasombra more than it would the Ventrue, Tremere, Toreador, nosferatu or malkavians?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:35:35-07:00","id":1394806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394656#post1394656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the Thin-Bloods feel like a completely different entity than they were in Revised/V20.<br /> <br /> In the previous editions they were weaker, but still functioned like other vampires for the most part. They took damage the same way (though sunlight was only lethal to 15/16th Gen it still burned them with no option to mitigate it completely) and had normal vampire disciplines for the most part (inceptors were rare) that they learned up to the 4th, 3rd or 2nd dot depending on their generation. Biological activity was a rare side-effect in 15-16th gens of having spent large amounts of blood and not a regular occurrence.<br /> <br /> Now they take damage like mortals, can walk around in sunlight and be biologically indistinguishable from a human, pick up random disciplines from feeding while not (usually) being able to actually permanently learn any, but can mix their blood up with things like nylon or what have you to create what amount to magic potions.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t even want to think about how V5 intends to implement Dhampirs given these changes (and on the few occasions I get to play instead of run, Dhampirs are my jam). Hunger dice don\u2019t fit the previous lore where expending their supernatural mojo left them exhausted rather than hungry.<br /> <br /> For similar reasons picking up disciplines from feeding doesn\u2019t fit Dhampirs since they can\u2019t actually feed on humans at all, their supernatural energy is restored with time and rest. And a lot of fun with a Dhampir was specifically in having a very limited, but also specific set of tools to use to help you survive in the world with vampires.<br /> <br /> The problem I foresee is that with how they\u2019ve set up V5, the thin-bloods ate quite a bit of the Dhampirs conceptual space while also incorporating things that make them utterly un-Dhampir-like (in the sense of how they worked in Revised/V20) so you can\u2019t really use a thin-blood to play a Dhampir.</div> </div> </div> </div>They take superficial damage that will cycle into aggravated damage in sunlight. There is an option for day walking, but it is not default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:36:40-07:00","id":1394809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394797#post1394797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I used to play vegetarian vampires.</span><br /> <br /> I'M SO ASHAMED!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/403ae5b6f76180b323f2169d9d937fed/tumblr_nrov4dvFKt1u9jpmmo2_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Forever Knight works better in VtR anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 06-07-2020, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:44:53-07:00","id":1394814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394791#post1394791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, before you continue, I should note that dhampirs would be among the only Kindred who could sustain themselves reliably and without difficulty on animal blood. Not only would animal blood not be like drinking a rancid pool, it would be perfectly normal for a human to eat animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has this already been in V1-V20 or is this is a VTMV newcommer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:48:25-07:00","id":1394817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394814#post1394814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Has this already been in V1-V20 or is this is a VTMV newcommer?</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is where it established lower generations could not drink animal blood. It was fluff before and now it's crunch.<br /> <br /> It was also established in fluff that Thin Bloods could drink animal blood without the revulsion other Kindred had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T11:09:47-07:00","id":1394820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394814#post1394814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Has this already been in V1-V20 or is this is a VTMV newcommer?</div> </div> </div> </div>back in revised (V3)<br /> feeding on animals increased the difficulty to resist frenzy when presented with opportunity to drink better blood<br /> <br /> however, nobody used that rule, because it was hidden in the Camarilla book under the description of an elder discipline that most people missed<br /> <br /> and the people who knew about it would eventually forget where they saw it...ahh, the good old days","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T11:32:16-07:00","id":1394828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394690#post1394690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>What I didn't like</b><br /> <br /> 1. <b>Not much Sabbat information</b>: We get some allusions to what the Sabbat are up to in the Gehenna War and that some are doing their usual thing when the Lasombra defect but I felt they could have inserted a little info about the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Obternation</b>: Frankly, I think some of the combinations of Disciplines don't make much sense. Quietus is mixed with Blood Sorcery? Necromancy is mixed with Obternation? I feel like the combination is a good idea in general but I feel like the choices are counter-intuitive. Obternation and Quietus should have been mixed with Obfuscate. Necromancy should have mixed with Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The Lasombra Bane</b>: Is ridiculous as there's no reason that Lasombra should have a problem with technology. This is nothing that was hinted at in previous editions and makes their Bane even worse than the Nosferatus (which was dialed back to &quot;really fucking ugly&quot; not &quot;monstrous nightmare creature&quot;). It also means they have to have ghouls when I think the Lasombra have never been a ghoul-heavy clan, that's been the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>No Lucita</b>: Nuff said. Even more so if she's actually dead-dead.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Lasombra craftiness is told not shown</b>: The Lasombra are going to agree to be Blood Bound to the Princes because they know about the Vinculum and the Camarilla doesn't. Also, they know that they have to kill a bunch of Sabbat on their way out so, &quot;Deliver a dead Sabbat Elder for your defection&quot; is fine. However, that's mostly left to inference. We should have had it spelled out the Keepers were playing the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>2 - quietus was blood sorcery turned into a discipline, even in MtA it was considered blood sorcery.<br /> Obfuscate is a mind power,<br /> unless you're suggesting turning obfuscate into a not-a-mind-power, which I might be ok with<br /> <br /> 4 - she should've been the one to die along with Talley,<br /> instead they killed Valez, and Valez wasn't even an elder, actually she's not even ancillae, she a neonate, disgraced abbott disowned by her sire with no known ties to the Amici or whatever,<br /> and she's the one taking one for the hood?<br /> and Talley was ok with that?<br /> and he's the good guy in all this?<br /> not that I'd be surprised if Talley was too dumb to tell the difference (guy is a plank), and considering the the Camarilla history in V5, they're probably just as dumb<br /> <br /> 5 - nah that's just the authors showing you how the camarilla is turning into the sabbat,<br /> just wait till the sabbat are back and realize the sect got bigger in their absence,<br /> Lasombra are playing some 18 dimensional chess game,<br /> Darth Sidious would be proud<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T11:41:34-07:00","id":1394831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394828#post1394828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 - she should've been the one to die along with Talley,<br /> instead they killed Valez, and Valez wasn't even an elder, actually she's not even ancillae, she a neonate, disgraced abbott disowned by her sire with no known ties to the Amici or whatever,<br /> and she's the one taking one for the hood?<br /> and Talley was ok with that?<br /> and he's the good guy in all this?<br /> not that I'd be surprised if Talley was too dumb to tell the difference (guy is a plank), and considering the the Camarilla history in V5, they're probably just as dumb</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Lucita is someone I support as long as they don't try to get her to convert to the Sabbat and lose everything interesting about her. *glares at Lasombra trilogy*<br /> <br /> 2. Valez was killed by Lasombra to show that they're in the state of a Civil War, I think. You need someone popular and well-liked to die in order to show the stakes (pun intended).<br /> <br /> 3. Obviously Valez wasn't willingly giving herself up to the flames. The whole thing is framed like a forced confession from the Inquisition or Soviet Union. I thought that was obvious.<br /> <br /> 4. Talley is not a good guy and neither are the defectors. They're still the same slimy and evil Lasombra they always were. LA By Night actually has a running subplot that the Sabbat defectors in Los Angeles are killing, torturing, and abusing Anarchs to the point they've successfully united the entirety of California's Anarchs against the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> 5. I doubt Talley was the one who killed Valez. It was probably some Neonate Lasombra younger than her as the deal is &quot;any Lasombra older than you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5 - nah that's just the authors showing you how the camarilla is turning into the sabbat,<br /> just wait till the sabbat are back and realize the sect got bigger in their absence,<br /> Lasombra are playing some 18 dimensional chess game,<br /> Darth Sidious would be proud </div> </div> </div>Hey, it's what the Lasombra are good at. Seriously, though, I felt that the Lasombra were meant to be established as having a strong enough bargaining position that they make the Camarilla's conditions look ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T11:52:50-07:00","id":1394834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394744#post1394744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also runs against all the real world lore on half-vampires where they gain some of the vampire\u2019s strengths (which make them better at hunting vampires) and none of the weaknesses and most importantly do NOT feed on their fellow mortals.<br /> <br /> Decisions like that... just completely retconing not just the mechanics, but the entire foundation of the concept (you could roll up a Blade or Alucard or even a Buffy-ish style Dhampir previously)... if that\u2019s where they go with it, do themselves no favors.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the movies Blade has the same hunger for human blood vampires do and takes a <i>specially prepared serum</i> to counteract it. He's also not notably fragile or weak compared to full-on regular vampires. He really fits the V5 Thin Blood mold better than the Revised/V20 Dhamphir one. He's just a Thin Blood who's been combat-trained since he was a teenager and funnels all the XP from a very active lifestyle into making himself more physically formidable rather than developing political acumen or spooky overtly supernatural powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 06-07-2020, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T11:54:49-07:00","id":1394836,"title":"","content":"I always treated Theo Bell as the WOD version of Blade.<br /> <br /> When you have Potence and Celerity of 5 plus a katana, you can be Blade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T12:18:00-07:00","id":1394839,"title":"","content":"Blade seems to have the physical prowess to equal or surpass nearly any vampire. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s good for V:tM thin bloods or dhampirs to be like that. They should have fewer vampire weaknesses, but they should also have fewer and weaker vampire powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T12:21:59-07:00","id":1394840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394839#post1394839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blade seems to have the physical prowess to equal or surpass nearly any vampire. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s good for V:tM thin bloods or dhampirs to be like that. They should have fewer vampire weaknesses, but they should also have fewer and weaker vampire powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Though funnily, the 25 Years of V:TM guys pointed out all of Blade's equipment showed up in THE FALL OF LONDON.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T14:26:47-07:00","id":1394852,"title":"","content":"Does it include the Titanium sword? <br /> <br /> I can see a good in-universe justification for a lot of the metaplot. The Cam downsizes, The Sabbat elders are in on it, The Cam turns it's neonates anarch whilst the Sabbat elders throw their childer to the middle east, All the elders get together to shield themselves from the SI they're using to kill all the young vampires. The Camarilla allows open religion because they're mostly elders now who don't need to lie to a bunch of neonates/Religious persecution's not cool anymore/The Sabbat elders asked for it. There's some cool ideas in there. Certainly not everything can be explained, some of it's straight up nonsense, but the thing i just described kinda works. <br /> <br /> I still don't like it though. <br /> <br /> The only thing I find interesting about V5's lasombra is that they're in the Camarilla now and also Tentacles is less masquerade breaking... But I still dislike the way the former is done, and the latter... I think the discipline's point was that it was freaky demon shit, it should be very overt. Little shadows aren't really that upsetting. I think, if things were the otherway round, and a once-subtle discipline became very overt, i'd be upset about it, because generally I think powers should follow the path-of-least-resistance when it comes to special effects and the masquerade. But the power has been established as freakishly horrifying for four editions now, and it's overt supernatural nature has been one of the power's &quot;weaknesses&quot; to ofset it's strength. What we have in V5 suits the Camarilla better. What we had before suited the Sabbat better. I can't really imagine someone path-of-nighting with the new less overt obtenebration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T14:40:06-07:00","id":1394854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394791#post1394791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, before you continue, I should note that dhampirs would be among the only Kindred who could sustain themselves reliably and without difficulty on animal blood. Not only would animal blood not be like drinking a rancid pool, it would be perfectly normal for a human to eat animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, for me, having to drink ANY blood and the associated hunger that might cause you to feed on and kill a human is an absolute NO SELL for me. VtM Dhampirs get tired from pushing themselves, they don\u2019t start trying to eat people no matter how drained they get and that is the appeal to me.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs are my way of interfacing with VtM in a way I am comfortable with without needing to go outside the VtM mythos by bringing in something like a Mage. I do NOT play characters who could lose control and eat someone... it holds less than zero interest to me.<br /> <br /> I have zero desire to engage with V5\u2019s hunger mechanics. I find the \u201cmust kill a human to reach hunger 0\u201d morally repugnant and so would would never play anything using those mechanics.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs had their own set of mechanics that made them something I could play. I pray the V5 devs pay no attention to your ideas on this so that, maybe someday, I might actually be able to give the system a try. Your ideas hold no appeal to me at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T16:30:47-07:00","id":1394869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394854#post1394854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, for me, having to drink ANY blood and the associated hunger that might cause you to feed on and kill a human is an absolute NO SELL for me. VtM Dhampirs get tired from pushing themselves, they don\u2019t start trying to eat people no matter how drained they get and that is the appeal to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>What fictional dhampyrs don't hunger for blood? I'm curious. Serious question.<br /> <br /> And I believe V5 actually made Thin Bloods not frenzy unless they're magically induced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 113</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hunger and Frenzy</b><br /> <br /> A thin-blood suffers hunger just as<br /> any vampire. However, the Beast<br /> is far less overt, and a thin-blood<br /> never frenzies unless provoked by<br /> supernatural means (such as Animalism,<br /> p. 244).</div> </div> </div> </div>So, yes, you're aces in playing a Thin Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-07-2020, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T16:35:18-07:00","id":1394872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394869#post1394869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What fictional dhampyrs don't hunger for blood? I'm curious. Serious question.<br /> <br /> And I believe V5 actually made Thin Bloods not frenzy unless they're magically induced.<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Ones from Golarion don't, they CAN but they don't need to, or in many cases want to (but Golarion is the setting for Pathfinder, and it has strange undead anyway)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:32:48-07:00","id":1394901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394869#post1394869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What fictional dhampyrs don't hunger for blood? I'm curious. Serious question.</div> </div> </div> </div>To start with, the ones in Revised and V20.<br /> <br /> Those should be the only ones that matter, but if that\u2019s not enough, then how about the actual Balkans legends of dhampirs where they are mostly normal, but have magical powers that allow them to hunt vampires. Time of Thin Blood even included flaws related to some of the hindrences associated with some of the Balkans legends like having soft bones.<br /> <br /> All I want is for Dhampirs to work like they did previously and not be retconned into something else entirely (which is retgone masquerading as a retcon). Is that really too much to ask for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:41:57-07:00","id":1394908,"title":"","content":"so, there are people who play VtM but don't want to play the bloodthirsty monsters?<br /> <br /> I always thought the whole dhampir thing was only used for npcs...color me surprised<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:43:04-07:00","id":1394911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394908#post1394908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so, there are people who play VtM but don't want to play the bloodthirsty monsters?<br /> <br /> I always thought the whole dhampir thing was only used for npcs...color me surprised</div> </div> </div> </div>FYI, the dhampyrs aren't confirmed to be Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> It was just a thought.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T18:40:15-07:00","id":1394926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394908#post1394908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so, there are people who play VtM but don't want to play the bloodthirsty monsters?<br /> <br /> I always thought the whole dhampir thing was only used for npcs...color me surprised</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer Mage. My friends all prefer Vampire. The compromise is I get to run a non-bloodthirsty supernatural that is tied to VtM lore (and isn\u2019t a blood bound slave either).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:06:36-07:00","id":1394951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394901#post1394901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To start with, the ones in Revised and V20.<br /> <br /> Those should be the only ones that matter, but if that\u2019s not enough, then how about the actual Balkans legends of dhampirs where they are mostly normal, but have magical powers that allow them to hunt vampires. Time of Thin Blood even included flaws related to some of the hindrences associated with some of the Balkans legends like having soft bones.<br /> <br /> All I want is for Dhampirs to work like they did previously and not be retconned into something else entirely (which is retgone masquerading as a retcon). Is that really too much to ask for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to look for inspiration in actual dhampir legends for this project; you are welcome to take a look:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\"> The hungry dead - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Strigoi: The hungry dead Why? I have wanted, for a long time, to create European creatures akin to the Wan Kuei. This is the first beta version. A summary: This </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:10:28-07:00","id":1394954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394926#post1394926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer Mage. My friends all prefer Vampire. The compromise is I get to run a non-bloodthirsty supernatural that is tied to VtM lore (and isn\u2019t a blood bound slave either).</div> </div> </div> </div>Something similar happened to me once: all my friends wanted to play Hunter: the Reckoning. I played a Mummy (from Mummy:the Resurrection); I made a point of helping them and staying away from their Conviction-addled-sight... (aka visions)<br /> <br /> By the way, have you considered playing a Mummy? One interested in helping the Cainites realize the depths of dammnation they are in and wanting to help them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T04:19:57-07:00","id":1395051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394926#post1394926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer Mage. My friends all prefer Vampire. The compromise is I get to run a non-bloodthirsty supernatural that is tied to VtM lore (and isn\u2019t a blood bound slave either).</div> </div> </div> </div>makes sense,<br /> though a dhampir must feel like a huge downgrade from a Mage, unless you use hedge magic<br /> <br /> I believe there are also undead mages in VtM, liches or something, but I don't know how they work<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T04:55:51-07:00","id":1395054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395051#post1395051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> makes sense,<br /> though a dhampir must feel like a huge downgrade from a Mage, unless you use hedge magic<br /> <br /> I believe there are also undead mages in VtM, liches or something, but I don't know how they work</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> they are from MtA, the book Dead Magic, they are weird, and really not suitable as a starting character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T06:16:30-07:00","id":1395065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395051#post1395051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> makes sense, though a dhampir must feel like a huge downgrade from a Mage, unless you use hedge magic</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is way bigger than just Hermetic-style spell slinging. It\u2019s about having the power inside you to change the world... and often through magic that comes off as pure coincidence.<br /> <br /> That might be Hermetic spells, prayers of faith, weird or super-science, mystic martial arts or even just the precision art of persuasion (including a magic paradigm called \u201cmoney makes the world go round/anything for the right price.\u201d).<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s take a look at what even one dot in disciplines can actually do;<br /> - Animalism (talk to and command animals)<br /> - Auspex (heightened senses and a fluky danger sense)<br /> - Celerity (\u201cEverybody was kung fu fightin\u2019. Those dudes were fast as lightnin\u201d)<br /> - Dominate (one word commands on mortals)<br /> - Fortitude (iron body technique)<br /> - Obfuscate (become one with shadows)<br /> - Potence (so many many things, breaking boards and greater leaps are just the start).<br /> - Presence (be a master of persuasion).<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s just the common ones a Dhampir could mostly figure out on their own (and many don\u2019t even require blood - meaning you can hold onto your pool for important things like healing yourself... another useful thing magic in Mage is used for).<br /> <br /> Throw in rarer stuff somehow and you can get weird (one dot in vicissitude and you can be a master of disguise, one in thaumaturgy and you can eventually learn all the level one rituals. Plus, if you\u2019re Dhampir the odds are high that you\u2019re spending more time with thin-bloods and who knows what the first dot of an incepted discipline will let you do.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not earth-shaking, but it can be very flexible. Plus, due to the way the pricing works and lack of much to buy in the way of backgrounds; you\u2019re in good stead to spend freebies on one or more discipline dots and some merits like clear-sighted, iron will unbondable*, virulent strike, true faith, medium, oracular ability, pale aura (good if your concept is to infiltrate undead society as say, a Brujah neonate with celerity, potence and presence 1).<br /> <br /> Willpower 10 as an almost supernatural level of self-control (or luck... if I recall, the quickie Mage stats from Hunter just gave Mages huge pools of Willpower and let them spend multiple points on the same task to reflect their coinciental effects resulting in supernatural luck) is justifiable for some builds.<br /> <br /> And if you want the Dhampir equivalent of \u201cmoney makes the world go round\u201d magic... how about you\u2019re a trust-fund kid with Resources 5, Fame and/or Influence because your thin-blood father knocked up a rich socialite while using his vampiric presence to live the high life... you inherited his magnetic personality, a good family name and a sizable pile of resources when your mom died of complications in childbirth and you were raised by your wealthy grandparents.<br /> <br /> Likewise, keeping up with the Jones isn\u2019t all that hard... while the vamps in the group are buying up more dots in disciplines, you\u2019re topping off your attributes and abilities for way less than in-clan discipline costs.<br /> <br /> The point being... there\u2019s quite a bit of subtle magic you can squeeze out a well-played Dhampir; a lot of which are fairly in keeping with those Balkans legends of half-vampire children who are mostly humans with a bit a magic to them.<br /> <br /> * I\u2019ve gotten more than one Storyteller to let me have unbondable for the lower Mage cost (3 points) since the primary benefit of unbondable for a mortal is you can become a ghoul without being blood bound... but Dhampirs in V20 explicitly cannot become ghouls or use more potent blood to learn disciplines above one dot, so it\u2019s only real use is not being enslaved if someone forces a blood bond on you... a much more limited circumstance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T07:05:02-07:00","id":1395072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394820#post1394820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> back in revised (V3)<br /> feeding on animals increased the difficulty to resist frenzy when presented with opportunity to drink better blood<br /> <br /> however, nobody used that rule, because it was hidden in the Camarilla book under the description of an elder discipline that most people missed<br /> <br /> and the people who knew about it would eventually forget where they saw it...ahh, the good old days</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me on the 6 Dot Animalism Power in V20 which makes each blood point of Animals count as two points and not 1/2 though each 3 times drinking from animals the difficulty on resisting to drink from Kine or Cainit increases on one point cummulative.<br /> If this power whas back then called greenfood then it either got revamped or it whas always the effect of this (optional) power only because vampires without this power can resist from drinking to non animal blood equaly hard no matter if they normally use animal blood to feed or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395065#post1395065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one in thaumaturgy and you can eventually learn all the level one rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dhampirs could theoretically acces True Faith too. About Thaumaturgy there is better to use the DAV20 rules where counterspelling is a different disciple and not just a path of thaumaturgy. Sadly Dhampirs are at real disadvantege whith Thaumaturgy and Necromancy because their paths are locked to only one because they can not unlock the requirements to increase more then one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":".  preventing double post 06-08-2020, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T09:20:48-07:00","id":1395086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395072#post1395072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dhampirs could theoretically acces True Faith too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons, inverted souls, artificial creations: This is the grand list of humanoids that don't have potential for true faith. (Inverted souls being mages who go through the caul, those who walk the black spiral... Not vampires. Vampires are fine and can have as much TF as they can muster) <br /> <br /> I feel like I'm in the minority with true faith: I'll let players use it as it is in the books. From what I've read here, everyone wants to hard-no it or make it something it's not (You don't need to be a priest or really know that much about your faith, that's why it's called faith) <br /> I'll discourage it because high humanity is for wankers and I want to be sure a player can pull it off, but it's available to anyone who wants to throw down 7 points on a power they'll risk losing. <br /> <br /> Lasombra are actually my favourite characters with TF, bar the Baali. There's just something so wonderful about that juxtaposition and reconciliation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T09:33:32-07:00","id":1395090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395072#post1395072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dhampirs could theoretically acces True Faith too. About Thaumaturgy there is better to use the DAV20 rules where counterspelling is a different disciple and not just a path of thaumaturgy. Sadly Dhampirs are at real disadvantege whith Thaumaturgy and Necromancy because their paths are locked to only one because they can not unlock the requirements to increase more then one.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, the best one dot Thaumatury discipline I've found is Movement of the Mind. A pound isn't much, but it IS a set of keys off a desk, a spilled drink or a door rattling like someone's trying to open it at the right time or the petty, but effective, wardrobe malfunction. Add in the first rank of rituals and you've got some reasonable flexibility... provided you could ever get someone to teach you actual blood magic (you'd pretty much need to build your backstory around it; maybe something related to a &quot;sleeping with the enemy&quot; of sorts involving the Arcanum and an thin-blooded Anarch who learned a bit of Old Skool Sorcery and passed it on their kid before getting ganked by someone, but leaving you with your Arcanum parent and their resources to help you puzzle out some reverse engineered versions of the level one rituals).<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Medium merit and maybe one dot in whichever of the Necromancy paths lets you actually see what Ghosts are around may not seem like much, but if you're willing to do some role-playing in order to do favors for the restless dead, you could get almost all the benefits of the Sepulchre path in terms of getting ghosts to do things for you and they won't even hate you for it because you've been helping them out too.<br /> <br /> But yes, between all the various options like True Faith, the first discipline dots, some of the supernatural merits and maybe some Hedge Magic you can actually pull off something like a linear version of many of the Tradition paradigms and practices if you wished to. Akashics, Celestial Chorus, Euthanatos, Hermetics and Verbena being on the easier side.<br /> <br /> Dreamspeaker might also be possible with the right disciplines (animalism, an incepted version of Spiritus, maybe Medium + the first dot in the Path of Spirit Manipulation so you can both see and talk to spirits... then just make actual role-played out deals with them as with the Necromancy version above), but you'd need a very specific backstory to justify it. Alternately Animalism + Auspex + Obfuscate would be a pretty decent Urban Shaman type who knows all sorts of hidden knowledge about the city and what's happening in it.<br /> <br /> Hardest would be the hi-tech paradigms like Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts, but some of the actual Technocrat paradigms like the NWO (auspex + dominate + presence) or Syndicate (all the social backgrounds at high levels) are actually pretty doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T09:49:11-07:00","id":1395092,"title":"","content":"Nah, you can do every paradigm you just described with regular 'blood sorcery'/ Necromancy. It's just a matter of style and beliefs. Check out Rites of the Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T09:56:57-07:00","id":1395095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1394869#post1394869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What fictional dhampyrs don't hunger for blood? I'm curious. Serious question.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Grey Prince from TES4 didn't hunger for blood. He didn't even seem to realise his vampiric heritage until you complete his quest.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is post-Morrowind Bethesda we're talking about, but still.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T10:18:10-07:00","id":1395101,"title":"","content":"Oblivion had a lot of good writing. Sure it had some bad, but it wasnt the regressive shitter of everything that came after<br /> <br /> But also, tes vampires dont really need blood, it's just good stuff. They arent really comparable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T11:48:43-07:00","id":1395121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395092#post1395092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, you can do every paradigm you just described with regular 'blood sorcery'/ Necromancy. It's just a matter of style and beliefs. Check out Rites of the Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have it, but in this case the specific wrinkle is \u201ccan you do most of the things attributed to that paradigm with only one dot in one thaumaturgic path?\u201d Because that\u2019s the limiter if you\u2019re doing it as a Dhampir (half the fun of playing a Dhampir is working around your very hard limits and employing your advantages to best effect).<br /> <br /> That said, I\u2019ve almost never done any Dhampir I\u2019ve played as a straight-up Mage replacement. The main thing for me is not being a parasite, but still being able to play with my friends who prefer Vampire and do so without disrupting the theme and mood too much by bringing some intruding cosmology and enemy groups into the game.<br /> <br /> My current PC has the pale aura and unbondable merits and, with celerity and presence in addition to potence, is passing themselves off as orphaned Brujah fledgling who agreed to be blood bound in order to avoid being destroyed and has been working to secure \u201cfeeding rights\u201d over a group of homeless in order to protect them from being fed on by vampires. Their long term goal is to find out which of the vampires in the city killed their parents and then ruin them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T12:04:48-07:00","id":1395125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395086#post1395086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasombra are actually my favourite characters with TF, bar the Baali. There's just something so wonderful about that juxtaposition and reconciliation.</div> </div> </div> </div>My favorite is still &quot;True Faith: Setite Gnosticism&quot;. The true believers are my favorite type of Setite. (Though I suppose that's also getting off-topic for this thread.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T14:50:22-07:00","id":1395156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395092#post1395092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, you can do every paradigm you just described with regular 'blood sorcery'/ Necromancy. It's just a matter of style and beliefs. Check out Rites of the Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Chris said, with the Only One Dot ceiling you can only get one path each for Necromancy and Thaumaturgy because former needs to have for second path first path on three and three+ paths need to have main path on 5 while Thaumaturgy requires the main path to be always one dot higher then the rest unless you reached five dots with it so a Gen 16 Vampire can have except first all Thaumaturgy paths on one dot, Gen 15 on 2 and Gen 14 on 3 while Gen 16 can not have a second Necromancy path too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T18:42:28-07:00","id":1395194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395156#post1395156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Chris said, with the Only One Dot ceiling you can only get one path each for Necromancy and Thaumaturgy because former needs to have for second path first path on three and three+ paths need to have main path on 5 while Thaumaturgy requires the main path to be always one dot higher then the rest unless you reached five dots with it so a Gen 16 Vampire can have except first all Thaumaturgy paths on one dot, Gen 15 on 2 and Gen 14 on 3 while Gen 16 can not have a second Necromancy path too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always took that as a social restriction, not an intrinsic one, if that makes sense. In other words, the institution of the Tremere Pyramid insists that you learn three dots of one path before starting on another, but if you had extenuating circumstances that could potentially change.<br /> <br /> Though it does raise the question of whether the Tremere will teach it to you in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T20:11:15-07:00","id":1395209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395194#post1395194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always took that as a social restriction, not an intrinsic one, if that makes sense. In other words, the institution of the Tremere Pyramid insists that you learn three dots of one path before starting on another, but if you had extenuating circumstances that could potentially change.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it were a social restriction it wouldn\u2019t apply to other practitioners of blood sorcery, but ot does.<br /> <br /> More likely it\u2019s an enlightenment restriction akin to how in Mage you could only buy spheres up to level of your Arete score. In Thaumaturgical terms this translates to \u201cYou need to understand something at the three-dot level before your brain can start expanding your horizons to other paths and a 5-dot understanding to handle multiple paths at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T20:20:22-07:00","id":1395216,"title":"","content":"New Lasombra Bane suggestions:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Mirror Revulsion</b>: A Lasombra cannot see their reflection in a mirror and if presented with their own lack of reflection, they are at a +2 difficulty to all actions until the mirror is done away with. Normal individuals can see the Lasombra's reflection.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Silver Vulnerability</b>: A silver lined mirror will not show a Lasombra's reflection and they suffer aggravated damage from silver injuries like a werewolf. Normal mirrors, photographs, and video will show them.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Reflectionless</b>: The Lasombra has no image in any reflective surface or photographs (but can be seen on videos or any moving footage). This would keep the essential spirit of the problem without making it too much of an advantage.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Repulsed by Reflections</b>: A Lasombra does not cast a reflection or create their own shadow. Any mirror, photograph, or video larger than a car rearview mirror or handheld one that should show their image but does not results in them having to make a self-control roll. They will also need to make one to allow themselves to be filmed or a photo taken. In short, they react to mirrors and recording devices like most vampires do fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T20:33:40-07:00","id":1395221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395216#post1395216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. <b>Silver Vulnerability</b>: they suffer aggravated damage from silver injuries like a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>This wold make combat LaSombras a little weak, I think. Silver is a hell of a bane, and one thing that really separates the banes of werewolves and vampires is that sunlight and fire are rather difficult to weaponise but silver isn't.<br /> <br /> According to CofD's Armory (I don't know how silver weapons are statted off the top of my head for WoD), they take a -1 penalty to damage and to durability as well if they're melee, but that is a small price to play for doing directly aggravated damage. Vampires wouldn't really have a hard time getting ahold of silver, either.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T20:35:17-07:00","id":1395222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395221#post1395221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This wold make combat LaSombras a little weak, I think. Silver is a hell of a bane, and one thing that really separates the banes of werewolves and vampires is that sunlight and fire are rather difficult to weaponise but silver isn't.<br /> <br /> According to CofD's Armory (I don't know how silver weapons are statted off the top of my head for WoD), they take a -1 penalty to damage and to durability as well if they're melee, but that is a small price to play for doing directly aggravated damage. Vampires wouldn't really have a hard time getting ahold of silver, either.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I doubt the vast majority of vampires are carrying around silver weapons. Let alone anyone else in the world but Pentex. Fire is also a helluva lot more common than silver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T20:48:36-07:00","id":1395225,"title":"","content":"If you knew a given vampire was a LaSombra and you thought an altercation would be likely, there's nothing much stopping you from carrying a silver knife or a mag of silver bullets. This is especially so because, unlike werewolves, other vampires aren't weak to silver and won't get penalised just for carrying them.<br /> <br /> Fire is common, yes, but weaponising it to actually deal significant damage to a vampire is difficult. The most common ways would be something like a molotov where you'd need to basically catch them with it, or Dragon's Breath shotgun shells which are much more limiting than silver bullets. Any bullet could theoretically be made from silver, while Dragon's Breath requires rather specific kinds of shotguns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T21:31:07-07:00","id":1395229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395225#post1395225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you knew a given vampire was a LaSombra and you thought an altercation would be likely, there's nothing much stopping you from carrying a silver knife or a mag of silver bullets. This is especially so because, unlike werewolves, other vampires aren't weak to silver and won't get penalised just for carrying them.<br /> <br /> Fire is common, yes, but weaponising it to actually deal significant damage to a vampire is difficult. The most common ways would be something like a molotov where you'd need to basically catch them with it, or Dragon's Breath shotgun shells which are much more limiting than silver bullets. Any bullet could theoretically be made from silver, while Dragon's Breath requires rather specific kinds of shotguns.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> Fair point. I think it works as a weakness but it is harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T21:42:33-07:00","id":1395232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395216#post1395216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Lasombra Bane suggestions:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Mirror Revulsion</b>: A Lasombra cannot see their reflection in a mirror and if presented with their own lack of reflection, they are at a +2 difficulty to all actions until the mirror is done away with. Normal individuals can see the Lasombra's reflection.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Silver Vulnerability</b>: A silver lined mirror will not show a Lasombra's reflection and they suffer aggravated damage from silver injuries like a werewolf. Normal mirrors, photographs, and video will show them.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Reflectionless</b>: The Lasombra has no image in any reflective surface or photographs (but can be seen on videos or any moving footage). This would keep the essential spirit of the problem without making it too much of an advantage.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Repulsed by Reflections</b>: A Lasombra does not cast a reflection or create their own shadow. Any mirror, photograph, or video larger than a car rearview mirror or handheld one that should show their image but does not results in them having to make a self-control roll. They will also need to make one to allow themselves to be filmed or a photo taken. In short, they react to mirrors and recording devices like most vampires do fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing these would be for V20 or earlier then especially with the self-control roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T22:02:17-07:00","id":1395237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395232#post1395232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing these would be for V20 or earlier then especially with the self-control roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just substitute as appropriate for V5. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T23:31:30-07:00","id":1395254,"title":"","content":"I'm getting so annoyed by the references to the 5-point-cap that I need to read them from my V5 corebook. Until them, I won't pay them any attention. No longer.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, thanks God and all the Forumites here for the latest ideas about the Lasombra. I need to read and reread the Chicago by Night section on them.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I also need school to finish. I'm a secondary school teacher and huge amounts of exams are stalking me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":".  Making it clearer and easier to read. 06-09-2020, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T04:18:49-07:00","id":1395294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong?p=1395216#post1395216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Lasombra Bane suggestions:<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Repulsed by Reflections</b>: A Lasombra does not cast a reflection or create their own shadow. Any mirror, photograph, or video larger than a car rearview mirror or handheld one that should show their image but does not results in them having to make a self-control roll. They will also need to make one to allow themselves to be filmed or a photo taken. In short, they react to mirrors and recording devices like most vampires do fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my favorite of the four because it keeps the essence of the weakness the Lasombra have had since 1992 but hits them with a hefty mechanical penalty they have always needed. Plus, it's <i>entirely</i> in keeping with how Dracula always reacts to mirrors in movies and TV. I like it very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}